Debes montar una montura para comenzar la carrera: un poney si tienes poca estatura, o un caballo si eres de estatura más alta.","Habla con Carl Ganapié","Corre hacia la décima puerta","Corre por la novena puerta alta sobre el salto precario","Corre hacia la quinta puerta","The Yule Run is a fairly new tradition in the Delving Fields of the Shire. Many challenges have been laid down to present a tricky course for the brave riders of Middle-earth who wish to demonstrate their mettle on horseback.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will be removed from your quest log when the current festival ends. </rgb>","Corre por la segunda puerta alta sobre el salto precario","Has ganado la carrera del festival de los Campos de Cavada","Corre hacia la undécima puerta","Corre por la segunda puerta baja a través del barro pegajoso","Monta un caballo de carrera","Cruza la línea de salida","Corre hacia la sexta puerta","¿Así que vas a probar suerte en la carrera? ¡Eres más valiente que yo! Los caballos y poneys están en el establo, justo allí.'","Corre por la novena puerta baja a través del barro pegajoso","Corre hacia la tercera puerta","Ha empezado la carrera","'Te doy la bienvenida, es un evento bastante extraño, ¿no crees? Correr por ahí sobre estas grandes bestias altas... ¡No estoy seguro de que me guste en absoluto! Pero la gente viene de cerca y de lejos para probar suerte en este juego.\
\
'Las reglas son muy simples: corre a través de cada puerta, y no debes caerte de tu montura antes de que se acabe el tiempo. Cuando veas dos puertas una al lado de la otra, debes elegir qué camino tomar, ya sea alto o bajo. El camino bajo puede estar embarrado, y el alto seguramente estará seco, pero es realmente precario. También habrá otros obstáculos para interrumpirte.\
\
'¿Te sientes preparado para este desafío? ¡Solo los jinetes más animados deberían siquiera intentar tal hazaña! Seguro que será muy peligroso. ¡Yo mismo nunca intentaría algo así!'","Corre hacia la primera puerta","Has perdido la carrera"},
[12014]={"You have discovered that Shathur-munzu is the den of the Wargs of the Vales, and feel you must do what you can to rid the land of this threat.","Completado.","Completado","Duskenvale has become a haven of the foul Wargs of the Vales.\
\
You should defeat wargs in Duskenvale and Shathur-munzu.","Defeat Wargs in Duskenvale","You have done much to cleanse Duskenvale of the warg menace. The people of the Vales are safer for your actions.","The Den of Wargs","Now that you have seen what lies inside Shathur-munzu, you feel it is your responsibility to deal with the warg threat as much as you are able. You should defeat as many wargs as possible in the wilds of Duskenvale and Shathur-munzu.","Defeat wargs in Duskenvale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated wargs in Duskenvale (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12015]={"'¡Asesta el golpe final a estos susi asesinos! Mata a la madre de la guarida y después habla con Santtu.'","La madre de la guarida puede encontrarse en una isla cerca de la orilla occidental del lago.\
\
Urho te ha pedido que localices a la madre de la guarida de la manada de lobos y la derrotes.","Derrota a la madre de la guarida","Habla con Santtu","La madre de la guarida","'Ahora que están huyendo, debemos asestar un último golpe a los susi. Muchos de los miembros de la manada son crías de un solo susi, la madre de la guarida que conduce a la manada por el bosque.\
\
'Si la madre de la guarida muere, los susi se dispersarán y quedarán confundidos... no creo que vuelvan a molestarnos durante muchos inviernos. ¿Harías esto por nosotros?\
\
'La madre de la guarida protege a su manada en una isla al oeste. Cuando la encuentres, mátala y después regresa con mi capitán, Santtu.'","'¿La madre de la guarida ha sido derrotada? Has hecho un buen trabajo, ${PLAYER}. Aunque los Lumi-väki no confían en los Sivullinen, mostramos respeto cuando se gana. Tus actos no pasarán desapercibidos.'","La madre de la guarida ha sido derrotada","Tras hacer retroceder a los lobos hasta los confines del bosque, los Lossoth están convencidos de que estas bestias no causarán más daños si la madre de la guarida es abatida.","Santtu se encuentra en Kauppa-kohta, en la orilla oriental del lago.\
\
Ahora que has derrotado a la madre de la guarida de los lobos, deberías regresar con Santtu para anunciarle tu victoria."},
[12016]={"'The time has come, ${PLAYER}. We must enter the mine and see what lurks within. Come, kízinek. We go.'","The bridge to another section of the Glimmerdeep is out and something looms across the divide","Defeat foes in the Glimmerdeep (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You should continue surveying the Glimmerdeep and defeating foes you find.","Orkish scaffolding has been erected all over the mine","Glimmerdeep is overrun with Orcs.","Continue to survey the Glimmerdeep","Enemigos derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The Glitgróf, or Glimmerdeep, is like no mine I have ever seen! There is some exploring to be done if we are to drive out these Orcs.'","This is a good place for surveying","You should talk to Hórin.","'Ah, ${PLAYER}. I fear there are indeed too many foes here for us to fend off alone.'","You should survey the Glimmerdeep and defeat foes you find there.","Survey another part of the Glimmerdeep","The Depth of the Problem","Defeat more foes in the Glimmerdeep (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Hórin","Survey the Glimmerdeep","Enter the Glimmerdeep","You should enter the Glimmerdeep, which lies on Mount Thrumfall north of Skarháld.","Large gem formations glimmer high above","Defeat even more foes in the Glimmerdeep (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12017]={"Habla con Glorfindel","Glorfindel has asked that you try to question Gultháva, the Maiden of the Gladden, about the fate of Kidzul-kâlah.\
\
You should talk to Gultháva.","Elrond's stance has relaxed considerably after hearing Gultháva's story.\
\
'It appears my suspicions were correct, but her reasoning was sound. She was benevolent enough to give the dwarves time to escape before acting. If she requires assistance clearing this place of evil, she will have it.'","'Gultháva presents a pleasant form, but her answers to Lord Elrond's questions are evasive. Even the patience of the Eldar is not infinite; not while we suspect her of some misdeed. Perhaps she will answer if the inquiry is from someone she trusts. We need to know if she caused the flood, and if she did, if it was due to some dispute with the dwarves, or another petty cause.'","Find Elrond and Glorfindel at Kidzul-kâlah","In the depths of Kidzul-kâlah, something evil has taken root. Elrond has asked you to help him investigate the matter, and hopes to learn how the Maiden of the Gladden is involved.","Elrond and Glorfindel have travelled to Kidzul-kâlah to seek answers from the Maiden of the Gladden.\
\
You should find them somewhere near the entrance to Kidzul-kâlah.","Gandalf has asked you to speak to Elrond. He can be found outside the Beorninghús.","'The darkness has been defeated, and the waters of the Gladden made safe. Thank you for your valour, heroes.'","Complete The Depths of Kidzul-kâlah","Habla con Elrond","Talk to Gultháva","Complete The Depths of Kidzul-kâlah on any difficulty mode.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>You may enter this instance by using the Instance Join panel. </rgb>","'I would ask you to speak with Lord Elrond when you are able, ${PLAYER}. Though we have unraveled one mystery, something still troubles the Master of Rivendell and draws his attention from present matters. With your help he may be able to focus his attention on the here and now.'","Elrond would like to speak with you.\
\
He is standing by outside Kidzul-kâlah.","Gultháva can be found either outside Kidzul-kâlah or inside after defeating the Grasping Maw.\
\
You should talk to Gultháva.","The Maiden of the Gladden waits to hear if you will help her cleanse Kidzul-kâlah.\
\
You should talk to Gultháva.","Glorfindel beckons you to speak with him","Las profundidades de Kidzul-kâlah","Glorfindel would like to speak with you.\
\
He can be found outside Kidzul-kâlah.","You tell the Maiden that you and the Elf-lords will assist her in Kidzul-kâlah.\
\
'Very well, ${PLAYER}. When you are ready, we shall begin. But know this: I must test your strength before I allow you into harm's way.'","Elrond appears lost in thought as you approach. He turns to greet you.\
\
'Gandalf was kind to send you. Indeed, something troubles me still, and my thoughts dwell on the years following the War of the Last Alliance.\
\
'In the early years of the Third Age, Khazad-dûm was still a thriving kingdom. Durin's Bane had not yet awoken. Despite this, I have memories of dwarves seeking refuge fleeing from a mining colony in the mountains at a time when all should have been well. It was known as Kidzul-kâlah. Many dwarves were waylaid on the road by Orcs and goblins as they attempted to reach Durin's halls or other nearby forts. They told us of a great flood, perhaps the same flood that caused the Gladden Fields to become the marsh it is today. Perhaps it is as simple as that, an earthquake and a flood....\
\
'And yet, I cannot help but think the Maiden of the Gladden may be involved. The Gladden is her domain, and the waters would answer her call. I would like to travel to Kidzul-kâlah and question Gultháva myself. I would ask you and Glorfindel to accompany me. We will travel to the Gladdenmere and seek her. Find us there.'","You approach Gultháva and ask if she might answer the questions of Lord Elrond. She seems to ignore you, barely acknowledging your presence, but then turns to you and speaks.\
\
'We meet again, ${PLAYER}. I have need of your aid.'\
\
She seems completely untroubled by the questioning of two very powerful Elf-lords. She turns to gaze at the ruins of what must have been a grand dwarf-fortress before its ruin. She does not hide her melancholy as she reminisces.\
\
'Once, the dwarves dwelled here in great numbers. They busily toiled below, sang songs, feasted, lived their lives. We had an understanding, and though I did not appreciate it then, I enjoyed their company. But now they are gone, at my bidding. It was I who flooded this place.'\
\
She notices your shock and confusion at this admission. You feel Elrond and Glorfindel's stances change, and see their faces harden. It appears Elrond's suspicions were justified.\
\
'Judge me if you wish, for I failed. I did not achieve what sought. On that day, a great darkness stirred beneath the mountains. The ground shook, and new paths opened deep below. I felt the taint of evil seep ever closer. I could not allow it to corrupt the Gladden. I bade the dwarves leave, and called forth the flood-waters. Dark, twisted things lurk in the depths now. They did not drown, as I had hoped. I merely halted their spread. I am not able to defeat them on my own. Perhaps with your help, I may finally be able to set things right.'\
\
You ask what became of the dwarves that used to occupy this place. Indignation briefly flashes across her face.\
\
'I would never have let them drown by my hand. Whatever befell them after they left the shores of the Gladden was beyond my control. My wish was for them to live their lives happily in other halls.'"},
[12018]={"Defeat the Grasping Maw","Defeated the Grasping Maw","'Glorfindel and I are prepared to assist you with the trial of the Maiden and whatever dangers lie beyond. Be wary; she is more powerful than she appears. If, despite her abilities, she is unable to defeat the foul creatures within the flooded mine, that is all the more reason to be on guard.'","The Depths of Kidzul-kâlah -- Solo/Duo","Habla con Elrond","Now that you have passed the Maid's test, it is time to confront the darkness within the mines.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> If Elrond or Glorfindel will not answer the call of the Beacon of Imladris, try using the chat command /pet release twice to dismiss them, and then re-summon them with the Beacon. </rgb>","Passed the Test of the Maiden","Elrond would like to speak with you.\
\
If he is no longer with you, you may call him to your side with the Beacon of Imladris.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> If Elrond or Glorfindel will not answer the call of the Beacon of Imladris, try using the chat command /pet release twice to dismiss them, and then re-summon them with the Beacon. </rgb>","In the depths of Kidzul-kâlah something evil has taken root. The Maiden of the Gladden has asked for your help in removing the corruption.","Elrond and Glorfindel are standing by.\
\
You should talk to Elrond.","The Maid wishes to test your strength before allowing you passage into the mines of Kidzul-kâlah.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> If Elrond or Glorfindel will not answer the call of the Beacon of Imladris, try using the chat command /pet release twice to dismiss them, and then re-summon them with the Beacon. </rgb>","'Our task here is done. Now that the corruption is purged and the water receded, perhaps life can one day return to this place. Thank you for your part in finding the truth of this matter. Without your presence, we might have punished Gultháva for a crime she did not commit!\
\
'With this mystery solved we will take our leave, and return to the Beorninghús. There is still a long road before us, and we should take advantage of Grimbeorn's hospitality while it is available to us.'","Pass the Test of the Maiden"},
[12028]={"Meriun is in the Orc-mines.\
\
You should return and tell Meriun that you have slain the Devourer.","The Devourer","'In the deepest reaches of the mine, there is a terrible worm that has grown to enormous size.\
\
'This creature has on occasion slithered out of its pit and preyed upon unwary slaves, murdering and devouring them before disappearing back into its hole.\
\
'If you could find and defeat this devourer of Men, you will save many from a terrible fate.'","One of the pit-worms has grown to gigantic size and has been known to crawl out of the pits below and prey upon unwary slaves.","Defeat the Devourer","You defeated the Devourer","'It is good to know that this nightmare no longer hunts my people in the depths of the mine. You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}.'","The Devourer dwells somewhere in the Orc-mines.\
\
Meriun asked you to find and defeat the Devourer, an enormous pit-worm that hunts unwary slaves within the mine.","Talk to Meriun in the Orc-mines"},
[12029]={"You tell Faeron that your attempts to heal Rhadrog have all failed.\
\
'This is dire. If our medicines cannot help him, we may need to seek out the goblin.'","'Rhadrog's condition is deteriorating rapidly. How could he have fallen ill so quickly from a simple mushroom? It is possible that goblin knew what he was talking about. Our supplies must be hidden nearby. See if you can find our medicines and heal our friend from Ithilien.'","Attempt to heal Rhadrog with Kingsfoil","Maiden's Helm doesn't seem effective","Kingsfoil doesn't seem effective","Attempt to heal Rhadrog with Maiden's Helm","Rhadrog has fallen ill from his exposure to the local flora of Agarnaith. Try to help him by finding the stolen medical supplies among the goblin's things.","Collect medical supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Rhadrog is becoming increasingly ill in Viznak's hideout.\
\
You should try and heal Rhadrog using the medical supplies.","Attempt to heal Rhadrog with Wanderbeard","Faeron can be found at Viznak's hideout.\
\
You should talk to Faeron.","Rhadrog is becoming increasingly ill in Viznak's Hideout.\
\
You should try and heal Rhadrog using the medical supplies.","Talk to Faeron","The Disease","The stolen medical supplies are hidden in Viznak's hideout.\
\
You should find and collect the medical supplies.","Collected medical supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Wanderbeard doesn't seem effective"},
[12030]={"Return to Barûl in Urmâkh with the cloth and rope you have collected.","'This is wonderful. I can help so many stray dogs with this. Thank you. I appreciate your help, friend.'","'I have a matter with which I could use your help, if you are willing. I do what I can to keep stray dogs off the streets of Urmâkh. I collect them, treat their wounds with stray cloth and fashion leashes from loose rope I find. I am running low on supplies. If you're willing, I could use whatever you find around Urmâkh. My work keeps me busy, so I have little time to collect more.'","Gathered discarded cloth in Urmâkh for stray dogs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gather loose rope in Urmâkh for stray dogs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Dog-catcher","Gathered loose rope in Urmâkh for stray dogs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gather discarded cloth in Urmâkh for stray dogs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to Barûl in Urmâkh with the items you've found","The local dog-catcher, Barûl, has asked for your help in acquiring some supplies with which to catch stray dogs in Urmâkh.","Barûl has asked for your help in collecting discarded cloth to treat wounds and loose rope for leashes for the stray dogs of Urmâkh. You can find discarded cloth and loose rope around Urmâkh."},
[12032]={"Return to Niriga in Urmâkh with what you have learned.","Speak with Sûdakh and Ghemûna in Urmâkh.","Speak with Niriga in Urmâkh to determine the best course of action.","Speak with Niriga when you are ready to go","Return to Niriga in Urmâkh","Speak with Sûdakh in Urmâkh","'Shakhdag is overrun with wild boar! Why would he take such a risk? Why not simply tell me he needed time alone? This is terrible, he could have been gored! You must go to Shakhdag at once. You must find my husband.'","'He's taken him? Barûl's taken my husband? We must find Namâkh. We must find him immediately!'","Speak with Ghemûna in Urmâkh","'Whenever he drinks he doesn't go anywhere without his co-conspirators. A terrible influence, they are. Best to start with them; Sûdakh and Ghemûna are their names.'","Speak with Niriga in Urmâkh","'He wasn't out with us last night, we could have used him. Had to finish off twice the ale with him gone! I didn't see him. Maybe Ghemûna knows more?'","The Dog-catcher, Part 3","'Well he wasn't with me, if that's what you're implying. I know that's what Niriga is implying. She's never been fond of our friendship. But no, he wasn't in my company either.'\
\
Ghemûna pauses. She looks like she is collecting her thoughts. Decision made, she turns to you.\
\
'Look, sometimes Namâkh needs time by himself. He has told me and Sûdakh as much. He goes out to Shakhdag and just thinks. Niriga would never understand. But if Niriga truly is worried about him, Shakhdag to the east is where I'd look for him.'","'Have you seen my husband, Namâkh? He never came home last night. I am worried about him. The jackals are getting hungrier and more ferocious with each passing day.\
\
'I love my husband, but he is a fool with drink sloshing in his head. He doesn't know his top from his bottom with a bit of ale in him.\
\
'Would you help me find him?'","Return to Niriga in Urmâkh and tell her what happened in Shakhdag.","Niriga, a resident of Urmâkh, is worried about her husband, Namâkh, who didn't come home last night."},
[12034]={"Search Urmâkh for Namâkh's personal effects (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Search Urmâkh for Namâkh's personal effects for clues as to Namâkh's location.","Comfort Niriga as best you can.","Speak with Niriga when you are ready to go","Return to Niriga in Urmâkh","'He's gone. I can't believe he's gone. And that... thing. I don't know what it was - it called itself The Hungry Storm? I thought it was just a legend? It was so awful. So awful.\
\
'I can't believe he's gone.\
\
'I can't believe he's gone.'","Niriga is worried her husband has been kidnapped by Barûl, the dog-catcher. Search for clues as to Namâkh's whereabouts.","'We must do everything we can to find Namâkh! I know he would have left me clues. I believe he and Barûl may still be in Urmâkh. We need to search Urmâkh for anything that could have been on my husband - anything he left behind for us.'","'Where did you say they were? That house all the items were around is abandoned... or at least it was. Quickly, we must go there! I believe Namâkh was there. And I am coming with you. I will do anything I can to help my husband.'","Found one of Namâkh's personal effects (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Speak with Niriga when you are ready to go.","'Quickly. My husband may be wounded or bound as we speak. We must go!'","Return to Niriga with the items and report the location you found them.","Comfort Niriga","The Dog-catcher, Part 4"},
[12038]={"Aid Freki","Spakorth can be found within Lûghash in Dor Amarth.\
\
You have aided the Stout-axes of Lûghash in completing many of Zôreth's tasks and have also discovered the whereabouts of their imprisoned lord. You should now speak to Spakorth.","Aid Dréri","Spakorth and his folk can be found within Lûghash.\
\
Spakorth has asked you to aid him and the other Stout-axes of Lûghash in easing the burdens laid upon them by Zôreth.","'It often falls to me to ensure that my folk best serve Mistress Zôreth, and as of late, that has meant tireless work. Even with so many new Stout-axes here after the fall of Barad-dûr, it seems like the work only grows more difficult. Our searches for Sauron's trinkets have not borne fruit, and the Mistress has become impatient. If we do not find something soon, I fear we shall lose her favour. And what would become of my folk then? Nothing good, I think!\
\
'In addition to a few tasks of my own, my brethren here in the barracks and down at the forges below have quite a few tasks to finish.\
\
'Will you aid them while I speak with Gimli?'","'You have done well to aid my folk, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'As Mistress Zôreth promised, King Greytooth lives yet, but we must still wrest him from the dungeons of the Dark Tower.\
\
'And that shall be no simple task....'","Aid Spakorth","Talk to Spakorth in Lûghash","The Stout-axes have longed served the Mistress of Lûghash, Zôreth, but her rule has become only more cruel and oppressive in the absence of the Dark Lord.","The Dominion of Zôreth","Aid Sversting"},
[12039]={"Habla con Gorwen","La habitación de Luilloth se encuentra en Sarch Vorn.\
\
Tras expulsar al Miedo Gris, Gorwen ha oído un ruido que resonaba en los pasillos de Sarch Vorn. Debes volver con Luilloth.","'¿Ha desaparecido realmente el Miedo Gris? ¿Ha sido expulsado de Cardolan para siempre?\
\
'Si las viejas historias son ciertas, el Miedo Gris podría regresar con el paso de los años. Quizás lo único que podamos hacer sea permanecer alerta y rezar para que nunca vuelva, ni bajo la apariencia del príncipe Amondir ni bajo ninguna otra.\
\
'No, debo creer que ha desaparecido, ${PLAYER}. Hemos conseguido esta victoria por Cardolan... por Meneldir...'\
\
Mientras Gorwen habla, un sonido resuena por los pasillos de Sarch Vorn.\
\
'¿Has oído eso? Parece que viene de la cámara donde descubrimos a Luilloth. No sé tú, pero yo no voy a salir de aquí mientras los muertos sigan vagando por estos pasillos.\
\
'¡Vamos a averiguar qué ha hecho ese ruido!'","Acaba con el Miedo Gris en Sarch Vorn, la Tumba Negra","Reúnete con Gorwen fuera de Sarch Vorn","'¡Ay de Luilloth!\
\
'No puedo afirmarlo con certeza, pero creo que ella misma derrumbó estos túneles... casi como para atrapar al Miedo Gris dentro de Sarch Vorn. ¡Y pobre Astoryn! Era tan leal que ni siquiera entonces abandonó a Luilloth.\
\
Por sus heridas, sospecho que murió cuando se derrumbaron los túneles. Al menos eso espero, porque sería un destino preferible a cualquier otro que pudiera haber encontrado en Sarch Vorn. Mejor eso que ser atormentada por el Miedo Gris hasta morir de hambre o sufrir algún otro final triste.\
\
'Pero sus restos no parecen haberse descompuesto como lo harían los de cualquier otra persona, y eso me trae muchos pensamientos desagradables a la mente. O bien Sarch Vorn estaba tan bien sellado cuando se derrumbaron los túneles que ella se conservó, o bien el Miedo Gris se apoderó de sus restos de la misma manera que los del príncipe Amondir.\
\
'Tantos horrores se cernieron sobre su familia que cuesta creerlo. ¡Debemos acabar con el Miedo Gris de una vez por todas!","Con el apoyo de Baya de Oro, tu búsqueda te lleva a Sarch Vorn, el último destino conocido de Luilloth. El camino hasta allí está oculto y protegido por la oscuridad. Sin embargo, hay alguien que conoce los caminos secretos que serpentean por la montaña.","Has vencido al Miedo Gris y has dado descanso a los restos de Luilloth en Sarch Vorn. Ahora debes regresar con Rhiangar.\
\
Rhiangar se encuentra en la posada de Herne.","Habla con Gorwen en la habitación de Luilloth en Sarch Vorn\
<rgb=#ff0000>¡Habla con Gorwen antes de seguir adelante!</rgb>","Entra en Sarch Vorn y busca algún rastro de Luilloth","El Miedo Gris se encuentra en Sarch Vorn.\
\
Debes derrotar al Miedo Gris en Sarch Vorn antes de que su maldad se extienda por Cardolan y las tierras de los Pueblos Libres.","'Se acabó. ¡Que Meneldir y tantos otros encuentren por fin la paz!\
\
'¿Es esa la hija del río de la que hablabas? Incluso en un lugar tan oscuro, siento una ligereza en mi corazón en su presencia.\
\
'Pero, a decir verdad, no deseo permanecer aquí más tiempo del necesario. El Miedo Gris ya no existe, pero eso no borra el daño que nos ha causado a nosotros ni a ninguna de las gentes de Cardolan.\
\
'¿Supongo que Rhiangar querrá saberlo? Te acompañaré hasta Herne, pero me temo que nuestros caminos se separarán cuando lleguemos. Al fin y al cabo, soy un Dúnadan y mi deber es hacia mi pueblo. Últimamente han surgido demasiados problemas en Cardolan y será nuestra tarea solucionarlos.\
\
'No obstante, no puedo agradecerte lo suficiente lo que has hecho por nosotros... y por Meneldir'.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Al avanzar en esta misión, saldrás de Sarch Vorn, la Tumba Negra, y viajarás rápidamente a Herne.</rgb>","Gorwen se encuentra en Sarch Vorn.\
\
Has liberado los restos de Luilloth del control del Miedo Gris. Deberías hablar con Gorwen.","'¿Tienes motivos para creer que el Miedo Gris realmente habita en Sarch Vorn? ¡Es peor de lo que temía!\
\
'No había vuelto a pensar en ese terrible lugar desde que era una niña. Entre los míos se hablaba de él casi como de un mito, una leyenda para endurecer el corazón de los niños por si los muertos volvían a salir de los túmulos de Tyrn Gorthad.\
\
'Sé cómo llegar a Sarch Vorn, ${PLAYER}, pero es un camino peligroso. Está al oeste de aquí, construido en una colina de piedra negra. Si ves un viejo puente de madera que cruza un abismo antes de una cascada, habrás encontrado el camino.\
\
'Si quieres derrotar al Miedo Gris, reúnete conmigo allí.'","Gorwen se encuentra en Sarch Vorn.\
\
Has desterrado al Miedo Gris. Deberías hablar con Gorwen.","Liberados del control del Miedo Gris, los restos de Luilloth vuelven a descansar en paz.","Habla con Baya de Oro en Sarch Vorn","Investiga la habitación de Luilloth en Sarch Vorn","Gorwen se encuentra cerca de la entrada a Sarch Vorn.\
\
Sarch Vorn se encuentra al oeste de la caravana de Gerwyn en Cardolan, y está construido sobre una colina de piedra negra. Deberías hablar con Gorwen.","Gorwen se encuentra ante un gran arco de piedra negra y parece inquieta.","Para tu sorpresa y alivio, Baya de Oro ha venido a Sarch Vorn","La perdición de Sarch Vorn","Para tu horror, has encontrado a Luilloth, ¡pero sus restos han sido profanados por el Miedo Gris!","Gorwen se encuentra en Sarch Vorn.\
\
Tras encontrarte con Baya de Oro en las profundidades de Sarch Vorn, has visto los restos de Luilloth descansando por fin en paz. Deberías hablar con Gorwen.","Acaba con Luilloth en Sarch Vorn, la Tumba Negra","Luilloth se encuentra en Sarch Vorn.\
\
Has descubierto los restos de Luilloth, animados por algún espíritu maligno en las profundidades de Sarch Vorn. Debes liberar a Luilloth del Miedo Gris y devolver sus restos al descanso eterno.","'¡Has vuelto! ¡Me alegro de verte, amigo mío!'\
\
Le cuentas tus hazañas.\
\
'La historia que me cuentas me hiela hasta los huesos. Sabía que la situación era grave, pero nunca imaginé que existiera una criatura así, con tanta historia. No solo has salvado mi patria, sino que también has hecho justicia a Luilloth y a su familia. '¡Que este ciclo profano de dolor llegue a su fin!'","Habla con Gorwen en la habitación del Miedo Gris en Sarch Vorn","Sarch Vorn se encuentra al oeste de la caravana de Gerwyn en Cardolan, y está construido sobre una colina de piedra negra.\
\
Deberías reunirte con Gorwen en la entrada de Sarch Vorn en Cardolan.","Baya de Oro se encuentra en Sarch Vorn.\
\
Tras expulsar al Miedo Gris, descubriste que Baya de Oro también viajó a Sarch Vorn. Deberías hablar con Baya de Oro.","'Qué alegría verte bien.\
\
Has vencido al Miedo Gris, ¿verdad? Si no lo hubieras hecho, no creo que hubiera podido entrar sin obstáculos en este viejo túmulo.\
\
'Es cierto que la sombra que se cernía sobre este lugar se ha disipado, pero aún queda un asunto pendiente.'","'¡Todavía no puedo creer que hayas encontrado tantas pruebas de las últimas horas de Luilloth! ¡Incluso has trabajado con alguien que habló directamente con ella! ¡Es increíble! ¡Todo lo que has logrado en tan poco tiempo es más de lo que yo he podido hacer en mis muchos años de investigación!\
\
'¡Estamos tan cerca! Ahora sabemos dónde fue Luilloth a luchar contra el Miedo Gris. ¡Sospecho que esta criatura no fue derrotada como se pensaba! ¡Puede que incluso estén ahora en Sarch Vorn!\
\
'Dudo en pedirte que vayas, pero... no, has demostrado tu valía una y otra vez. Creo que puedes seguir los pasos de Luilloth y, al hacerlo, tal vez podamos dar descanso a los muertos, como ella hizo en su día. ¡Esta vez para siempre!\
\
'No sé cómo llegar a Sarch Vorn, pero conozco a alguien que podría saberlo. He estado hablando con el montaraz Gorwen. Pregúntale si conoce el camino a ese lugar profano.'","Habla con Rhiangar","¡Has expulsado al Miedo Gris!","'En todos mis años, nunca me he atrevido a acercarme más a Sarch Vorn.\
\
'Pero si es aquí donde habita el Miedo Gris... ¡es aquí donde debemos ir! No hay otra opción, a menos que permitamos que este mal se extienda por todo Cardolan, quizás incluso por todo Eriador.\
\
'Si esto es realmente obra de Angmar, entonces mi venganza es doblemente merecida. Cardolan ya ha sufrido suficientes pérdidas, ¡y no podemos permitir que el Miedo Gris lo arruine una vez más! Si la búsqueda de Luilloth la llevó a estas antiguas tierras, tal vez podamos encontrar alguna señal de su paso por Sarch Vorn o alguna herramienta que nos ayude a vencer al Miedo Gris. ¡Incluso la cosa más insignificante puede resultar de gran ayuda!\
\
'Vamos, ${PLAYER}. Si esperamos más, me temo que mi valor me fallará.'","Rhiangar te ha pedido que sigas los últimos pasos de Luilloth hasta Sarch Vorn. Ella desconoce el camino, pero sospecha que el montaraz Gorwen podría saber cómo llegar al lugar donde se encuentra la tumba.\
\
Deberías hablar con Gorwen en la caravana al sur de Andrath.","Habla con Gorwen en Sarch Vorn","Es probable que los restos de Luilloth o algún otro indicio de sus aventuras de antaño se encuentren en algún lugar de Sarch Vorn.\
\
Deberías buscar algún indicio de Luilloth en Sarch Vorn."},
[12041]={"Defeat enemies at Jal Kepir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated enemy at Jal Kepir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Jal Kepir is located next to Cair Andros.\
\
You should defeat enemies at Jal Kepir.","'I trust my mother to lead us from now on. She is strong-willed like my father and caring like my older brothers. She is all the family I have left, and she contains the best qualities of all the family I have lost.\
\
'Speak with her about what we should do next.'","You, Dúneth, and Tolwin enter Jal Kepir, an enemy encampment across the river from Cair Andros, in order to make a path to the fallen Gondorian stronghold.","Speak with Dúneth","Dúneth can be found outside of Jal Kepir.\
\
You should speak with Dúneth.","'We have come this far and I am not about to give up. Let my mother lead us to victory.'","Travel to Jal Kepir","Speak with Tolwin","'I thought my entire family was lost. I came to these woods to plan my last stand and take revenge for the death and destruction that Korpûrta has caused. He took the life of my sweet Gilgír and two of my sons.\
\
'I must stand strong. Now that we are all here, perhaps we stand a chance to see this revenge through.\
\
'I would recommend that we head to Jal Kepir, a blockade right outside Cair Andros. If we can take the blockade, then we may have a chance to get inside Cair Andros and confront Korpûrta.'","'Good work! I was able to take out the scouts patrolling near the bridge. I think we have a shot at getting into Cair Andros.\
\
'I hope that this isn't too much for Tolwin. He is a brave warrior, but still so young.'","Dúneth's camp is located in Talath Anor's eastern woods.\
\
You should speak with Dúneth at her camp.","Jal Kepir is located next to Cair Andros.\
\
You should travel to Jal Kepir in north-eastern Talath Anor.","Speak with Tolwin.","The Doorstep of Cair Andros"},
[12042]={"Talk to Rethvárd outside Eiricháv","Agal Dûn can be found in central Câr Bronach.\
\
You should travel to Agal Dûn.","Free another hillman","Defeat foes at Agal Dûn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Brathar beckons you closer","'Yes, the Dourhand is Rethvárd, our escaped prisoner. He has told me only what I needed to know. He would rather speak to you, ${PLAYER}.'","The Dourhand Proposition","Free a hillman","'Your friend, Uzvát, has informed me that a representative of the Dourhands has a proposition for us. They wish to work together to topple High Priestess Ásachal and her reign over Tûr Fúar. I do not trust those who openly do the bidding of the Iron Crown. For that, we will not be involved.\
\
'If you wish to listen to this Dourhand and work with them, that is for you and the dwarves to decide. I will think no less of you for what you decide, friend. Understand this: we will have no part in it.'","Freed a hillman!","'There you are, ${PLAYER}. So far, the Dourhands have kept their promise! We were able to take Agal Dûn and now sit at the entrance of the Drearspire. For Gundabad!'","Eiricháv can be found in north west Câr Bronach.\
\
You should talk to Uzvát outside Eiricháv.","Talk to Brathar Crack-helm","Seek out Brathar Crack-helm","Eiricháv can be found in north west Câr Bronach.\
\
You should talk to Rethvárd outside Eiricháv.","'I am glad that you came. Has Rethvárd filled you in? Good!\
\
'I have been infiltrating Ásachal and her followers not for loyalty. Bah! They are nothing but an enemy to the Dourhand! I put my enemy close to see them fall! As we can both see, we have a common foe. I have been trying to get everyone to in Câr Bronach to work together. The hillmen are too timid, and as much as I have tried to sway the stone-giants, they seem to have other plans.\
\
'I know that now is a good time to strike, while the Angmarim do not expect such an alliance to form. I also have heard, with good authority might I add, that atop the spire lies a stone of immense power! We can not let that artifact stay in the hands of the Iron Crown. Now, what do you say?\
\
'Good. I am glad that you are with us! There will still be much work to accomplish after the Drearspire is taken. For that we will need the hillmen on our side. Let us rescue those who have been captured in an effort to show we mean to work together.'","'Greetings. I bring direct word from Lord Brathar. He wishes to speak to you, ${PLAYER}. I will tell you where to find him. I assure you this is not a trap. I surrender myself again in good faith!\
\
'Brathar has a plan. He has been building trust with the Angmarim, in order to crush them. All that is left in the plan is that he requires assistance from you and the Zhélruka!\
\
'Please, just speak with him and Uzvát and I will make sure that the rest of your Gabil'akkâ remain at the ready.'\
\
Uzvát nods with his approval of the plan.","Brathar Crack-helm can be found just south of Agal Dûn in Câr Bronach.\
\
You should seek out Brathar Crack-helm.","The escaped Dourhand, Rethvárd, carries a missive and proposition from his commander, Brathar Crack-helm.","Defeated foes at Agal Dûn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Many under the Iron Crown defend the walls of Agal Dûn","Travel to Agal Dûn","Freed another hillman","Múta can be found at Agal Dûn.\
\
You should talk to Múta at Agal Dûn.","Agal Dûn can be found in central Câr Bronach.\
\
You should defeat foes at Agal Dûn and rescue the two hillmen held as captives.","Now is the time to strike the Drearspire!","Talk to Uzvát outside Eiricháv","Talk to Múta at Agal Dûn"},
[12043]={"Secure the courtyard outside of the Citadel of the Winds.","With Ragrekhûl slain, the City of Umbar can now begin to count their dead and rebuild damaged portions of the city","Defeat Ragrekhûl","As Ragrekhûl's escapes, the storms surrounding the creature light fires all around the arena. A Tempestuous Flame has flickered to life","With the approach secured, you may now enter the courtyard held by the cult of the All-Seeing Eye","Secure the approach to the Citadel of the Winds","Ragrekhûl's rampage across Umbar has endangered the Umbari citizens. Defeat Ragrekhûl in the Courtyard of the Citadel of the Winds before more perish.","Defeat the All-Seeing Eye cultists","Defeat the Tempestuous Flame","During the commotion, members of the cult of the All-Seeing Eye have taken the opportunity to attack the city. With Ragrekhûl circling the Citadel of the Winds, you must now secure the approach to the Citadel of the Winds.","With Ragrekhûl's escape, a Tempestuous Flame has appeared within the arena. Defeat the creature so it does not cause additional damage and loss of life.","As the cultist falls, Ragrekhûl makes his approach. High Cultists emerge and begin to attempt to gain control of the powerful creature","'Welcome to Dahâl Huliz, the grand arena of Umbar Baharbêl! Today on this sacred ground, I will unveil a most fearsome spectacle, Ragrekhûl, the Storm Serpent.\
\
'As you know, Shaidal was sent forth to capture this beast, and to my surprise, he was successful!\
\
'This will be one of my greatest displays and ensure my legacy. I have asked you here to witness the unveiling, and for you to see Shaidal receive his well-deserved reward.\
\
'Now, to the presentation!'","Talk to Rothog the Storm in the Arena","Rothog has summoned you to witness the unveiling of his latest spectacle for the Arena. Speak to him.","Dahâl Huliz has long been home to many spectacular contests, pitting capable gladiators against all forms of opponents. Rothog has summoned you to witness the unveiling of his latest spectacle for the Arena.","The Dragon and the Storm -- Solo/Duo","With the Tempestuous Flame defeated, cries of help are heard throughout the city from Ragrekhûl's wrath. Leave the arena and seek out Ragrekhûl"},
