[12373]={"'¿Escuchaste, ${PLAYER}? ¡Lobelia tiene demasiado miedo para investigar! ¡Eso significa que podemos ir a buscar tesoros! ¡Es maravilloso, simplemente maravilloso!\
\
'Estoy seguro de que muchos de estos curiosos tendrán un tiempo maravilloso explorando y llevándose los tesoros que encuentren. Es terriblemente emocionante, ¿no es así?'","El Agujero Embrujado","Lobelia no está contenta con la bodega y te ha dado permiso para explorarla a tu antojo","'Ese loco Bolsón ha ido demasiado lejos... ¡es una buena cosa que él y ese Frodo se hayan ido para siempre!'","'¡Oh, cielos, qué maravillosas noticias! Aparentemente, mis cucharas encajan como llaves en la cerradura de esa puerta del agujero de hobbit allá abajo. ¡Ese viejo loco planeó que yo tuviera su tesoro después de todo!\
\
'Vamos, iré a abrir la puerta, y tú podrás ayudarme a sacar el tesoro que encuentre. Encontrémonos en el Árbol de la Fiesta. ¡Dame un momento y bajaré!'","Ahora puedes entrar en el Agujero Embrujado (¡a tu propio riesgo!)","¿Contiene la carta de Bilbo una pista para acceder a la bodega cerrada? Lobelia parece pensar que sí...\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando finalice el evento con el que está asociada. </rgb>","Habla con Lobelia dentro del Agujero Embrujado","Lobelia ha bajado al Agujero Embrujado para investigar, cuya puerta se encuentra en el Árbol de la Fiesta, debajo de Bolsón Cerrado.\
\
Deberías unirte a Lobelia en el Agujero Embrujado.","Opal Buenavista está en el Árbol de la Fiesta en Hobbiton.\
\
Deberías hablar con Opal Buenavista para entender lo que acaba de suceder.","'Me reuniré contigo en la bodega de abajo, junto al Árbol de la Fiesta. ¡No puedo esperar para poner mis manos sobre el tesoro!'","'¡Ese Loco Bolsón ha ido demasiado lejos... es una buena cosa que él y ese Frodo se hayan ido para siempre!'","'¡Estoy furiosa! ¡Me han engañado! ¡Este lugar no es más que un agujero lleno de monstruos, fantasmas y bichos! Bilbo me hizo creer que había algo que valiera la pena en esta abominable bodega. ¡Cómo lo odio con todo mi corazón!\
\
'¡No hay nada aquí más que suciedad y corrupción! No quiero nada que ver con este maldito agujero. Hagan lo que quieran con él y manténganse alejados de mí!'","Habla con Opal Buenavista para discutir el destino del Agujero Embrujado"},
[12374]={"Find Daervunn in the Mournshaws","'Seek out Daervunn in the northern reaches of the Mournshaws.'","You have learned that an unknown Ranger of the Grey Company has entered the Mournshaws in search of a hidden path to the south. \
\
The Algraig firmly believe this forest is haunted by powerful and fey spirits. Only the Derudh of Nan Laeglin and a few brave hunters dare enter the place.\
\
Even fewer return....","Find Daervunn the Ranger who has wandered into the northern reaches of the Mournshaws.\
\
It is uncertain whether he still lives, but if so it is possible he has found a path into Dunland that is unwatched by enemy eyes.","'I have heard that a duvodiad wandered into the haunted wood....'","'Several days ago, Daervunn entered the Mournshaws -- a great forest to the west of here.\
\
'He was hoping to find a way through that forest to the south that would be hidden from the prying eyes of our enemies, but I have heard nothing from him since.\
\
'The locals call the forest Galar-gwig, and believe it to be inhabited by powerful spirits that do not care for the company of Men.\
\
'There is one group among the Dunlendings, called the Derudh that dare frequent the forest - and even among their ranks it said that one will occasionally vanish into the forest... never again to be seen beneath mortal sun.\
\
'I'd watch your step there.'","'${PLAYER}! You are the last person I expected to meet here. I have not had much success here. The forest is treacherous and wild, and I do not know its paths. I have made the acquaintance of one hunter who will dare the place -- indeed, he rescued me from a pack of strange hounds just last morning.\
\
'What little I know concerns tales of a gathering of 'lords' in the forest...wild spirits or some such according to the tales, but each story I have heard is different, save they all refer to a great Huntsman who leads them.\
\
'My hope is that they might be a hidden company of Elves, hiding themselves from the people of Nan Laeglin behind veils of myth and folk tales -- that might be a real stroke of fortune if we could find them.'","The Haunted Forest"},
[12377]={"Call forth and defeat the leader of the Haradrim in Thama Aklam","Talk to Steward Malthellim","'I have no patience for these snakes, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I hope all his men saw his resolve falter when you confronted him. If you can defeat their war-masters, I have hope that you will aid us in driving all of the Haradrim and their Corsair brethren from our lands.'","'Chief among the threats facing Ost Anglebed is the war-master of the nearby Haradrim. He leads a substantial force, and it grows by the day...\
\
'Already Lornost has fallen to their warriors, and their riders gloat in the fields - the arrogant lot they are. They think themselves safe because of the half-trolls they command, but even those foul creations that could only be of the Dark Lord's designs cannot protect them now. We have taken enough prisoners, ${PLAYER}... it is time for a show of force.\
\
'Travel to their camp, and confront their war-master. Perhaps then they shall learn that the people of Lebennin are not yet beaten!'","Thama Aklam can be found to the south-east of Ost Anglebed.\
\
Steward Malthellim has asked you to defeat the leader of the Haradrim in Thama Aklam.","Steward Malthellim of Ost Anglebed hopes to cripple the Haradrim forces across the river Serni by shattering their leadership.","The Headless Serpent","Steward Malthellim can be found in the Lord's Hall in Ost Anglebed.\
\
You have defeated the leader of the Haradrim in Thama Aklam, and should now return to Steward Malthellim.","Despite his boasts, Waradi has been defeated"},
[12378]={"Maldor would like you to seek a healer in Linhir on Berion's behalf.","The Healer in Linhir","Maldor has asked you to speak with a healer in Linhir regarding Berion.\
\
Talk to Nanthel in Linhir.","Talk to Nanthel","The healer reads the letter before folding it back up and tucking it into the folds of her dress.\
\
'Too often, so long as the body appears to be intact, we ignore injuries to the mind and heart. I will correspond with Sergeant Maldor and Berion. You have my word as a healer that I will do what I can.'","'I'm not so incompetent a sergeant that I don't know what's been happening with Berion. Nor am I so heartless that I would deprive the lad of his livelihood because he remains haunted by the war.'\
\
He stops to rub the weariness from his eyes. It doesn't work.\
\
'He isn't the only soldier I've known to be troubled in this way.'\
\
Casting his gaze to the south-west, he says, 'I've heard of a healer in Linhir who is interested in cases like Berion's. I would ask that you deliver this letter to her. I want to help Berion, but I don't have the knowledge.'"},
[12379]={"The Healer's Rounds","'You there, idle hands! Are you well and able? Then why, I should like to know, are you standing about? There are soldiers, grievously wounded, in every one of the Houses of Healing and scant few healers to attend to them. Not enough by half!\
\
'Why, has the sun ever shined on a slower wit? Go. Make the rounds. Help attend to those who need attending to!'","Attended to patient (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Houses of Healing can be found in the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.\
\
Go to the High Hall, House of Remedies, or House of Rest and tend to patients.","'What is that? You've gone the rounds and treated some of the wounded? I knew there was a fine head on those shoulders the moment I saw you!\
\
'Now, about this malady that will not be healed.... You are not the first who has spoken of it, nor, I fear, the last. Into deep slumber they fall, colder and colder. What will come of it, I cannot say. Nothing good, that much is clear.'","Minas Tirith's healers are overwhelmed by the number of wounded soldiers in need of care.","Ioreth can be found in the High Hall of the Houses of Healing, on the Sixth Circle of Minas Tirith.\
\
You should let Ioreth know that you have treated many patients, although there were some possessed of a strange ailment you were unable to treat.","This patient does not respond to your care. You cannot tell what even ails him.","Attend to patients (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to Ioreth"},
[12381]={"Defeated strange spiders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Spiders scurry out of the woods!","Blómgard can only survive so many raiding parties of vicious spiders before all that is left of the town is complete ruin.","Blómgard can be found in Laerlad in the Vales of Anduin.\
\
You must defend Laerlad from the spider invaders.","'There is something strange about these spiders, ${PLAYER}, but I cannot put my finger upon what it might be. They are hiding somewhere in Laerlad, I can tell you that, and I can tell you too that we have to help these people! You because you are an adventurer, and me because, well, I owe them that. Let us leave it at that, and speak no more of my faults for now. Oh, it is a worrisome thing to remember!'\
\
Suddenly, you hear shouts from the eastern side of the village.\
\
'They are on the attack again! You must defend the village. Go now, quickly and hastily and with great speed, ${PLAYER}!'","Defeat the strange spiders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The wounded warrior says that strange voices call for his people in the shadows","Defend Laerlad from the spider invaders","Radagast can be found in Blómgard.\
\
You should talk to Radagast.","'You have done Blómgard a good service, for the village is defended and we are safe... for now, at least. You say that you have done this in the name of Radagast? Perhaps we will let you and Radagast stay here until this threat is no more.\
\
'My guards have informed me that one of the injured spiders tried to escape, and he tracked the beast. Before it could disappear into the thick of the woods, it turned into some sort of... well, into some sort of man! We captured the wounded beast and have kept it under guard.'\
\
You explain that this creature could be one of the Ungoledain, a group of skin-changers from Mirkwood who worship spiders and hold them to be sacred.\
\
'If you know of these creatures, it seems to me that you are the one to speak with our captive.'","Blómgard can be found in Laerlad in the Vales of Anduin.\
\
You must defend Laerlad from the approaching invaders!","Habla con Radagast","The last of the spiders flees into the woods","Odahild can be found in Blómgard.\
\
You should talk to Odahild.","The Heart of the Mother","'Lóbruth cares not what some ${RACE} wants. He listens only to Mengris, our Tásakh, and will follow her to death or end of world. Voice in shadows, it tells her where to go. Woodmen are in the way, says Tásakh. Pah! It matters little to Lóbruth. If Mengris says slay you all, then you must die!'","Talk to the wounded Ungoladan warrior","Defend Laerlad from the approaching invaders","'The Ungoledain, yes, that would explain a great deal... a great deal indeed! It seems I owe the Woodmen for not one failing but for two! Firstly, I abandoned Rhosgobel, leaving the Woodmen to face the harsh blades of war on their own. I had my reasons, of course I did, but looking back on it I question if they were worthwhile enough to leave the Woodmen so unprotected.\
\
'And secondly, well, now they face an enemy of my own creation! Yes, ${PLAYER}, you did not mishear me. I am responsible, in part, for the creation of the Ungoledain. I made them, and though it was not on purpose, I should have known better! Looking back, it could have been so easily avoided!'","The wounded Ungoladan warrior can be found in Blómgard.\
\
You should talk to the Ungoladan and learn what you can.","Talk to Odahild"},
[12382]={"Lleva el pañuelo a Adan Rhuvyg","Deberías llevar el pañuelo a Adan.\
\
Adan está en Lintrev.","Encuentra el pañuelo perdido de Adan Rhuvyg","Adan Rhuvyg te ha pedido que encuentres su pañuelo perdido.\
\
El pañuelo fue arrastrado por el viento al noroeste de Lintrev.","El viento se ha llevado el pañuelo favorito de Adan Rhuvyg","El pañuelo es sorprendentemente pesado. ¡Tiene una piedra atada!","'¡Lo encontraste! Oh, qué cosa tan extraña. Alguien ha atado un montón de cuerdas a mi pañuelo y lo ha lastrado con una piedra. Supongo que eso fue suficiente para que el viento no se lo llevara, pero aun así era demasiado pesado para flotar.'\
\
Hace una pausa en sus reflexiones, como si recordara que estás aquí.\
\
'Jo jo. ¿Quién podría haberle hecho esto a mi pañuelo, me pregunto?'\
\
Mira a su alrededor y luego te guiña un ojo de manera conspirativa.","El Pañuelo Pesado","'Como ayudarte resultó tan bien, he decidido dejar que me ayudes una vez más. A cambio de una paga otra vez, por supuesto.\
\
'Esta mañana logré perder mi pañuelo favorito. Eh... el viento se lo llevó y fue a parar a algún lugar al noroeste de Lintrev. Si lo encuentras, ¿me lo traes?'"},
[12383]={"Carrete de cuerda recolectado","Deberías hablar con Adan sobre la vista.\
\
Adan está en lo alto de los acantilados de Lintrev.","El Hobbit Pesado","Este es un buen lugar para <rgb=#FF0000>mirar</rgb> los Valles de los Fuertes","Habla con Adan junto a los acantilados","Encuentra un buen punto de observación","Cuéntale a Adan lo que viste","Adan Rhuvyg ha estado tramando travesuras secretas.","<rgb=#FF0000>Mira</rgb> los Valles de los Fuertes","Deberías llevar los materiales de la cometa a Adan.\
\
Adan se encuentra en Lintrev.","'Impresionante, ¿no? En fin, quizá te preguntes por qué te pedí las alas de ave y por qué hay una piedra atada a mi pañuelo favorito. Verás.....'\
\
Hace una pausa dramática y baja la voz hasta convertirla en un susurro.\
\
'Voy a ser el primer hobbit en volar como un ave. He estado experimentando y estudiando cosas que vuelan. Aves, pañuelos que no están lastrados con piedr...s... ese tipo de cosas. Mis experimentos no han dado del todo los resultados que esperaba, pero tengo un nuevo plan que seguro funcionará.\
\
'Aquí es donde entras tú. Necesito que reúnas algunos materiales para mí. Si lo hago yo mismo, no acabarían las preguntas ni las interrupciones. Necesito la rama más recta que puedas encontrar, cuerda y la lona púrpura que cuelga de una de las casas al pie de los acantilados del sur.\
\
'Vamos a construir una cometa más grande de lo que nadie haya visto jamás, y luego saltaré desde este borde como un águila y planearé sobre los Valles de los Fuertes. Ya lo verás.'","'¡Oh, hola! Veo que lograste reunir todas las cosas que necesitaba para la cometa. Bueno, ejem, tardaste demasiado y me dio hambre y..... supongo que tendré que posponer el vuelo de hoy. Eirlys me horneó una tarta de manzana increíble y sería descortés dejar que se enfríe. Quizá intente volar mañana, ya veremos.\
\
'Quizá desde una colina cercana, en lugar ...e...'\
\
Levanta la vista hacia los acantilados y traga saliva.\
...\
'...tan alto.'","Adan te ha pedido que encuentres materiales con los que fabricar una cometa.\
\
Los materiales de la cometa pueden encontrarse por todo Lintrev.","Adan Rhuvyg te ha pedido que te reúnas con él en lo alto de los acantilados cercanos.\
\
Los acantilados están al norte del pueblo de Lintrev.","Recolecta un carrete de cuerda","Recolecta una rama caída","Recolecta la tela de la cometa","Lleva los materiales de la cometa a Adan","Contemplas la vista gloriosa","'¿Ya has ido al borde de los acantilados cercanos? Si no, tienes que contemplar la vista. Si quieres, me reuniré contigo allí y te mostraré el mejor punto de observación.'","Tela de la cometa recolectada","Adan Rhuvyg ha sugerido que disfrutes de la vista desde los acantilados de Lintrev.","Esta rama se ve agradable y recta","'Ah, llegaste. Ven, ven, Mira hacia allí. ¿No es maravilloso? En días despejados puedes ver hasta Tharbad. Bueno, quizá no, pero ¿no sigue siendo una maravilla? Adelante, ve y echa un vistazo.'"},
[12384]={"Azruthor's tent can be found in Azruthor's Rue in Tarlang's Crown.\
\
Although Azruthor's encampment was left in ruins, the Corsairs of Umbar have taken up in it. You should search for Azruthor's tent.","You notice a small encampment that has clearly been abandoned by the Corsairs of Umbar","Tarlang's Crown can be found by following the road south from Sardol, in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
Bregon has informed you that the Corsairs of Umbar have returned to Tarlang's Crown. You should follow the road into Tarlang's Crown and begin your search for them.","You find nothing of note as Azruthor's tent has been pillaged and left in ruin","Tarlang's Crown can be found by following the road south from Sardol, in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
You have found a small abandoned encampment on the road through Tarlang's Crown. You should examine it.","'W-what do you want?'\
\
Bregon eyes dart around to the other inhabitants of Sardol, and he appears deeply uncomfortable to have caught your attention.\
\
'You're the King's emissary, aren't you? The one called ${PLAYER}? Oh, I've done it now....'\
\
Bregon shakes his head.\
\
'It's like I told Amathon. There's a bunch of Corsairs making trouble in Tarlang's Crown and snooping about at that old camp. Yes, it is true that I was something of a freebooter during the War, but I've learned my lesson. I swear it!\
\
'As for those Corsairs, I don't know what they're up to, but it can't be good. Go on, and see for yourself if you don't believe me!'","Examine the damaged barricade","Follow the road through Tarlang's Crown","You notice a damaged and mouldering barricade left behind from Azruthor's campaign","'What did you find out, ${PLAYER}? Was there any truth to Bregon's claims?'\
\
You tell Amathon that while you did find a company of Corsairs in Tarlang's Crown, it appears they have only returned to pillage what remains of Azruthor's encampment.\
\
'Let us hope that is the case, my friend. I doubted much of note remained after the Heirs of Castamir were routed, but part of me still feared there could be some new conspiracy afoot. It is reassuring to know that my fears were ill-founded.\
\
'Thank you, my friend. I am glad that the King thought to send you on his behalf!'","Tarlang's Crown can be found by following the road south from Sardol, in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
You have found a damaged barricade on the road through Tarlang's Crown. You should examine it.","Amathon can be found in Sardol, in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
You have found no sign that the Corsairs of Umbar seek to do anything but pillage the remains of Azruthor's encampment in Tarlang's Crown. You should return to Amathon.","Tarlang's Crown can be found by following the road south from Sardol, in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
Bregon has informed you that the Corsairs of Umbar have returned to Tarlang's Crown. You should continue to follow the road deeper into Tarlang's Crown.","Although Azruthor, one of the Heirs of Castamir, was defeated at his encampment in Tarlang's Crown, it is believed that the Corsairs of Umbar may seek to avenge his death and advance his yet-unfinished designs against Gondor.","It appears this camp was ransacked and its heraldry torn apart after Azruthor's campaign failed","The Heirs' Legacy","Follow the road deeper into Tarlang's Crown","Examine the abandoned encampment","It seems the Corsairs have abandoned this barricade, perhaps lacking the men to hold it","Talk to Bregon in Sardol","'Ah! I must say, it is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Little has changed since you were last in Sardol, I must admit, but at least the spiders have not troubled us nearly as much of late! However, aside from those who returned from the War, we do have one unexpected guest, and that would be that man over there named Bregon.'\
\
Amathon sighs.\
\
'He seems a rough sort, and by his own admission, he was a freebooter during the War. He says he was run out of Tarlang's Crown by Corsairs, but I thought that the Heir of Castamir, Azruthor, who led them was slain. Why would they linger there eking out the meagre life of a highwayman when they could surely find better fortunes elsewhere? Is Umbar in such a poor state that this seems the wiser choice? I do not know for certain, but from what I have heard, there is something afoot across the Bay of Belfalas.\
\
'Why don't you talk to Bregon and see what you make of his claims?'","Bregon can be found at Sardol in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
Amathon has asked you to speak with Bregon, a seemingly-reformed freebooter from the Blackroot Vale, and learn if he knows what the Corsairs have planned in Tarlang's Crown.","Find Azruthor's tent and search for any evidence of a new plot against Gondor","The abandoned encampment can be found in Tarlang's Crown.\
\
You have found a small encampment abandoned by the Corsairs in Tarlang's Crown. You should examine it.","It seems a company of Corsairs has taken up in what remains of Azruthor's encampment!","Talk to Amathon in Sardol"},
[12385]={"Collected the second half of the broken amulet","'Seek the second fragment of the amulet, ${PLAYER}. I am confident that you are correct...it should shed some light upon the mystery of the Oathbreakers.'","Bring the two halves of the amulet to Lhudd at the Hall of Sanctuary","Lhudd the hermit dwells at the Hall of Sanctuary, west of the main road and south-west of Mincham's camp.\
\
Mincham told you to bring both halves of the amulet to Lhudd the hermit.","'Ah, I see your Ranger friend has sent you.\
\
'I hope that the two pieces of this amulet when mended become the object that I have long sought. My belief is that this amulet may be the key to an ancient rheg -- a curse -- that has held the land and causes Men to wander as shades across the Lich Bluffs. \
\
'Thank you for delivering these to me, as I truly hope it may allow these spirits to be released from their suffering.'","'If you have found the remaining fragment of the amulet, bring it to Lhudd at the Hall of Sanctuary.'","The second half of the broken amulet may be found on shades throughout the Lich Bluffs.\
\
When you locate the other half of the broken amulet, seek out and locate the hermit Lhudd in a small grove of trees to the west of the road called the Hall of Sanctuary.","Mincham is interested in finding the remaining fragments of the amulet you brought him, in hopes that a local hermit might be able to decipher the mystery it represents.","Collect the second half of the broken amulet","The Hermit","'The hermit who inhabits a small grove near here has been searching for relics from older days, and this fragment you brought me appears to resemble some of those things he seeks.\
\
'You should seek out the shades that have been haunting this place. My hope is that you might be able to find the missing half of the amulet among them.\
\
'Please take this fragment and seek the other half. If you can complete the amulet, bring it to the hermit Lhudd at the Hall of Sanctuary, south-west of here. He may be able to unravel this mystery.'"},
[12386]={"'Aye, ${CLASS}. Have you been to Zikrum-dûl?'\
\
You explain to Lukíd that you found Angârmu, but he wishes to stay, and that Zikrum-dûl is still very dangerous.\
\
'Hold on a moment though, what do you mean you found the old cloud-shouter? That was just a myt-uh, I meant that is great that you found him! Are you are sure it was him and not just some trader?'\
\
Lukíd has a look of confusion mixed with surprise on his face, he appears to have not expected you to find the hermit. He regains focus and continues.\
\
'And true shame about Zikrum-dûl, especially for those thieves trying to take advantage of all this chaos.'\
\
Lukíd tries not to appear disappointed at the news.\
\
'Thank you for your help. Galâmka was right about you.'","Speak with the hermit at his camp in Zikrum-dûl.","Speak with the hermit","Seek out the hermit of Zikrum-dûl","Return to Lukíd in Ub Nishir","'You must be the ${CLASS} of which Galâmka spoke. He mentioned you might be around, asking people if they are in need of help. I am Lukíd.'\
\
Lukíd shifts slightly with a wince of pain on his face from his injury.\
\
'I know of a place nearby, and someone who might be in need. Over to the east. In Zikrum-dûl.\
\
'Have you heard of the old cloud-shouter? He is a hermit who is said to live there. Well, I fear for his safety and all, what with the Orcs and other beasts roaming the land... and of course the brigands after the treasures said to be in the ruins.'\
\
Lukíd trails off slightly as he mentions the treasure.\
\
'I thought you might you go and see if you can check the area? Then let me know what you find. I'm hoping to hear information such as if it is dangerous for people or not. I would hate for people to go searching for that treasure if it is not safe.'\
\
Lukíd's eyes grow wide.\
\
'Oh! And of course making sure old cloud-shouter is well!'","'Oh my, a visitor! Who are you? I am Angârmu!'\
\
You explain you were sent to find him and to see how dangerous Zikrum-dûl is.\
\
'I have never known this Lukíd or this Ub Nishir. No. No, I will stay here. In my home.\
\
'This land here though, Zikrum-dûl, is filled will dangers, yes. I have seen Orcs roam the land, and thieves, and beasts. Very dangerous, now that you ask me.'\
\
Angârmu's eyes look to the sky briefly and seem to squint at the sight of the clouds.\
\
'But I stay. I fear not these dangers. I have other, more fearsome dangers for which to watch. Yes much more fearsome. I can not let them find me.\
\
'Thank you for your visit.'","The Hermit of Zikrum-dûl","Return to Lukíd in Ub Nishir to the north of Maurûsh and tell him that you found the hermit and what you saw in Zikrum-dûl.","Lukíd has asked you to investigate Zikrum-dûl and seek out the mythical hermit.","Found Old Cloud-Shouter","Lukíd has asked you to investigate Zikrum-dûl. He claims there is a hermit in the area that may be in need of your help."},
[12387]={"The Hidden Fortress","You have reclaimed Dun Shûma from the Ekhamâti forces.\
\
You should talk to Mizâdi.","'We are victorious. I now hold the Lion-crown of Aragín the Queller, and must make official my claim to the throne of Hamât. This, I fear, is just the beginning of a long campaign.\
\
'That sorcerer has given us a parting gift, a secret he expected us to take to our graves: Ordâkh is manipulating Ekhamât, puppeteering Bârshud to fight their war for them. The new Hul must be eager to regain control of all Shagâna, and will use unwitting vassals to do so. Even if Bârshud’s claim over Hamât is defeated, my people will not be truly safe until the threat of Ordâkh is eliminated for good.\
\
'You have been by my side through all of this, ${PLAYER}. For now, I have little to offer but my sincerest thanks, but once this war is finally won, the Kingdom of Hamât will forever be in your debt.'","Talk to Mizâdi","Use the Instance Finder to complete 'Dun Shûma, the King's Fortress' on any difficulty.","Complete 'Dun Shûma, the King's Fortress' on any difficulty","The hostile forces of Ekhamât have claimed Dun Shûma, the hidden fortress of Shâr Shûma III, seeking the lost crown of Aragín the Queller.","Completed 'Dun Shûma, the King's Fortress'","'Bârshud has fled, but our work is not yet finished. The remainder of the Ekhamâti Umûni and their Ordâkhai forces are holed up inside the hidden fortress before us.\
\
'Dun Shûma, built by an ancient Shâr of Nísaka, is said to hold many of our ancestral treasures. I suspect there is one treasure in particular that Bârshud seeks: the lost crown of Aragín the Queller. Holding such a thing would give his claim to the throne of Hamât legitimacy. We must prevent Ekhamât from seizing it, at all costs.'"},
[12388]={"Debes regresar con Almetha en el mercado del valle","Visita los muros de Alto Sundergrót","Los Hogares Ocultos de los Holbytlan","'¡Te doy la bienvenida de vuelta! Espero que hayas disfrutado tu visita a nuestro hermoso valle. Si encuentras una madriguera que te guste, ¡me alegrará que te sumes a la vecindad!\
\
'Solo pedimos que mantengas en secreto nuestro hogar oculto. Allá afuera abundan los peligros, y hemos vivido en paz durante tanto tiempo.'","Visita una madriguera cómoda","Las antiguas murallas de Sundergrót han protegido durante mucho tiempo los valles de los Holbytlan","Una gran madriguera con bellas vistas del valle residencial a tus pies","Una madriguera cálida aparece escondida en lo alto de un paso traicionero","Los sonidos del mercado y de los artesanos llenan el aire","Los hogares de los Holbytlan se encuentran al suroeste del pueblo de Lyndelby. Almetha Ditchel te ha pedido que explores los valles de su gente y regreses con ella cuando hayas visto los parajes del valle.","Escondidos en los bordes orientales de las Montañas Nubladas, los valles ocultos de los Holbytlan han abierto sus puertas a visitantes y nuevos residentes por igual.","Visita una madriguera cómoda escondida","Un paso estrecho conecta las madrigueras con Lyndelby","Regresa con Almetha en el mercado del valle","Una madriguera cómoda se alza ante ti, esperando convertirse en tu hogar","Visita el mercado del valle","Visita la entrada del valle","Visita una madriguera humilde escondida","Visita una gran madriguera","Una madriguera pequeña pero acogedora se alza ante ti, lista para que te mudes","Una joya escondida y espaciosa, con hermosas vistas de Lyndelby en el valle al norte","'¡Hola! No solemos recibir exploradores por aquí, y menos aún amistosos. Pero pareces de buen corazón. Si has visitado a mis primos en Lyndelby, al norte, no me sorprendería que hayas tenido que esforzarte un poco para ganarte su confianza.\
\
'Aquí amamos la vida sencilla de nuestro valle y damos la bienvenida a los visitantes una vez que los conocemos. Siéntete libre de explorar nuestras tierras. Me encantaría tener la oportunidad de hablar contigo otra vez y quizá algún día considerarte parte de nuestra vecindad.'","Visita una madriguera humilde"},
[12392]={"'There you are, little ${RACE}. Do you see this grate? Perhaps you can enter Isengard through there.'","Speak with Dagoras within Isengard","'Hoom now, meet me by the river, little ${RACE}.'","Quickbeam is at the river's edge, down in the Vale below his home.\
\
Quickbeam has asked you to meet him down by the river's edge, where he believes he has found a way to sneak you into Isengard.","Talk to Quickbeam by the Isen","'You want to find a way into Isengard? Hoom. Well. There is no way one such as I could enter unseen, but you are so small, little ${RACE}, it seems that you could slip in through the cracks in the stone!\
\
'Perhaps I can help you there. I saw a small stream made by the hands of Men coming from within Isengard. It carries the stench of fire and iron, so I suspect that you can find your way inside along it.\
\
'Meet me down by the edge of the river below, and I will show you the way.'","The Hidden Way","You should sneak into Isengard through the tunnel Quickbeam has opened for you.","Quickbeam says that there is little more he can do until his kindred decide upon some course of action... but he believes that he has found a way for you to enter the fortress of Isengard undetected.","'You must not delay overlong, little ${RACE}. Ta-rum, it is dangerous here.'","'Ah, there you are, ${PLAYER} -- I thought Quickbeam would find you a way in here eventually, but keep your head down lest the Orcs discover us.'"},
[12393]={"'Many are the songs that will be sung of this day, my friend. At long last, Hrímil Frost-heart is dead and Mount Gundabad is ours. And I would be remiss to overlook the role you played in our victory, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'With Hrímil's death, our conquest of the Mountain-home is all but certain. Gorgar is slain, and the line of Azog is ended. The Orcs and their wild cousins from the North have fallen into disarray, and it is my firm belief that those who linger within Gundabad will be routed in the days ahead.\
\
'Even so, I grieve the loss of my uncle, Náin, and it is with great sorrow that I shall have to deliver word of his death to my father, King Thorin. My heart aches, too, that he was so soon to follow my grandfather, Dáin, in death.\
\
'May his deeds and his memory never be forgotten! Long live Náin—slakeless, now and evermore!'","Prince Durin can be found at Zidir-nesad, the Steepset.\
\
You have triumphed over Hrímil Frost-heart at the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. You should talk to Durin at Zidir-nesad.","From deep within the darkness of the passage ahead, a voice seems to beckon you...","Talk to Náin at Amgaruslun","The Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra can be found beyond the frozen falls of Amgaruslun in the Clovengap.\
\
According to Prince Durin, the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra can be found beyond Amgaruslun in the Clovegap. You should see if the dwarves of Náin's company have broken through the ice concealing the passage to the ancient Greymaul treasury.","The Hiddenhoard Revealed","'I can hardly explain it, my friend. How could Durin know of such a passage? Could it be true?'\
\
Náin absent-mindedly strokes at the air beneath his shorn beard before lowering his hand.\
\
'You know of what I speak, ${PLAYER}. When Durin told me that he had proclaimed himself to be Durin the Seventh—Durin the Deathless reborn, I must admit I balked at his words. Durin confided in me, and he spoke of visions and of ancient memories that returned to him deep within Mount Gundabad. And so, you must imagine my disbelief when he told me that Hrímil had made a lair for herself in an old Greymaul treasury—the so-called Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. Such a thing should not even exist!\
\
'Yet, with each swing of those pick-axes, I find myself more convinced.'\
\
Náin glances over his shoulder at the dwarves of his company picking away at the ice of Amgaruslun.\
\
'It has been some time, my friend. Why don't you see if we have broken through?","Discover the passage to the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra","Meet up with Náin and his company at Amgaruslun in the Clovengap","It appears that Náin and his company have uncovered an old passage deeper into the Clovengap","Náin can be found at Amgaruslun in the north-western reaches of the Clovengap.\
\
The dwarves' hard work has borne fruit. You have discovered the passage to the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. You should return to Náin.","'Even with the combined might of the Gabil'akkâ behind him, Durin shall have need of you and your strongest allies if victory is to be won!'","Complete 'The Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra'","Prince Durin believes he has discovered where Hrímil Frost-heart has made her lair within Mount Gundabad: the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.","Talk to Durin at Zidir-nesad, the Steepset","<rgb=#00FF00>It is recommended, but not required, that you complete The Legacy of Durin and the Trials of the Dwarves before playing 'The Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra'.</rgb>\
\
'There are those who believe that Hrímil Frost-heart has abandoned Mount Gundabad. I say they are wrong! It is true she has fled, but only deeper into the Mountain-home—to Abnankâra!\
\
'Does that name sound unfamiliar to your ear? It should, my friend. It is known to none who still live, save for me, and that is only because I share the memories of the Durins who came before me!\
\
'Not long after the Greymaul Rebellion was ended and Motsóg came to dwell in solitude in the caverns deep beneath the Mountain-home, he confessed a secret to me—to the Durin I was then. Before that ruinous war between our peoples, he had set the Greymauls upon a great task: to delve a hidden treasury within the depths of Mount Gundabad. It was named Abnankâra, the Hiddenhoard, and it would have been the jewel of Motsóg's kingdom. Had the Greymauls succeeded in their plot to steal the wealth and mithril of Khazad-dûm, it is certain the spoils would have come to rest at Abnankâra.\
\
'Whether it was by some sense of duty or mere curiosity, I—when I was Durin the First—heeded Motsóg's words and found the hidden way to the gates of Abnankâra. I strode within its halls only once, and when I had seen all that I meant to, I sealed it behind me—leaving the few, ill-gotten riches of the Greymauls to be forgotten. And so it has been for many Ages of the world!\
\
'It lies still in the Clovengap, my friend, and in my heart, I am certain that that is where Hrímil Frost-heart has gone. I have sent my uncle, Náin, ahead with a small company to seek for the Hiddenhoard.\
\
'Will you aid him, my friend? Will you see our long struggle for the conquest of Mount Gundabad to its end?'","The Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra can be found in the Clovengap.\
\
Náin has asked you to muster your allies and aid Prince Durin in confronting Hrímil Frost-heart in the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra.\
\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You must complete 'The Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra' on any difficulty Tier to advance this quest.</rgb>","'Go on ahead, my friend, and see if we have broken through!'","'You say you heard a voice on the wind? It can be no other—we have found the lair of Hrímil Frost-heart!\
\
'I shall send word to Durin at once, my friend. If ever I doubted his words, I have now all the proof I sought. Alas that the Black Mattock was lost in the Deepscrave! This will have to do....'\
\
Náin hefts a war-mattock of the Iron Hills in his hand.\
\
'In the meantime, ${PLAYER}, I would ask that you gather your strongest allies to Mount Gundabad. When you are prepared, we shall see what awaits us within Abnankâra!\
\
'Even with the combined might of the Gabil'akkâ behind him, Durin shall have need of you—and of them—if victory is to be won!'","Náin can be found at Amgaruslun in the north-western reaches of the Clovengap.\
\
After arriving at Amgaruslun, you have found Náin's company hard at work excavating what appears to be an old passageway deeper into Mount Gundabad. You should talk to Náin.","'My uncle Náin has gone to seek the old passage to the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra. Travel to the Clovengap and join him, my friend!'","Náin and his company can be found at Amgaruslun in the north-western reaches of the Clovengap.\
\
Believing that an ancient Greymaul treasury known as the Hiddenhoard of Abnankâra had long laid hidden in Mount Gundabad, Prince Durin has asked you to join Náin and his company at Amgaruslun in the Clovengap. You should meet up with Náin and his company at Amgaruslun."},
[12400]={"'¿Glóin te envió para ayudar? Cuando vuelvas a verle, dale las gracias. Hay mucho que hacer aquí.'","Larus y Vighar están en un pequeño campamento en Risco Alto, al este del campamento de Glóin.\
\
Glóin te ha pedido que encuentras a sus amigos Larus y Vighar en el campamento de Risco Alto y les ayudes.","El Risco Alto","'Hay mucho por hacer en las colinas nevadas al norte y al este de aquí. Unos amigos míos, Larus y Vighar, se aventuraron hacia el este y montaron un pequeño campamento en el Risco Alto. Ve a buscarlos y ayúdalos en lo que puedas.'","Glóin ha enviado varios enanos como avanzadilla para establecer un pequeño campamento en el Risco Alto."},
[12402]={"Las patrullas Angmarim transportan con frecuencia órdenes y cajas de caudales a través de Imlad Balchorth.","Recolecta órdenes Angmarim.","Entrega las órdenes y la caja de caudales a Birgir","El Salteador de Caminos","Las patrullas Angmarim pueden encontrarse en los caminos de Imlad Balchorth, al oeste de Myrkworth.\
\
Birgir te ha pedido que embosques a las patrullas Angmarim y recuperes cualquier orden o caja de caudales que puedan estar transportando.","Recolecta la caja de caudales","'Muy bien. Sin nada más, este dinero me permite ofrecerte una recompensa. ¡Quizás aún más importantes sean estas órdenes! Podrían contener información valiosa sobre la disposición de tropas en las Tierras de las Quebradas del Norte.\
\
'Me aseguraré de revisarlas cuidadosamente y de que lleguen a manos de los Montaraces de Esteldín.'","'Por favor, regresa a Imlad Balchorth y continúa hostigando a las patrullas enemigas.'","Caja de caudales recolectada","Órdenes Angmarim recolectadas","'La ruta principal entre Carn Dûm y Ram Dúath, que conduce a las tierras del sur, soporta mucho tráfico de los Angmarim. Mensajeros y patrullas se desplazan por este camino, que serpentea entre los senderos encantados de Imlad Balchorth.\
\
'Quizá por el temor que inspira ese lugar, el tránsito a través de Imlad Balchorth está débilmente custodiado. Te pediría que busques a las patrullas y mensajeros Angmarim y los embosques, trayendo de regreso cualquier orden que porten, junto con cualquier riqueza en forma de cajas de pago que puedan llevar consigo.\
\
'Sé que esto suena a simple bandidaje, pero por un lado, la pérdida de esas órdenes puede retrasar los planes bélicos de los Angmarim y de los orcos que ya se encuentran en las Tierras de las Quebradas del Norte... y por otro lado, sin esos fondos, su comercio con algunos de los mercaderes menos respetables del sur y del este podría verse afectado, y sus propios hombres podrían rehusarse a marchar si no se les paga. En este caso, ser un salteador de caminos puede que no sea algo tan malo.'"},
[12403]={"Los Montañeses de Minas Agor","Los Corcur, descendientes de los montañeses de Rhudaur, han acampado en las ruinas de Minas Agor, en el sur del Bosque de los Trolls.","Corcur derrotados en el sur del Bosque de los Trolls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota Corcur en el sur del Bosque de los Trolls (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los Corcur están acampados en las ruinas de Minas Agor, en el sur del Bosque de los Trolls.\
\
Mientras estés en el sur del Bosque de los Trolls, deberías encargarte de los Corcur que se han asentado allí."},
[12404]={"Los montañeses de Rhudaur","Los Corcur han comenzado a invadir Nan Tornaeth, en el Bosque de los Trolls.\
\
Mientras estés en Nan Tornaeth, deberías expulsar a los Corcur que han venido al Bosque de los Trolls para reclamar sus antiguas tierras.","Corcur derrotados en Nan Tornaeth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los Corcur, descendientes de los montañeses de Rhudaur, han descendido desde Angmar buscando reclamar sus antiguas tierras por orden del Señor Oscuro.","Derrota Corcur en Nan Tornaeth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12405]={"Reach Khûn Sagaz","Locate where weapons are kept in Khûn Sagaz","'I see you wish to help then. Perhaps you are indeed bold instead of foolish.\
\
'You undoubtably have seen these Orcs in these lands, these Utûgi, these Sere Ones, I loathe them. I ask for your aid in driving them from my falls. I regret to say that my song holds no power over them so I can not get rid my waters of them myself.\
\
'They have a dwelling nearby. It has been called many names, but the brigands who resided there before the Orcs gave it the name Khûn Sagaz. You must travel there and learn all that you can.\
\
'Of course, I recommend you also slay any Orc that crosses your path.'","Locate where supplies are kept in Khûn Sagaz","'I see you have returned to my home and I trust you have been to Khûn Sagaz.'\
\
You tell Enârshan that you have found where the Orcs store their supplies and keep their weapons. As well as slain any that you had encountered.\
\
'Good. Then you have not betrayed me, ${CLASS}. I will trust you for the time, but remember, these are my waters. I know how we can deal with this plague upon Ilûritu.\
\
'Return to me when you are prepared to do more.'","Return to Enârshan behind the waterfall in Ilûritu","Enârshan has asked you to investigate Khûn Sagaz nearby and find out more about it.","Investigate Khûn Sagaz near the Falls of Ilûritu for Enârshan the Idâmi.","Defeated Orcs in Khûn Sagaz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Reached Khûn Sagaz","Return to Enârshan in her home behind the waterfall in Ilûritu.","Located the weapons in Khûn Sagaz","Enârshan has asked you to travel to Khûn Sagaz at the top of the hill nearby to investigate.","The Hills Above","Defeat Orcs in Khûn Sagaz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Located the supplies in Khûn Sagaz"},
[12406]={"Los saqueadores de tumbas han huido a las colinas sobre el Camino de los Reyes. Desde allí, alertan a las fuerzas de Angmar, sus nuevos aliados, sobre las acciones de los Montaraces.","Ayuda a Maladan a explorar Arthobel","Nimbellas está en el campamento de los Montaraces a lo largo del Camino de los Reyes.\
\
Las colinas han sido despejadas de amenazas. Deberías regresar de inmediato a Nimbellas.","Las criptas bordean el Camino de los Reyes que conduce a Annúminas.\
\
Antes de que los Montaraces puedan moverse para investigar el estado de las criptas en el Camino de los Reyes, deben asegurar las colinas de los saqueadores de tumbas restantes. Nimbellas te ha pedido que hagas esto.","'Una vez que aseguremos las colinas, podrá comenzar el verdadero trabajo.'","Ayuda a Nethrandir con los espejos de Tham Sarch","Ayuda a Rodlam con los arcos largos de Tham Laegamon","Habla con Nimbellas en el Camino de los Reyes","Ayuda a Rodlam con los ladrones de Tham Laegamon","'Las colinas han sido despejadas, y estamos preparados para aventurarnos en el Camino de los Reyes con más audacia.'","'Me alegra por fin recibir algo de ayuda. Hemos estado intentando hacer todo lo que podemos aquí abajo, pero con cada movimiento que hacemos, nuestros enemigos ya están ahí esperándonos. He descubierto por qué, pero simplemente no hemos tenido gente suficiente para hacer algo al respecto. Poco después de que liberaras Rantost, varios barcos desembarcaron en la orilla aquí. Observé una reunión entre los saqueadores de tumbas recién llegados y las fuerzas de Angmar. Después, los saqueadores se dirigieron a las colinas, y los angmarim reanudaron su búsqueda.\
\
'Solo puedo imaginar que se llegó a un acuerdo. Por un lado, los saqueadores de tumbas espiarían para Angmar e informarían de nuestros movimientos desde arriba. A cambio, a medida que Angmar encontrara reliquias, daría a los saqueadores las que no quisiera.\
\
'Si vamos a avanzar hacia el Camino de los Reyes, el antiguo cementerio de los gobernantes de nuestros antepasados, nuestras acciones deben estar ocultas al Enemigo. Para que eso ocurra, debemos vaciar las colinas y reclamarlas para nosotros.'","Las colinas tienen ojos","Ayuda a Nethrandir con los ladrones de Tham Sarch"},
[12407]={"'¿Has conseguido mis suministros, ${PLAYER}? No puedo continuar hacia el sur sin ellos.'","Ilmo es pastor y requiere algunos suministros que ya ha encargado para cuidar de su rebaño.","Consigue la montura de Rauno","Has conseguido la montura de Rauno","Ilmo te ha pedido que consigas una montura de Rauno, reinas de Matti y una piedra de sal de Kaleva, en Sûri-kylä.","'¿Estás aquí por la piedra de sal entonces?\
\
'¡Dile a Ilmo que los últimos filetes de hirvi que nos entregó eran muy buenos!'","'Soy pastor de profesión, una profesión de hecho respetada entre los Lossoth. Proveemos de carne, pieles y transporte rápido para cruzar los campos nevados para aquellos lo suficientemente valientes para montar en hirvi.\
\
'Llevamos este rebaño a Sûri-kylä para comerciar, pero mi chico ha tenido que volver para un recado importante a Pynti-peldot. No puedo entrar en el pueblo tal y como están. Quizá tú podrías conseguirme algunos objetos que ya he procurado.\
\
'Necesito una montura de Rauno, reinas de Matti y una piedra de sal de Kaleva. Traéme estos objetos de vuelta y estaré en deuda contigo.'","Has conseguido la piedra de sal de Kaleva","Lleva los objetos a Ilmo","Consigue las riendas de Matti","El rebaño de hirvi","'¿Las riendas de Ilmo? Sí, las tengo por aquí. Deja que las busque.","'Te doy las gracias, ${PLAYER}. Sin ti, el rebaño podría haber sido dispersado por los Peikkos que a menudo atacan por la noche.'","'¿Ilmo ha llegado por fin con el rebaño entonces?\
\
'Su nueva montura está en el suelo, aquí a mi lado. Puedes llevársela y asegúarte de darle las gracias por llevar a mi hija a Pynti-peldot.'","Ilmo está en el exterior de Sûri-kylä con su rebaño de alces.\
\
Debes llevarle inmediatamente los objetos que has conseguido.","Consigue la piedra de sal de Kaleva","Has conseguido las riendas de Matti"},
[12408]={"Arcil is at the Mead Hall of Aldburg.\
\
You have explored Aldburg and learned a little about its history. You should now return to Arcil.","'Do you hear that? No? Well, never you mind that. You are here to find out more about this great city, are you not?\
\
'I have been Quartermaster of Aldburg for longer than my memory goes back. I have seen quite a bit in my day and I have...I heard it again! You did not?\
\
'There is not much for me to do these days, but talk with my new friend. Now, there is much to do, and not enough hands to do it. If you speak with Arcil, let him know of my needs.'","Explored the Quartermaster's house","The Quartermaster's house is located in the western portion of Aldburg.\
\
Wilflad suggested that you visit the Quartermaster of Aldburg.","Arcil suggested that you explore the former capital city of Rohan, Aldburg and learn something of its history.\
\
You should seek out Éothain and speak with him first.","Talk to Téothic","'This is the oldest stable in the area, and it is showing its wear. I have been trying to acquire assistance with repairs, but with everyone heading west, help has been hard to come by. Perhaps you could convince Arcil that I need help rebuilding the stable?\
\
'This very stable has housed the steeds of some of Rohan's greatest warriors...Éorl and Folca, among others.\
\
'As you make your way around Aldburg, be sure to stop and speak with the Quartermaster, located in the western part of the city.'","The History of Aldburg","Wilflad is near the stable of Aldburg.\
\
Wilflad may be able to provide more information about the stable.","Explore the Aldburg training hall","'Thane Arcil has yet to decide what to do about the Orcs? It is not surprising. We will decide on a course of action soon, I am sure.\
\
'In the meantime, I agree with him: you should acquaint yourself with Aldburg. On the surface it may not look like the city of a king, but it is, in truth, a city rich with history.\
\
'I recommend beginning in the eastern part of the city at the training hall.'","Explored the Aldburg stable","Talk to Arcil","Explore the Quartermaster's house","'While we decide a course of action in regards to these different Orcs, might I recommend that you explore Aldburg? Despite the damage that has been done, it still is a very lovely place.\
\
'While you are exploring, talk to some of the inhabitants and gain some knowledge about the history of our great home. \
\
'As you might have noticed, we are very vulnerable here in Aldburg. Most of our men have gone west, for good reason. As you speak with others, feel free to assist those who may need it.'","Bertred is at his house in the western part of Aldburg.\
\
Wilflad told you to speak with Bertred, Quartermaster of Aldburg, to learn more of the city's history.","'I had not realized that there was so much that needed to be done around Aldburg. I was too focused on other affairs. I still have yet to decide what to do about the Orcs.\
\
'Allow me to consider this problem further. Since so much in Aldburg requires another set of hands, I am certain you can find work to occupy yourself with.'","Explore the Aldburg stable","Talk to Bertred","Talk to Wilflad","The training hall is in the eastern part of Aldburg.\
\
Éothain recommended starting your exploration of Aldburg at the training hall.","Téothic is at the training hall in Aldburg.\
\
You should speak with Téothic about the Aldburg training hall.","The stable of Aldburg is to the north-west of the training hall.\
\
Téothic recommended that you go see the stable next.","'There is not much stored within the walls of the training hall these days. When our men went west, they took most of the arms with them. What remains inside, however, are weapons that span the history of the Riddermark.\
\
'My sole purpose here is to ensure that our enemies do not gain access to what remains.\
\
'Thank you for speaking with me. I do not entertain many visitors these days. From here, you should see the stable, located to the north-west.'","Upon arriving in Aldburg and speaking with Thane Arcil, he recommends exploring Aldburg to learn more about the former capital of Rohan and to speak with some of its inhabitants in the process.","Talk to Éothain","Explored the Aldburg training hall"},
[12410]={"'¿Funcionó mi plan, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'¿Cómo? ¿Aún no lo has intentado? ¡Pues a ello! Mejor tú que yo.'","¡Has derrotado a la reina de la colmena!","Thórhall cree que las glándulas olorosas que has recogido podrían atraer a la reina de la colmena y hacer que se revele, permitiendo así acabar con ella.","Invoca y derrota a la reina de la colmena grodbog","La guarida de los grodbog se encuentra en el Palacio de Náin, al norte de Lamâb-dûm.\
\
Thórhall te pidió que llevaras las glándulas olorosas hasta la colmena de los grodbog y las aplastaras. El olor resultante debería hacer surgir a la reina de la colmena.","Thórhall se encuentra en el pequeño campamento enano de Lamab-dûm, al sur del Palacio de Náin.\
\
Deberías informar a Thórhall de tu éxito.","'¡Excelente trabajo, ${PLAYER}! Con la reina de la colmena grodbog eliminada, la colmena caerá en el caos y su número también disminuirá... al menos hasta que logren criar una nueva reina.'","Has aplastado una glándula olorosa de grodbog","'¿Qué te parece, ${PLAYER}? ¡He tenido una idea! Si aplastas las glándulas olorosas que has recogido, se liberará un potente olor y los gredbyg surgirán.\
\
'El olor atraerá sin duda a la reina de la colmena fuera de su escondite. Si logras matarla, toda la colmena quedará muy debilitada... al menos hasta que consigan criar una nueva reina. Eso debería mantenerlos apartados durante bastante tiempo, y es lo mejor a lo que podemos aspirar.'","La reina de la colmena","Habla con Thórhall en Lamab-dûm"},
[12411]={"El caballito de madera va a Herne","'Mi corazón está pesado, pensando en el miedo que debe haber sentido el pobre Cai. Sé que mi caballito de madera está bastante deteriorado, pero aún me gustaría regalárselo. He eliminado todo rastro de orco y he cepillado su crin una vez más.\
\
'Sé que es un regalo humilde, dado el peligro en el que estuvo, pero quizás le traiga consuelo, y le haga saber que tiene un amigo entre los Elfos. ¿Se lo llevarás, si vuelves a pasar por Herne?'","Mellanion te ha pedido que lleves su caballito de madera a Cai.\
\
Cai está en la posada, en Herne.","'Oh, hola. ¿Tienes algo para mí del hijo de la Mujer Llorosa?'\
\
Le entregas el caballito de madera y sus ojos se abren como platos.\
\
'¡Bendito sea, este es el mejor regalo de todos! ¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:seguro[m]|segura[f]} de que puedo quedármelo? ¡Oh, qué maravilla! ¡Mira mamá! ¡Soy un jinete de Rohan!'","'¡Has realizado una gran hazaña para Wenna! Tu relato sobre la Elfa es conmovedor, y me alegra que su pena también haya llegado a su fin.'","Lleva el caballito de madera a Cai","'¡Nunca, nunca podré agradecerte lo suficiente por salvar a mi hijo! O por lo que hiciste por esa pobre Elfa. Me alegra en mi corazón que ambas hayamos recuperado a nuestros hijos, pero me alegra aún más que ella no atraiga a más niños.'","Mellanion desea forjar un vínculo de amistad con el joven que su madre atrajo."},
[12413]={"Defeated and burned Zhavár-hai in Dath Nethryn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have defeated and burned many of the Zhavár-hai in Dath Nethryn.","The Hollowed of Dath Nethryn","The Zhavár-hai of Dath Nethryn have grown mightier and possess thicker hides than their untainted, Orkish brethren.","'Although the Silent One has fled into its shallows, he is not the only Orc I have spied.\
\
'${PLAYER}, I fear more of the hollowed Zhavár-hai lurk in the swamp-lands below. They carry with them the children of Ungwetári... or Shelob as the Orcs now seem to call her.\
\
'Even if the Zhavár-hai are slain, the terrible things dwelling within them may not be. Thus, I ask that you burn the bodies of any Zhavár-hai you encounter in Dath Nethryn.\
\
'It is an unfortunate task, but it is the only way to put an end to the danger they pose to us and King Elessar's armies!'","Completado","Defeat and burn Zhavár-hai in Dath Nethryn (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","It seems the longer the Zhavár-hai bond with Shelob's children, the more potent their might and the thicker their flesh.\
\
You have done well to defeat and burn many of the Zhavár-hai in Dath Nethryn. They can no longer pose a threat to any who venture into Lhingris, and can no longer hinder Legolas's quest to find the spider-queen, Ungwetári -- now known as Shelob.","Zhavár-hai can be found in the shallows of Dath Nethryn in southern Lhingris.\
\
Legolas has spotted numerous Zhavár-hai roaming the foetid swamp of Dath Nethryn in Lhingris. Even if the Orcs are slain, the insects and spiders within them pose a great threat, so he has advised you to burn them after defeating them."},
[12417]={"¿Hay un ganso graznando dentro de El Toro Bramador?","Jarras rotas limpiadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recupera los repollos robados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El ganso simplón debe estar todavía en el pueblo de Quiebra Larga.\
\
Busca en Quiebra Larga y descubre hacia dónde se ha dirigido.","El ganso anda suelto y fue visto por última vez en el pueblo de Quiebra Larga.\
\
Busca al ganso.","¿Será verdad? ¿Me estás diciendo que son TRES gansos?","'¡Hacía días que no veía tanto revuelo por aquí, y te has perdido el espectáculo! Ese ganso entró como una exhalación, tiró todas las botellas que se encontró en su camino y salió pitando... ¡justo cuando llegaas!\
\
'Te agradezco mucho que me hayas ayudado a limpiar el desastre con las botellas. ¡Buena suerte atrapando a ese ganso simplón!'","'Gracias por ayudarme a levantarme. ¿Has visto a ese ganso? Estaba yo a lo mío, llevando a casa verdura fresca del mercado, cuando de buenas a primeras aparece este ganso espantoso, me derriba y me birla todos mis preciados repollos!\
\
'¡Tienes que recuperar mis repollos!'","¡Un hobbit parece confundido y enfadado por algo posiblemente relacionado con el ganso!","'Oh, gracias por recuperar mis repollos, ¡ya que rescatándolos también me has salvado a mí! ¿Cómo, te preguntas? Bueno, el estofado de repollo es la comida favorita de mi esposa y le prometí que se lo prepararía... ¡hoy por nuestro aniversario de bodas!\
\
'No creo que se hubiera creído que me robó un ganso, cuanto menos tres gansos. Estoy en deuda contigo.'","El hobbit desprevenido se encuentra en el pueblo de Quiebra Larga.\
\
Ayuda al hobbit desprevenido.","Busca al ganso suelto en El Toro Bramador","El Toro Bramador se encuentra en el pueblo de Quiebra Larga.\
\
Recoge el desastre provocado por el ganso en El Toro Bramador.","Sal de El Toro Bramador y continúa buscando al ganso","Con la cantidad de animales que Prunella Valeoro cuida voluntariamente, ¡ha perdido de vista a un ganso particularmente pendenciero!","Limpia las jarras rotas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Registra Quiebra Larga en busca del ganso suelto","Ayuda al hobbit desprevenido","Redahild Bienbueno se encuentra en El Toro Bramador en el pueblo de Quiebra Larga.\
\
Habla con Redahild Bienbueno en El Toro Bramador.","El ganso simplón debe estar todavía en el pueblo de Quiebra Larga.\
\
Sal de El Toro Bramador y continúa buscando al ganso.","Prunella Valeoro se encuentra en el pueblo de Quiebra Larga.\
\
Habla con Prunella Valeoro.","Repollos robados recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","¡El ganso te ha visto venir y ha escapado de nuevo!","El espantoso ganso se ha dirigido al límite del pueblo de Quiebra Larga.\
\
Busca al ganso en los límites de Quiebra Larga.","El ganso anda suelto y fue visto por última vez cerca de El Toro Bramador en el pueblo de Quiebra Larga.\
\
Busca en El Toro Bramador al ganso.","¡El ganso se ha escapado y ha dejado un montón de botellas derramadas que hay que limpiar!","Registra Quiebra Larga y averigua adónde ha ido el ganso","'¿Dices que había tres gansos sueltos molestando a mis vecinos, y no solo uno?'\
\
Prunella se frota la barbilla.\
\
'Eso explica porqué mi ganso era tan escurridizo. Siempre fue capaz de causar una cantidad de entuertos impresionante. ¡El triple de lo habitual, por lo visto!\
\
'¿Quién podría decir adónde se han marchado ahora? Quizá volvamos a verlos algún día. ¡Gracias por toda tu ayuda! Croe que ahora debería averiguar si el granjero que me confío ese ganso sabía toda la historia de semejante criatura...'","Los repollos robados de los hobbits desprevenidos se encuentran en el extremo del pueblo de Quiebra Larga.\
\
Recupera los repollos robados.","El hobbit desprevenido se encuentra en el pueblo de Quiebra Larga.\
\
Devuélvele los repollos robados.","Devuelve los repollos robados","Busca al ganso en el límite del pueblo de Quiebra Larga","El espantoso ganso se ha dirigido al límite del pueblo de Quiebra Larga.\
\\Registra Quiebra Larga y encuentra al ganso.","Registra Quiebra Larga en busca del espantoso ganso","Habla con Redahild Bienbueno en El Toro Bramador","'Echamos de menos a un ganso particularmente problemático, al que suelo tener que vigilar muy de cerca. No hace falta decir que no me han sobrado ojos últimamente, ¡como puedes comprobar!\
\
'Me temo que el ganso anda suelto y está haciendo de las suyas en algún lugar del pueblo. Esto... bueno, ¡no es la primera vez que ocurre! Ten cuidado, ${PLAYER}, ¡este ganso se las sabe todas!'","El ganso espantoso","Habla con Prunella Valeoro","¡El ganso se ha escapado otra vez!"},
[12419]={"'Twice I've found my horse wandering these hills, but she has always run off again before I could lead her to the stables here.'","Find the runaway horse","You found the runaway steed in the Beacon Hills. Now you should lead her back to the stables in Ost Rimmon.","Talk to Sithgar","Lead the horse to Ost Rimmon","The Horseless Rider","'Why, you have done it! But how? That a foreigner can handle Witherbreca better than a Man of Rohan... but never mind that. I have hope once more of rejoining my Éored, and that is enough.'","'Fortune scowls on my every venture, ${CLASS}! I was given a horse half-broken in, and now she has run off on me. Twice I have found her again, only to have her bolt off before I could lead her to the stables!\
\
'Like as not, she has returned to the hills west of the ford, in view of the Entwash. But what use is going after her again?\
\
'My Éored has gone on without me and at a brisk pace at that. What hope have I of catching them? None! No hope at all.'","Sithgar has lost his steed and won't be able to re-join his Éored until he finds it.","Sithgar stands by the Ost Rimmon stables, in the Beacon Hills.\
\
Now that you have led his horse back to the stables, you should talk to Sithgar.","With patience and a gentle hand, you guide the horse back to the Ost Rimmon stables","Search the Beacon Hills for Sithgar's runaway steed.","You have found Sithgar's steed far from Ost Rimmon"},
[12420]={"This collar was taken from a slain hound in the Heathfells. Crafted of heavy leather, studded with crude iron, it is clearly of Dunlending-make.\
\
The Dunlending Hound-masters leash their beasts upon such collars, and if these dogs wear them, then their master cannot be far away. Perhaps you can defeat him and scatter his hounds.","The Dunlending Hound-master has set camp somewhere in the Heathfells.\
\
You should find the Dunlending Hound-master and defeat him and his hounds.","You have defeated the Hound-master","You found a heavy, studded collar upon a slain Dunlending war-hound. If the beasts still wear collars as they roam these hills, then their master must be somewhere nearby.","Defeat the Hound-master","Captain Cadfrith is at the encampment in north-west Heathfells.\
\
You should inform Captain Cadfrith of the Dunlending Hound-master's defeat.","Talk to Cadfrith","'So, one of the Dunlending barbarians crept behind our lines to guide the hounds against us?\
\
'Well done discovering his hiding place and dealing with him. That should scatter his packs for good.'","The Hound-master"},
[12421]={"'Those beasts have been hounding us for days now. I am glad you were able to drive some of them off.\
\
'Now we need to get word through to the Ford about the Dunlendings' increasing presence in the Isendale.'","Talk to Captain Cadfrith at the Rohirrim encampment","Captain Cadfrith is at the Rohirrim encampment in the north-west Heathfells.\
\
You should return to Captain Cadfrith with your report.","Defeated vicious war-hounds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat vicious war-hounds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated cunning hunting-hounds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Dunlendings have released packs of war-hounds into the wild to harry Rohirrim scouts.\
\
You must drive these beasts off lest they harry the Rohirrim attempts to track the Dunlending's movements in the Heathfells, and waylay messengers.","War-hounds can be found throughout the Heathfells.\
\
Captain Cadfrith has asked you to defeat packs of Dunlending war-hounds that have been released into the Heathfells.","'Do you hear that howling, ${PLAYER}? Those are the Dunlendings' war-hounds. They have released entire packs of them into the wild parts of the Heathfells to harry our scouts and messengers.\
\
'Those beasts are nearly a match for a Warg. We have to drive them off, or we will lose precious time in getting word to the Ford and back should the Dunlending army begin to move.'","Defeat cunning hunting-hounds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Hounds"},
[12422]={"'Did you hear that, ${PLAYER}? That howling sound has been spooking the horses and making the men uneasy.\
\
'We have not yet located the wretched beast, but I know I would like to see the noise ended. The more sleep we get before the march, the better.\
\
'Let me know if you find it while you're out in the Noman-lands. It sounded as if it was coming from the hills west of here.'","The calmed hound heads for the Camp of the Host","Complete quest 'Hidden Dangers' with Faroth","Good-bye, Faroth!","Faroth deserves some praise from all his hard work! Why don't you give him a pat?\
\
If you should get separated from your hound, blow the hound-calling whistle to summon him back.","<rgb=#FF00FF>Pat</rgb> Faroth because he's a good dog","Talk to Mablung","He thought it sounded like it was coming from the hills to the west of the Camp of the Host, in the Noman-lands.\
\
Mablung has asked you to find the source of the howling sound.","Mablung can be found in the Camp of the Host, on the northern edge of North Ithilien.\
\
The hound has returned to the Camp of the Host. You should return to Mablung and tell him of your success.","Find the source of the howling sound","The source of the howling sound was actually an injured hound.\
\
You should find a way to calm the injured hound.","Mablung can be found in the Camp of the Host, on the northern edge of North Ithilien.\
\
Now that Faroth's work in the Noman-lands is finished, you should return to Mablung.","Complete quest 'Sniff Them Out' with Faroth","'So this was the source of the howling. Ah, Faroth, old boy! When you went missing, we thought you were gone for good.'\
\
Mablung looks closely at the hound. \
\
'He must have run afoul of those Orkish traps. It must have been a lucky scrape, for he is well on better already. I think he will be on the look-out for those from now on!\
\
'In truth, I have work for this little Ranger. He has taken a liking to you, it seems. Perhaps you would go with him on his rounds in the Noman-lands, ${PLAYER}?'","Completed quest 'Stalker of the Scrublands' with Faroth","You have found the source of the howling sound! It's not a fearsome beast at all, but a scared and possibly injured hound. Does he belong to the Rangers?\
\
You should try to calm it down and then return to Mablung.","Talk with Faroth to part ways for now.\
\
If you should get separated from your hound, blow the hound-calling whistle to summon him back.","'Very good! You two have completed all the work I have for you this day. Faroth has proved himself quite capable, hasn't he? He deserves some praise!'","Mablung, Captain of the Rangers of Ithilien, would like you to find the source of the howling sound that has been bothering the men in the Camp of the Host.","Return to Mablung","Completed quest 'Sniff Them Out' with Faroth","Faroth wags his tail enthusiastically!","Complete quest 'Stalker of the Scrublands' with Faroth","Say good-bye to Faroth","<rgb=#FF00FF>Calm</rgb> the frightened hound","Mablung would like you to work with Faroth to complete quests in the Noman-lands.\
\
If you should get separated from your hound, blow the hound-calling whistle to summon him back.","Faroth looks up at you happily. It seems he enjoys life as a Ranger hound!","Completed quest 'Hidden Dangers' with Faroth","The Howling"},
[12424]={"Habla con Náin","Náin can be found at the entrance to the Howling Pit in Járnfast.\
\
You should talk to Náin.","Náin can be found in Járnfast.\
\
You should talk to Náin.","'Now is the time to finish what Grár began when he gave his life for us! If you find any sign of Grár, bring it to me.'","'You have done a great service to all in the Iron Hills. Songs will be sung of this day and Grár may finally be laid to rest.'","El Foso Aullante","Deep under Járnfast, chief fortress of the Iron Hills, is a place where the red stone once cracked, revealing a horrible abyss beneath the Dwarf-halls.","'As I peer into the abyss my mind begins to cloud. There is both shadow and madness down there. I fear our only option is to enter the pit and hope to bide us some time until the seal can be repaired. If you are not able, I understand, and will send some of my best warriors instead. What choice do I have? If nothing is done, doom is certain.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>WARNING: This is an extreme challenge instance suited for a 3-Man Small Fellowship. Proceed at your own risk!</rgb>"},
[12425]={"The Howling Regiment","'Your hunt has gone well, and the Wargs of Gathbúrz have suffered badly this day. That is one less threat to worry about when it comes time for us to withdraw back beneath the boughs of Lothlórien.'","The Wargs of the Enemy will present the greatest threat to the Malledhrim when it comes time for the Golden Host to withdraw from Mirkwood, for they would be able to overtake the Elves swiftly.","Defeat Wargs in Gathbúrz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Curses upon the Wargs of Dol Guldur...if you will hunt them, I will be most appreciative.'","'We know we do not have the power to pull down Dol Guldur now, ${PLAYER}, and with an enemy army approaching, it is only a matter of time before we must retreat. My people are swifter than any enemy bound by foot, but we cannot run faster than Wargs.\
\
'There is a force of these beasts housed in Gathbúrz, and if they are free to pursue us when we begin our retreat, they will pull down many a valiant Elf, ere we can reach the boats.\
\
'Those Wargs must be slain ere the time for our withdrawal comes, and I believe that you have the strength to accomplish this task.'","Defeated Wargs in Gathbúrz (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Rodelleth at Thangúlhad","Wargs can be found in Gathbúrz.\
\
Rodelleth has asked you to defeat several of the Wargs prowling through Gathbúrz to help ensure a safe retreat for the Malledhrim.","Rodelleth is at Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz.\
\
You should return to Rodelleth and let her know that many Wargs fell beneath your assaults."},
[12426]={"The Hunger of Shelob","'Indeed, Shelob must desire something within the Tower of Cirith Ungol!\
\
'The mind of a spider so ancient is unknown to me, but perhaps she seeks to expand her lair and heal her wounds within the walls of the fortress.\
\
'I can hear the cries of her children within the walls, and they have only grown stronger. Captain Róglarg's garrison is failing without his leadership, and it is likely Cirith Ungol will soon fall.\
\
'It pains me greatly to agree with one of the Gúrzyul, but Ugrukhôr was wise to reinforce the garrison. Shelob wields power few have ever known, and if she ventures from the Ephel Dúath, it could spell doom for not only Mordor, but also the lands of our peoples as well!\
\
'Cirith Ungol must not fall to Shelob! You spoke of an emissary to one of the Gúrzyul, my friend. I shall seek him in the tower and attempt to convince him that the will of his master is imperiled! If they do not reinforce the tower with an even greater garrison, all will be lost!\
\
'While I search for him, I would appreciate your skill in hindering Shelob's siege of the tower.'","Legolas has grown concerned that if Cirith Ungol falls, Shelob shall soon venture forth into Mordor and lands beyond to sate her hunger.","Legolas can be found in the turret of the Tower of Cirith Ungol.\
\
You have aided Legolas in hindering Shelob's siege of Cirith Ungol and should now meet him in the turret of the tower as he asked.","'I believe I have found the emissary to the Gúrzyul you spoke of, but we must deal with him before the tower is overrun!'","Aided Legolas in hindering Shelob's siege of Cirith Ungol (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Legolas can be found beside the road to Cirith Ungol.\
\
Legolas has asked for your aid in hindering Shelob's siege of Cirith Ungol. You should speak to him and learn what must be done.","Find Legolas in the turret of the Tower of Cirith Ungol","Aid Legolas in hindering Shelob's siege of Cirith Ungol (${CURRENT}/${MAX})"},
[12427]={"El montaraz Culang ha sabido de un gran tesoro enterrado hace mucho tiempo por un terrateniente Dúnadan y quiere recuperarlo antes de que sea encontrado por los saqueadores de tumbas.","La inscripción en este hito de piedra es apenas legible, pero se pueden distinguir las siguientes palabras:\
\
   \\qPara zanjar disputas, en el círculo de piedra se ha de luchar.\
Fuera del muro, mi hito se esconde en algún lugar.\\q\
\
Este nuevo acertijo podría revelar la verdadera localización del tesoro.","El tesoro podría estar bajo otro hito de piedra en algún lugar de Evendim, según el acertijo:\
\
  \\qPara zanjar disputas, en el círculo de piedra se ha de luchar.\
Fuera del muro, mi hito se esconde en algún lugar.\\q\
\
Debes examinar el hito cuando lo encuentres en busca de alguna pista sobre la localización del tesoro.","'¿Otro acertijo? ¿Cómo dice?\
\
   \\qPara zanjar disputas, en el círculo de piedra se ha de luchar.\
Fuera del muro, mi hito se esconde en algún lugar.\\q\
\
'No lo sé a ciencia cierta, pero estas palabras podrían estar hablando de la arena de Ost Forod, al noreste de Tinnudir, en las colinas de Tyrn Fornech.'","Encuentra la solución al acertijo","El hito de piedra está rodeado de signos de excavación. Si una vez marcaba la localización del tesoro, seguro que ha sido encontrado.\
\
El hito lleva una inscripción, desgastada por el paso del tiempo.","La caza del tesoro continúa","La inscripción en este hito de piedra es apenas legible, pero se pueden distinguir las siguientes palabras:\
\
  \\qPara zanjar disputas, en el círculo de piedra se ha de luchar.\
Fuera del muro, mi hito se esconde en algún lugar.\\q\
\
Este nuevo acertijo podría revelar la verdadera localización del tesoro."},
[12428]={"Lieutenants of Gazathrug can be found in the southern part of Máttugard.\
\
You should defeat Gazathrug's Lieutenants and retrieve their orders.","Read the second lieutenant's orders","Read the first lieutenant's orders","Retrieve the third lieutenant's orders","Retrieve the second lieutenant's orders","Gazathrug's outpost can be found in the southern part of Máttugard.\
\
You should talk to Hetbrúda at Gazathrug's outpost.","Defeated the lieutenant and retrieved the Orc's orders","Talk to Hetbrúda at Gazathrug's outpost","Hetbrúda searches for Gazathrug, the captain of the upper reaches of Máttugard.","The Orc outpost has been abandoned","Search Gazathrug's outpost for signs of the Orc Captain","Gazathrug's outpost can be found in the southern part of Máttugard.\
\
You should search Gazathrug's outpost for signs of the Orc Captain.","Read the orders","Retrieve the first lieutenant's orders","Read the third lieutenant's orders","'I have been looking over the Orc-orders we collected again. I cannot believe I missed this before! Look, it is crude and difficult to read, but each order is signed by someone named Gazathrug. Most likely this Gazathrug is an Orc and probably commands the Orcs here in Máttugard!\
\
'We did not see Gazathrug at Tholmuzog, but he must have lieutenants nearby. We should seek out Gazathrug's Lieutenants and find out where hides their commander. Perhaps we can capture Gazathrug and learn what plans or schemes the Orcs of Deepscrave have made for us!'","You should read Gazathrug's orders to his lieutenants.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Note: The orders can be found in your inventory.</rgb>","'This is certainly Gazathrug's outpost... but no one is here! There are dead Orcs scattered about as well! Did another dwarf get here before us?'","The Hunt For Gazathrug"},
[12429]={"¡La Búsqueda del Tesoro Enterrado!","Los Enanos de Ered Luin han descubierto un campo lleno de tesoros enterrados, y la gente acude en masa para poner a prueba su suerte desenterrando hallazgos raros.","¡Completa la misión para recibir un mapa del Campo del Tesoro!","¡Únete a los enanos en su búsqueda del tesoro!","¡Completa para recibir un mapa de los Campos del Tesoro!"},
[12430]={"Habla con Miluimil en las Hondonadas Enmarañadas","'¡Gollum se nos ha escapado una vez más! Tengo buenas razones para creer que ha huido al norte, hacia las Hondonadas Enmarañadas, un laberinto de barrancos y hondonadas infestadas de arañas y otras criaturas malvadas.\
\
'He enviado instrucciones a mis exploradores allí para que estén atentos, pero no he recibido noticias de ellos desde entonces y temo que algo vaya mal.\
\
'¿Estarías dispuesto a adentrarte en las Hondonadas Enmarañadas y ayudar a mis exploradores a capturar a Gollum? Es más escurridizo que cualquier criatura que haya encontrado, y puede que necesiten tu ayuda. Habla con Miluimil.'","'Conozco a Fuirgam desde hace mucho tiempo, ${PLAYER}, y rara vez lo he visto tan alterado por algo. Desde que esa criatura, Gollum, escapó a las Hondonadas Enmarañadas, parece completamente preocupado por el asunto.\
\
Sea lo que sea lo que Gollum sabe, debe de ser de gran importancia. Debemos capturarlo rápidamente.'","La caza de Gollum","Miluimil se encuentra en el campamento de Ivorel en las Hondonadas Enmarañadas, al norte de Ost Galadh.\
\
Fuirgam te ha pedido que informes al explorador Miluimil de que Gollum podría haber llegado al norte, a las Hondonadas Enmarañadas, y que ofrezcas toda la ayuda que puedas para encontrarlo y capturarlo.","Fuirgam cree que Gollum ha huido a los retorcidos senderos de las Hondonadas Enmarañadas para evitar su captura y desea que ayudes a sus exploradores a rastrear a la escurridiza criatura antes de que escape o caiga en manos del Enemigo en Dol Guldur.","'¿Fuirgam cree que Gollum está ahora aquí, en las Hondonadas Enmarañadas? Me sentiría más seguro sobre nuestras posibilidades de encontrarlo si la mayoría de mis exploradores no hubieran desaparecido ya.\
\
Estos barrancos son traicioneros para cualquiera que se atreva a adentrarse en ellos, y me temo que ya será una suerte salir de ellos indemnes, mucho más capturar a alguien como Gollum en su interior.\
\
No obstante, la orden de Fuirgam es clara, y no la habría dado si la necesidad no fuera acuciante. Veamos qué podemos encontrar de esta criatura escurridiza, ¿de acuerdo?'","'Asegúrate de encontrar a Gollum y de que no caiga en las garras del Enemigo. ¡Todo lo que hemos ganado aquí —y todo lo que hemos perdido— no habrá servido de nada si lo capturan! Encuentra a Miluimil, encuentra a Gollum y hazlo tan rápido como puedas.'"},
[12432]={"A vicious growl fills the air...","Rúkbag has asked you to find Lumbag.\
\
She last saw him at Dor Pherkha, south-east of Kafagur.","Hedâkha has been defeated.\
\
You should check on Lumbag at Dor Pherkha.","As you approach, Lumbag narrows his eyes","'During our last hunt at Dor Pherkha, the sabre-tooth Hedâkha overwhelmed us. So many fell. I ran back here, but one of the newcomers -- Lumbag, I think his name is -- stayed behind. I told him that trying to prove himself was stupid, but maybe that was low of me.\
\
'Could you venture south-east and make sure he's still alive? I don't doubt his skills, but trying to act like a hero isn't going to land him in a good place.'","Find Lumbag at Dor Pherkha","You have found Lumbag hiding at Dor Pherkha.\
\
You should talk to him.","Lumbag lets out a shaky breath -- almost like he's been holding it this entire time, waiting for you to return.\
\
'It's gone... heh. Rúkbag was right; I couldn't fight Hedâkha alone after all. After I saw it tear through everyone...' He gulps.\
\
'Thanks for the help. I'll return to Kafagur to rest.'","The Hunt for Hedâkha","The sabre-tooth known as Hedâkha has been a thorn in Kafagur's side for too long.","'Shhh! There're a bunch of things here that want to hurt me and I'm trying to think.\
\
'Oh, hang on -- you can be part of my plan! Look.'\
\
He triumphantly waves around a slab of raw boar meat.\
\
'I hunted myself some bait! Just find a good place to set it down and lure out Hedâkha. A beast like that should be no problem for you, right? ...Right?'","Talk to Lumbag","Lumbag has given you some raw boar meat that might lure out Hedâkha.\
\
You can find a good spot to place the bait somewhere in Dor Pherkha.","Hedâkha defeated","Lure out and defeat Hedâkha"},
[12434]={"'Ah, hello ${CLASS}. Might I trouble you for your help? I am in dire need of it.\
\
'I wish for you to defeat an Orc by the name of Ogarkha. This monster killed my companions and many more. I was powerless to prevent it. I barely escaped with my life. He must be defeated to spare others from his malice.\
\
'If you seek him out, he has been spotted to the north-east, wandering the lands between Maurûsh and the Gorge of Woe. He can be identified by a golden ring he wears on his hand.\
\
'I beg of you, bring down this monster, and bring me his ring as proof of your victory.'","Deliver the golden ring to Shulum in Ub Nishir","Shulum in Ub Nishir has asked you to slay Ogarkha to the north-east of Maurûsh, near the Gorge of Woe, and bring him a trophy as proof.","Retrieved Ogarkha's ring","'${CLASS}, you have returned!'\
\
You hand Shulum the trophy you collected from Ogarkha.\
\
'And you gathered the proof for which I asked. I thank you. You have saved many lives by ridding the lands of that demon. My sorrow over my companions has eased slightly knowing they have been avenged.\
\
'I shall cherish this trophy in their honour.'","The Hunt for Ogarkha","Shulum in Ub Nishir has asked you to slay Ogarkha to the north-east of Maurûsh, near the Gorge of Woe and bring back a trophy of your conquest.","Bring the golden ring to Shulum in Ub Nishir","Return to Shulum in Ub Nishir and give him the trophy you took from Ogarkha.","Defeat Ogarkha and retrieve his golden ring"},
[12435]={"You come across another wind-worn cairn","The old cairn can be found in Elderslade.\
\
You should examine the cairn.","Fróthi brought Scatha's tooth with him to Annâk-khurfu.\
\
You should examine Scatha's tooth.","This cairn looks quite old!","'This pass is not on my map of Elderslade. Fróthi, what of yours? Hmm, it looks like the map on Scatha's tooth has led us to this rocky pass. Could this map lead to Scatha's cave or even his hoard? There is but one way to find out! First, let us rest here for a moment.'\
\
Léothred continues his tale.\
\
'When Gundobad learned the meaning of his name, and of his father's fate, a zeal awoke within him. He would succeed where Gundáric had not, and lead a host of Ai-thúda to conquer Gundabad! Hildáric begged him to reconsider, but he refused, so when Gundobad was of age, Hildáric refused to honour his promise, and remained Lord of Framabárg.'","'This is a very exciting discovery! If this map was carved by Fram, it certainly changes how we should perceive this missive to the dwarves. With all the layers of dust on this tooth, I would say the tooth had not been touched since Thráin discarded the necklace in some forgotten vault of Erebor.\
\
'Now I have more questions than answers, as any historian should. What I do know, however, is that we must follow this map to see where it leads. We should head to the shores of Dvergvát as soon as we are ready!'","'It worries me that we did not find a cairn or some sort of marking here. Let us press on towards the next mark on the map in hopes that it lead us in the right direction!'\
\
Léothred continues his tale.\
\
'Sadly, Gisilhári met with tragedy himself soon after feasting his victory. Flush with pride, and plenty of ale, he declared his intent to name himself King of the Thíuda. He sought out the mearas, announcing his intent to tame and ride one. The attempt ended in failure, and not for the last time among the masters of the Ai-thúda. The mearh he chose threw him, and in the fall he broke his back. He was unable to walk afterward, and died at the age of forty-two, older than any lord of his people since Frumgar, but still far too young.'","You come across another wind-worn cairn by the river's edge","The rocky pass heads north along the river","Talk to Léothred on the shores of Dvergvát","Léothred and Fróthi look to unearth a piece of lost history in Elderslade.","The shores of the Dvergvát lie west of Annâk-khurfu.\
\
You should search Dvergvát's shores for the location where Fram's map begins.","The shores of the Dvergvát lie west of Annâk-khurfu.\
\
You should search the old dwarf-dock for any signs that this is the beginning of Fram's map.","You find another singular, worn stone","Talk to Léothred","Search for signs that this is where Fram's map begins","Léothred can be found at Annâk-khurfu.\
\
You should talk to Léothred at Annâk-khurfu.","Talk to Fróthi at Annâk-khurfu","Whomever made the other cairns must have also made this one","'Ah, another cairn, similar to the one we found on the shores of Dvergvát. It would seem we are following the map correctly after all!'\
\
Léothred continues his tale.\
\
'Gundahári, Gisilhári's son, succeeded him and ruled unremarkably, but well enough. For the first time the Ai-thúda knew true prosperity in the Wells, and they flourished, building many homes in Misthallow and grazing their herds across the Floodfells and even into the valleys of Mithrin. He died peacefully at sixty, and was succeeded by his son Gundáric.'","The Hunt for Scatha","You find a singular, worn stone but no cairn","'Thanks to Fróthi for deciphering the map thus far. We have not lost the trail yet!'\
\
Léothred continues his tale.\
\
'Hildáric became lord of the Ai-thúda after his brother’s disappearance, though matters grew complicated six months later when Bryngertha, Gundáric's widow, gave birth to a son. She called the boy Gundobad, a play on the name of the hall where his father had vanished. When he was born, Hildáric promised to cede lordship to him once he came of age.'","Perhaps this old dwarf-dock is the location?","The next mark on the map lies somewhere in Elderslade.\
\
You should travel east to search for the next location on the map.","The next mark on the map lies somewhere in Elderslade.\
\
You should travel south east to search for the next location on the map.","As you start cleaning the dust-coated tooth, you see some small, hand-carved markings","Examine Scatha's tooth","Léothred can be found following Fram's map in Elderslade.\
\
You should talk to Léothred.","Fróthi can be found at Annâk-khurfu.\
\
You should talk to Fróthi at Annâk-khurfu.","Talk to Léothred at Annâk-khurfu","Search for the next location on the map","'This cairn indeed looks quite old. Perhaps this is the starting point of the map! We must now seek the second marking on the map.\
\
'While we travel, I will continue to recall the tales of Fram's legacy. I believe I had talked of Gundamári. After Gundamári's death, the lordship fell to Fram's youngest son, who had been just five years old when his father died. Gisilhári, who had always seemed less hot-blooded than his brothers, proved to be the most fortunate of the siblings. Under his careful command the Ai-thúda pushed back against the Orcs, winning several decisive battles before finally breaking them and slaying their chief in a great battle by Dvergvát, these very shores.'","'I believe that we are still on the trail. Let us continue.'\
\
Léothred continues his tale.\
\
'Gundáric was an adventurous youth, and had bragged that he would one day be the first Man to enter the Mountain-hold and behold the wonders within. Two years into his reign, he defied the warnings of his advisors, including his younger brother Hildáric. The fool rode to Gundabad's gates and was never seen again.'","This cairn looks very similar to the first cairn that you found","The next mark on the map lies somewhere in Elderslade.\
\
You should travel north-east to search for the next location on the map.","'Fróthi and I agree that we should begin our search in Elderslade with the necklace made from Scatha's teeth. Since it is a relic of those days which we can closely examine, perhaps it will provide a clue as to where Scatha hid. I am no expert on beasts, but to a trained eye, a beast's teeth may tell one much about a creature's eating habits and natural surroundings.\
\
'Perhaps you should take a closer look at the teeth, ${PLAYER}. You have much more experience with beasts than either Fróthi or myself.'","Examine the second cairn","The shores of the Dvergvát lie west of Annâk-khurfu.\
\
You should talk to Léothred there.","'Hmm, let me take a closer look at these markings.... Yes, I see they are indeed carved. These markings are too precise to have been made from any battles the worm was in.... Hmm, for a moment I had wondered if this was a runic inscription, but I have studied much of Rói's Edda-stone in Erebor and these markings are not any form of dwarf-writing, that much is certain!\
\
'Oh! Do you see this curved marking, with the round indent in its centre?! It is different than the others, and if I am not mistaken looks exactly like the lake of Dvergvát, here in Elderslade! I believe this is a map! It is a crude map, but a map all the same!'","Search Dvergvát's shores for the location where Fram's map begins"},
[12436]={"Los cazadores lossoth quedaron impresionados por tu actuación contra el huargo, aunque no lo reconozcan abiertamente.","'Es extraño que pudieras derrotar a un Surmâja sin haber recibido entrenamiento de nuestros cazadores... aunque en nuestro campamento no había sido bien alimentado y la semana pasada estaba muy enfermo.\
\
'Si deseas cazar con nosotros, está bien. Adéntrate en el bosque y recoge la grasa de los bajos vientres de los Surmâja. Uno de nuestros cazadores podrá utilizarla más adelante.\
\
'Busca al suroeste, en las colinas que se alzan tras el lago... ahí es donde encontrarás más Surmâja.'","Grasa de huargo recogida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los huargos pueden encontrarse en las estribaciones del suroeste.\
\
Valtteri te ha ordenado adentrarte en el bosque y cazar huargos, recogiendo la grasa de sus vientres para que los Lossoth puedan usarla más tarde.","La caza ha comenzado","Valtteri se encuentra junto a su jaula de huargos en Kauppa-kohta.\
\
Deberías devolverle a Valtteri la grasa de huargo que te pidió.","Recoge grasa de huargo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'No pensé que sobrevivirías a mi desafío, Sivullinen. Incluso mis propios cazadores podrían haberse visto superados por tantos Surmâja.\
\
'Ahora que has demostrado tu valía, tenemos una última petición.'","Habla con Valtteri","'¿No eres lo bastante hábil para recoger la grasa de Surmâja que te he pedido?'"},
[12437]={"'What is this? The Hunter King? It is a name we have heard rumoured, but there is not much more I can tell you. Perhaps you can help us find the truth.'","The Hunter King?","Talk to Daervunn at Echad Daervunn in the Mournshaws","According to Prestadir, the medallion you found says something about a Hunter King and the Mournshaws.","'You should speak with Daervunn in the Mournshaws, ${PLAYER}. He may have learned something of this Hunter King.'","'Some of our kinsmen have gone on to the Mournshaws to scout the way. Perhaps you should bring this sigil to Daervunn at Echad Daervunn...perhaps he has come upon some knowledge of this Hunter King.\
\
'Echad Daervunn lies far to the south of here in the northern reaches of the Mournshaws.'","Daervunn is at Echad Daervunn in the Mournshaws, far to the south of Echad Idhrenfair.\
\
Prestadir suggested you take the sigil you found to Daervunn in the Mournshaws."},
[12438]={"Gytha Lainey, una cazadora de gran destreza, se encuentra en las Tierras de Bree, en el Campamento de Adso, sobre el Gran Camino del Este entre Bree y Los Gamos.\
\
Gytha está esperando para hablar contigo sobre tu victoria contra Colmilloamarillo en el Bosque Viejo.","El Camino del Cazador","Gytha Lainey, una cazadora de gran destreza, se encuentra en las Tierras de Bree, en el Campamento de Adso, en el camino entre Bree y Los Gamos.\
\
Se te ha indicado que hables con Gytha Lainey para recibir instrucción en el arte del cazador.","'Puedes encontrar a Gytha Lainey en el Campamento de Adso, en el camino entre Bree y Los Gamos.'","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir? Viajaremos al Bosque Viejo, y juzgaré tu valía — si puedes derrotar a Colmilloamarillo, podrías ser digno de mi enseñanza.\
\
'Sin embargo, ten presentes estas dos advertencias. El Bosque Viejo es un lugar confuso para los desprevenidos, y parece que los árboles se mueven cuando no los estás mirando. Incluso si ya has viajado bajo su dosel antes, podrías encontrar que los senderos te son desconocidos ahora.\
\
'Y en segundo lugar, Colmilloamarillo no es tonta. No te enfrentará a menos que logres sacarla de su escondite. Tu habilidad en combate, así como tu destreza para rastrear, serán puestas a prueba.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no puede completarse en comunidad.</rgb>","' ${PLAYERNAME:Ningún cazador[m]|Ninguna cazadora[f]} común podría haber vencido a Colmilloamarillo. ¡Lo has hecho bien!'","Gytha Lainey, una cazadora de gran destreza, se encuentra en las Tierras de Bree, en el Campamento de Adso, sobre el Gran Camino del Este entre Bree y Los Gamos.\
\
Gytha está esperando para hablar contigo sobre el viaje al Bosque Viejo.","'Tu puntería es certera y tu mirada aguda, , pero tu presa aún es débil. Todavía no tienes la habilidad suficiente para enfrentarte por tu cuenta a los enemigos que debes enfrentar.\
\
'Puede que conozca a alguien que pueda guiarte. Gytha Lainey es una cazadora de gran destreza, y aunque tiene poca paciencia para los que no se lo merecen, si considera que eres ${PLAYERNAME:digno[m]|digna[f]} de su instrucción, te enseñará con gusto lo que sabe.\
\
'Búscala en el Campamento de Adso, en el Gran Camino del Este, entre Bree y Los Gamos.'","Para un verdadero cazador, la velocidad y la precisión lo son todo. La falta de una trae mala fortuna. La falta de ambas, desastre.","'Dices que eres ${PLAYERNAME:cazador[m]|cazadora[f]}, pero ¿qué prueba tienes de que has elegido el camino correcto? Tal vez deberías haber sido juglar, como ese tal Prescott que a veces canta sobre mis hazañas. O quizás te habría ido mejor como ${PLAYERNAME:saqueador[m]|saqueadora[f]}, como ese hobbit allá atrás que no le quita los ojos al asado de Adso.\
\
'Aun así, dices que eres ${PLAYERNAME:digno de llamarte cazador[m]|digna de llamarte cazadora[f]}. Entonces seré yo quien lo juzgue, pues tengo un desafío para ti. Un lobo formidable acecha entre las hojas caídas del Bosque Viejo, pero muestra una astucia poco común para su especie y representa una amenaza para quienes se desvían de los senderos.\
\
'Habla conmigo si estás ${PLAYERNAME:dispuesto[m]|dispuesta[f]} a aceptar este desafío, y te acompañaré al bosque. Allí juzgaré tu habilidad para derribar a la temible Colmilloamarillo.'","'Me has sorprendido, . No creí que fueras capaz de encontrar y derrotar a Colmilloamarillo, y por eso te pido disculpas.\
\
'Eres ${PLAYERNAME:un cazador[m]|una cazadora[f]} con gran potencial, y ya estás en camino de dominar una técnica importante por tu cuenta: la capacidad de lanzar tus flechas con mayor rapidez.'","'Lamento haber dudado de ti, ${PLAYER}.'","Viaja con Gytha Lainey al Bosque Viejo"},
[12442]={"La cueva desafortunada","Mineros atrapados rescatados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","La mina parece estable. Encuentra y retira la joya brillante en la parte más profunda de Jid Phêsi.","¡Escapa a la entrada antes de que la mina se derrumbe!","¡Llegas a la entrada justo a tiempo!","'¡Rápido! ¡Debemos salir de aquí antes de que todo se derrumbe!'","¡La cueva está temblando violentamente! ¡Sal de la mina!","Joya recogida. ¡La cueva comienza a temblar!","¡Rescata a los trabajadores y excava los escombros antes de que la mina se derrumbe!","¡Ayuda a los mineros a escapar antes de que la cueva se derrumbe más!","Escombros que bloqueaban el camino destruidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","La cueva parece estable. Recoge la gran joya de la zona más profunda de la cueva","Los enanos de Temámir han estado excavando una cueva en el Cabo en busca de piedras preciosas, pero las paredes resultaron ser demasiado débiles. ¡Ayuda a los enanos a escapar del derrumbe!","Rescata a los mineros atrapados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","La mina se derrumbó","Destruye los escombros que bloquean el camino (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12443]={"Léothred can be found at Hlithseld.\
\
You should talk to Léothred at Hlithseld.","'Sorrowing at the failure of his own wisdom, the Grey Wizard returned to Framabárg bearing grim tidings. Fram was, unsurprisingly, enraged in his turn; he sent the Wizard away as well in scorn.\
\
'One would assume that Wandalb departed in sorrow, with the hope that he might return in time to bring together the two stubborn lords and make them understand each other when their heads had cooled. It would not be so.'","Léothred, the Rohirric scholar, wishes to learn more of the political tensions that arose during Fram's reign over the Ai-thúda.","Talk to Léothred at Hlithseld","Léothred can be found at Framsburg.\
\
You should talk to Léothred at Framsburg.","'Now, ${PLAYER}, I will explain why the treasures of Scatha were all made by dwarves. This is best told to you by the telling of the ill-fated feast:\
\
'Fram invited the lords of neighbouring lands to his hall for a great feast to celebrate the slaying of Scatha. Both Thranduil of Felegoth and Thráin of Erebor sent emissaries, as did the lords of the Wood-men and the Lake-folk, distant kin to the Ai-thúda.'","Talk to Léothred at Framsburg","'The feast was meant to be a great celebration.'","El festín desafortunado"},
[12444]={"Lleva la nota carbonizada a Teitur en Anazârmekhem","El fuego ha dañado terriblemente esta nota, pero algunos fragmentos aún transmiten un significado, que es aterrador y claro: Igash y Kranklûk eran de hecho algo más nefasto de lo que parecían. Mazog puede saber lo que son, pero no es consciente de su lealtad al verdadero Enemigo. El general Talug de Fil Gashan no es más que un regalo de los uruks negros a Mazog. \
\
La nota continuaba explicando que el ejército del general Talug estaba creciendo cada día más y pronto estaría listo para algún tipo de transformación.\
\
Deberías llevar esto a Teitur, el agente de Narfi encargado de vigilar Fil Gashan en Anazârmekhem.","La ilusión del liderazgo","Una nota carbonizada y arrugada, encontrada en el cadáver de Kranklûk, confirmó algunas sospechas que tenían los agentes enanos que vigilaban las Forjas de Khazad-dûm. Lo peor es que mencionaba que Talug, el general de Fil Gashan, no era más que una marioneta.","'¡Absurdo! Raf tenía razón... Le debo una cerveza. Sí, hicimos una apuesta. Él contaba historias de cómo este Orco parecía tener una extraña sombra alrededor de sus ojos... Debería haberlo escuchado.\
\
'Significa que debemos ser rápidos en nuestro asalto contra Fil Gashan, me temo. El tiempo es ahora de la esencia y la necesidad, parece.'","Teitur se encuentra en Anazârmekhem.\
\
Has descubierto esta nota en el cadáver del Uruk Kranklûk, y después de descifrar lo que pudiste, quedó claro que debería ser llevada a Teitur, quien vigila Fil Gashan en Anazârmekhem."},
[12445]={"The cage-waggons can be found to the south-east of Ondoher's Folly.\
\
Faramir has asked you to dismantle the cage-waggons making for Ondoher's Folly and free any slaves you encounter. He also hopes you can learn the identity of the true master of Ondoher's Folly.","Damage wheels on Mordor cage-waggons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Impostor King","Artamir can be found to the south outside Ondoher's Folly in Dagorlad.\
\
You damaged the cage-waggons and learned much of the master of Ondoher's Folly, but you were unable to rescue any slaves. You should return to Artamir and tell him what has happened.","'It is time you learned of the greatest insult dealt against me and my family...\
\
'When my father fell on the hill above, his banner was paraded by the Wainriders and the Orcs as the rest of his company fell. Our foes chased them as they fled into the marshes, and for many years I saw naught of my father's heraldry.\
\
'Not long ago, a man returned to the hill bearing the banner... but it had changed. Age had worn it thin, but what remained was perverted into something between the familiar and the horrid. With the banner unfurled, he called forth the first of the slaves the Orcs had captured in Ithilien... and one by one he tortured and beheaded them beneath my father's banner as the others watched. After all were slain, the bodies were defiled in such terrible ways... I cannot speak them.\
\
'This man dishonours the memory of my father, Ondoher, and twists it to suit his own cruelty. His name is unknown to me, but the Orcs must know it well... for they avert their eyes in his presence.\
\
'If you wish to aid me, learn what you can of this man and free the poor men that have fallen into his hands. The slaves and prisoners are drawn by cage-waggons to the hill along a rough pathway to the east.'","'The Orcs slaughtered them in their cages... like beasts. How horrid...\
\
'Our foe may be of Númenórean blood, but he is no man. Burudagath the Bloodletter... who would hold such a title willingly?\
\
'If he is the true master of Ondoher's Folly, the Host of the West should remain vigilant. You slew so many at Ondoher's Folly, but still their numbers do not dwindle... and this Burudagath seems to hold sway over them all.\
\
'Mincham learned from Orcs and evil Men that the Enemy wishes us to come to the Black Gate safely, but how can such words be trusted now?\
\
'Ruse or not, my friend, I believe only one course remains.'","Talk to Artamir outside Ondoher's Folly","'So the banner of Ondoher did survive! What a shame that it has been used to such an end...'","In his time wandering the Wastes, Faramir has learned the identity of the true master of Ondoher's Folly: a vile Black Númenórean bearing a perverted banner of Gondor.","Damaged wheels on Mordor cage-waggons (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Free slaves from the cage-waggons"},
[12446]={"'Puedes entrar al escondite. Te acompañaré adentro y luego volveré a mi puesto.'","'Me has dicho la contraseña, así que puedes entrar. Te mostraré el camino. Mucha gente ya está dentro. Dejé pasar a Culver el Ingenioso, a Garrett el Retorcido y a algunos de los otros.\
\
'Avísame cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para entrar.'","Habla con Artie Root","Otis Bosquero, el portero de los infiltradores, ha aceptado dejarte entrar al escondite si le dices que estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}.","Artie Root está en su casa en Bree y quiere agradecerte por venir a su pequeña fiesta.","La sorpresa de los infiltradores","Benegar Vallelargo escuchó a un grupo que se hacía llamar 'los infiltradores' planear una sorpresa para Bree y quiere que los detengas antes de que terminen sus preparativos.","Habla con Otis Bosquero y explora el escondite de los infiltradores","'¡No puedo creerlo, ! ¡Este ha sido el mejor cumpleaños de mi vida, y ahora tengo tantos nuevos amigos con quienes compartir esta casa! ¡Mira a todos los pequeñines!\
\
'¡Esa fiesta fue una sorpresa maravillosa y debe haber llevado mucho trabajo! ¡Gracias por ser parte de ella, mi ${PLAYERNAME:nuevo amigo[m]|nueva amiga[f]}!'"},
[12447]={"No debes dejar caer el vino añejo","'Zzz... ¿qué? ¡No me hagas dejar caer mi vino! Oh, ya lo bebí. Eso es terriblemente decepcionante. Iba a donarlo a la Liga de las Posadas para una rara oportunidad de degustación, pero... parece que me dio sed después de tanto correr por el sótano de Bilbo.\
\
¡Cómo me da vueltas la cabeza! Es completamente imposible para mí ir a buscar otra botella ahora, pero estoy seguro de que vi algunas más. Creo que se pueden encontrar en cualquier parte, realmente, si buscas un poco.\
\
¡Deberías ir a buscarla! La Liga de las Posadas estará muy emocionada de tenerla, estoy seguro. Yo solo... tomaré una pequeña siesta mientras estás fuera y por ahí.' \
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Solo puede haber una misión del Agujero Embrujado en curso a la vez.</rgb>","'¡Encantador! ¡Me trajiste otra botella! Eso fue rápido.\
\
'... ¿Dónde está el vino?'","¡Tienes el vino! Ese delicioso vino... No lo dejes caer....","Cora Rizopardo encontró algo maravilloso cuando se aventuró en el Agujero Embrujado de Bilbo: una botella de delicioso, caro, excelente y valioso vino. Le gustaría tener un poco más, pero tiene un poco de sueño.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando termine el evento con el que está asociada. </rgb>","Cora Rizopardo se encuentra fuera del Agujero Embrujado, cerca del Árbol de la Fiesta.\
\
Deberías darle el vino a Cora Rizopardo.","'¡Eso estuvo muy bien hecho, ${PLAYER}! Entregar ese vino a salvo no es tarea fácil. ¿Te importa si me tomo otra copa antes de dárselo a la Liga de las Posadas?'","La excavación de la Liga de las Posadas","Recoge el preciado vino... Mmm","No pudiste llevar el vino a un lugar seguro","Habla con Cora Rizopardo","El excelente vino de Bilbo se encuentra en el Agujero Embrujado, pero debe ser transportado con cuidado o se caerá y se romperá.\
\
Debes llevar el vino a Cora Rizopardo, que te espera en el Árbol de la Fiesta."},
[12448]={"Ausma is ready to infiltrate the fortress.","'Now that we have the location of Shakhajât, we need to gather more information. Specifically, it will be valuable to know how many hobgoblins are stationed in the fortress, and which ones serve as advisors to the warlord. We also need to know Dushtalbúk's plans, both to plan a battle strategy and in order to catch him alone....'\
\
She flashes you a wicked grin.\
\
'There's no way around it: we are going to sneak inside. I hope you still remember the stealthy skills I taught you in our previous adventures together!'","Complete 'Instance: The Inner Circle\\q","Talk to Scout-master Ausma","'Good work on a successful infiltration! I am pleased to learn that the Orc and hobgoblin relationship remains tense; we can exploit that. Still, this bargain with the Angmarim is concerning. Are they trying to make an alliance with Hrímil? She has previously shown animosity to Sauron's servants. Perhaps they need a good word from the hobgoblins to get in the good graces of the Frost-horde? We will need to find out.\
\
'Finding Dushtalbúk's throne room is a good first step, but it is going to be hard to catch him alone. We should continue investigating the surrounding area, and see what we can find out about this Angmarim plot.'","You have successfully infiltrated Shakhajât.\
\
You should talk to Scout-master Ausma in Bárgstad.","The Inner Circle","'Let me know when you're ready to move out. I'm eager to get started!'","Scout-master Ausma thinks the time is right to enter Shakhajât with stealth and learn more about the hobgoblin leadership."},
[12449]={"Master Builder Curugond has tasked you with surveying the damage at the southern and northern Rammas. He believes you may be able to lend a hand to the men stationed on the Out-wall.","Turgon can be found at the South-gate of the Rammas. Ingold can be found at the North-gate of the Rammas.\
\
You should speak with Turgon and Ingold and assist them with protecting the Rammas.","The Integrity of the Rammas","Speak with Ingold","Speak with Turgon","'You are not here to convince me to leave my post, I hope. If so, it is a fool's errand for I plan to defend this gate until the Rohirrim arrive.'","'I would be thankful if you were to lend a hand here at the South-gate. My men and I have been busy protecting the Rammas from the Orcs gathered in the Harlond. Alas, we have not yet been able to turn our attention upon the newly gathered forces in Pelennor Fields.'","'I am Curugond, head builder in Minas Tirith. I've been overseeing city repairs for many years though my crowning achievement is without a doubt the Rammas Echor. Now I have been told that the Rammas is being decimated by Orcs and Trolls. How dare they destroy my livelihood!\
\
'I would like to start overseeing repairs as soon as it is safe again to leave the city. If you are venturing out in Pelennor would you be interested in surveying the damages of the Rammas Echor?\
\
'While you're out there, know that men still protect the Out-wall at the South-gate and North-gate. You may be able to lend a hand to Turgon and Ingold. I am sure they could use it!'"},
[12450]={"Complete: Smuggled Goods","Talk to Skótmun","Talk to Mervárth","The guards' barracks can be found near the entrance to Lake-town.\
\
You should find the Lake-town guards' barracks.","Dagrun can be found in the Trade Commission Headquarters.\
\
You should talk to Dagrun.","Complete: Clean-up Duty","Complete: Taking Notices","'I think he's said all he's going to say to us. Let him rot in that cell.\
\
'We have done well together ${PLAYER}, and then some. Murder unveiled, notorious smuggler-ring broken up, Skótmun locked up, Dagrun happy... not bad for a single day of work!'","The crime scene investigation is complete.\
\
You should talk to Mervárth and decide what to do next.","'I think our first stop should be the Guards' Barracks. I'm on good terms with the Captain, Álarr, and I might be able to get some information out of him. If he's in a good mood today, that is. We'll soon find out!'","There's a rumour spreading around Lake-town that the Master was murdered! Join Mervárth on his investigation to uncover the truth.","Mervárth quickly explains that you found a Lake-town Smuggler kerchief at the murder location. Dagrun grins and slams her hands flat on her desk.\
\
'This is it! This evidence, combined with the illegal goods you found in Esgaroth, is enough to bring in Skótmun for questioning - that louse! Mervárth, get into that warehouse and bring him in. I doubt he will come easily, so bring your friend. At last, we've got him!'","The Investigation","Skótmun can be found in the holding cell in the Trade Commission Headquarters.\
\
You should talk to Skótmun.","With access to the location of the murder, you can now begin the investigation into the Master's unexpected demise.\
\
You should investigate the murder location with Mervárth.","'Oh, it's YOU. Come to relish your victory?'","'I am certain the Master's death was no mere accident and I have every intention of revealing those responsible! I imagine you're intrigued by this mystery as well? By all means, feel free to come along.'","Find the Lake-town guards' barracks","Found the Lake-town guards' barracks","'You're here about the Master's death, is that it? As much as I hate to admit it, especially to his face, Mervárth here was instrumental in catching an especially elusive house-robber just last month. So for you two, I will confirm the rumour: the Master WAS murdered, but keep it to yourselves! We don't want all Lake-town in a panic over it. \
\
'I suppose Mervárth might help in finding the killer... if you helped with some of this tedious work that's been piling up.'","Captain Álarr can be found inside the guards' barracks in Lake-town.\
\
You should talk to Álarr.","Captain Álarr has agreed to give you access to the location of the murder in return for taking care of some unpleasant work for him.\
\
You should complete quests for Captain Álarr.","'Good work bringing in Skótmun. I've questioned him, but he would not admit to the murder. Belligerent fool, as always. You may go speak to him yourself, if you wish.'","Talk to Captain Álarr","'You're quite good at this, ${PLAYER}! If you ever want to retire from the adventuring life, I'm sure I could put you to work scrubbing the floors! You can go ahead and investigate the murder location now. I've sent word that you're coming.'","Dagrun can be found in the Trade Commission Headquarters.\
\
You should complete quests for Dagrun.","Mervárth can be summoned to your side if you were separated.\
\
You should talk to Mervárth.","Complete: The Smugglers' Den","Talk to Álarr, The Captain of the Guard","Talk to Dagrun","Mervárth can be found near the Master's Manor in Lake-town.\
\
You should talk to Mervárth.","Complete: The Site of the Murder","Find the Trade Commission Headquarters","'If the Lake-town Smugglers are involved, we should go have a chat with my boss, Dagrun, Captain of the Market. She will want to know. You can find her headquarters on the other side of town.'","Complete: Breaking Up the Gang","The Trade Commission Headquarters can be found in Lake-town.\
\
You should find the Trade Commission Headquarters."},
[12451]={"Muestra el collar a alguien en el campamento de los cazadores de tesoros","La leyenda cuenta que un poderoso huargo recibió la oportunidad de gobernar a todos los huargos a cambio de servir a la Corona de Hierro. Se forjó un collar de hierro y se usaron poderosos hechizos para encantar el objeto. La gran bestia fue abatida y el collar retirado, pero las historias sobre la bestia se han transmitido entre los Hombres de las Quebradas del Norte a lo largo de las eras.","'Ah, este collar es una cosa maligna. ¡Pero es bueno que lo hayas encontrado!\
\
'Este es el collar de Krithmog, perdido durante medio siglo. Supongo que ha pasado de huargo en huargo, y lo encontraste por casualidad. Una vez se usó para atar a Krithmog al servicio de Angmar. ¡Quizá vuelva a atarlo, pero esta vez a su perdición!'","Will Saucedal está en el campamento de los cazadores de tesoros fuera de la ciudad de Fornost, en el norte de las Quebradas del Norte.\
\
Deberías hablar con Will Saucedal.","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","El collar de hierro","Recuerdas la leyenda del rey de los huargos, Krithmog. El campamento de los cazadores de tesoros, ocupado por gente interesada en Fornost, sería un buen lugar para llevar el collar de hierro que descubriste."},
[12452]={"The wildflowers vanish beneath the surface of the water, but nothing changes","Rossaran and Bruidis have a plan to help those who were wounded during the storm and the Wave-hunter's arrival on the Shield Isles.","'All done? Very good, and thank you!\
\
'The salve will take awhile to steep, but once it is prepared I will have Rossaran bring it around to the injured sailors. You have done more than enough, and we appreciate every bit of it! But do not let me distract you any further... there is surely work to be done elsewhere on the Shield Isles, and I know the Lady Nauriel wants nothing to delay the rescue of her son from the Kindred of the Coins!\
\
'But I know a thing or two about such things, and we will want the members of the crew to be as rested and comfortable as they can be when the time comes to mount the rescue. Injured men fight poorly, no matter how brave they may be when hale, or during peacetime.\
\
'Thank you once again, ${PLAYER}. We will not forget that you helped us... all of us!'","'Add the fish-scales to the tub of water, if you would.'","Bruidis is by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles.","'My wife Bruidis wants to prepare a salve that will ease the sailors' recovery. She has set me to fish, for apparently this salve has need of fish-scales, but there are other ingredients to be gathered. Speak to her and she will tell you what else she needs, if you are of a mind to help.'","Rossaran is on the Wave-hunter where it has run aground in the Shield Isles.","Collect scraggly herbs from the nearby beach (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Add the herbs to the tub of water by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles","The herbs sink into the water. Now what?","'This salve requires herbs tough enough to grow on the nearby beach, flowers nourished by the damp air blanketing this isle, and several pieces of tree-bark, which you should be able to take from a large grey tree I saw to the west. Bring these ingredients back to me and I will tell you about the next steps.'","'You found the things I need! I am very pleased to hear it, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Now you need to steep each of the ingredients in the tub of water I have prepared to the south-east: the herbs the longest, followed by the flowers, and finally the tree-bark. After you have added each of these things to the water, speak to Rossaran and obtain as many fish-scales as he can give you, and add those to the tub last of all.'","Rossaran gives you the scales from the several fish he has caught","Talk to Rossaran on the Wave-hunter in the Shield Isles","The Isles: Bruidis and Rossaran","Add the wild-flowers to the tub of water by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles","Collect tree-bark from the large grey tree west of Bruidis (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected scraggly herbs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected wild-flowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Many of the sailors who crewed the Wave-hunter sustained injuries during the storm, and Bruidis wants to prepare a salve that will help make them more comfortable while they recover. She has set me to fish, for apparently this salve has need of fish-scales, but there are other ingredients to be gathered. Speak to her and she will tell you what else she needs, if you are of a mind to help.'","The tree-bark sinks into the water, but nothing obvious changes","The tub of water where Bruidis plans to brew the salve is to the south-east, near the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles.","The fish scales join everything else in the tub. Is the salve complete?","Collected tree-bark (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Your timing is just about perfect, ${PLAYER}, for I have finished scaling the fish I caught. Here you go.\
\
'What next? You need to add the scales to the water tub? Go on, then.'","'I hope I caught enough fish-scales for Bruidis's purposes.'","'My husband should have enough fish-scales by now.'","Add the fish scales to the tub of water by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles","Collect wild-flowers from the isle near Voyage's End (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Now you need to steep each of the ingredients in the tub of water I have prepared to the south-east: the herbs the longest, followed by the flowers, and finally the tree-bark. After you have added each of these things to the water, speak to Rossaran and obtain as many fish-scales as he can give you, and add those to the tub last of all.'","Add the tree-bark to the tub of water by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles","Bruidis sent you to look for herbs, flowers, and tree bark at several different locations throughout the Shield Isles.","'Rossaran has enlisted you to help me gather the ingredients I need to brew the salve? He is a good man, my husband. But you would have offered to help me anyway, would you not? I think I am a good judge of character, not just of husbands but of friends, as well.\
\
'This salve requires herbs tough enough to grow on the nearby beach, flowers nourished by the damp air blanketing this isle, and several pieces of tree-bark, which you should be able to take from a large grey tree I saw to the west. Bring these ingredients back to me and I will tell you about the next steps.'","Talk to Bruidis by the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles"},
[12453]={"Driftwood's eyes light with recognition and surprise","Return to Voyage's End and check on your crew","Manadhon told you the man called Driftwood might be found on the lower level of Halrax, on the south-western side of the inlet.","'But Driftwood is a man grown, and he does not need me to protect him. He lives on the lower level of Halrax, on the south-western side of the inlet, if you need to speak with him so badly. But I don't want anyone coming back here and causing trouble if he doesn't want to speak to you.'","Having defeated many supporters of the Heirs of Castamir throughout the Shield Isles, you should return to the Wave-hunter.","Despite his parting words, Driftwood has come to the Wave-hunter","Horn stares at the Elf, his mouth agape. 'Sigileth... the sister of Corudan!'","'I believed Corudan's sister Sigileth was dead, ${PLAYER}, and that she perished within Dol Guldur before we adventured in Rohan. But no, she is alive and seems eager to shame me on his behalf! Have you learned what happened to Corudan at Helm's Deep? You had better tell me what happened to him, and quickly, for I think his sister may be about to stick me with her famous knives, and right now I confess I might deserve it!'\
\
You tell Horn what you know about Corudan's captivity by the Kindred of the Coins and your mission to Umbar. When you have finished, he rubs his eyes.\
\
'After the Battle of Pelennor Fields, I wandered without purpose. I came to this land because I did not want to get involved, but even that proved a lie. I called myself Bymerë at first, and told myself Horn was dead. But as I lived here, drowning my old sorrows with ale and trying to forget what I had done and what I had been, I saw crimes I could not forgive; as I opposed them I took on a new name: Driftwood. I believed the Heirs of Castamir might again threaten Gondor... and if they had victory there, would not Rohan be next? So I made things difficult for them, as I could. I thought I might gain an audience with Balakhôr's widow if I claimed to have slain one of her enemies, and so end the threat of the Heirs of Castamir.\
\
'Most of my plans ended in the bottom of a mug of ale, ${PLAYER}. When I was Horn, and fought alongside friends, it was different. Driftwood is alone, and accomplishes nothing. It is useless.'\
\
You tell Horn that it could be different, and he shakes his head.\
\
'This is my place now. I spend my days fighting Corsairs and my nights here, drowning in my cups. I suggest you defeat the Corsairs of the Shield Isles, for the sake of our past friendship, and then return to your ship. Horn is dead; only Driftwood remains, and he cannot help you.'","'This is my place now. I spend my days fighting Corsairs and my nights here, drowning in my cups. I suggest you defeat the Corsairs of the Shield Isles, for the sake of our past friendship, and then return to your ship. Horn is dead; only Driftwood remains, and he cannot help you.'","Sigileth has joined you in Halrax.","Driftwood stands on the lower level of Halrax.","'Aye, I know the man called Driftwood. Leastways, I know him as much as any other who lives in Halrax. You don't ask questions about folk who end up in Zîrar Tarka. This is a place for lost things, and some of those things don't want to be found, if you take my meaning.'\
\
You tell Manadhon that you might have information of interest to Driftwood, and a friend to the man would help you find him.\
\
'Maybe that's so and maybe that isn't, but this is not a place for friends, stranger. He is here most every night, drinking, and he is generous with his coin. Perhaps that makes us friends after all.\
\
'But he is a man grown, and he does not need me to protect him. He lives on the lower level of Halrax, on the south-western side of the inlet, if you need to speak with him so badly. But I don't want anyone coming back here and causing trouble if he doesn't want to speak to you.'","Talk to Driftwood at Voyage's End","Manadhon, the bartender of Halrax, has given you a lead on the man called Driftwood.","Many Corsairs throughout the Shield Isles support the Heirs of Castamir, and Driftwood has asked you to continue his work of making things difficult for them.","The Isles: Driftwood","'Sigileth... the sister of Corudan!'","Defeat Corsairs throughout the Shield Isles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The man called Driftwood is deep in his cups on the lower level of Halrax, on the south-western side of the inlet.","Defeated Corsairs throughout the Shield Isles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Find Driftwood on the lower level of Halrax","Driftwood, troubled by his past and seeking to do right, has joined your crew!","Driftwood stands suddenly, knocking his chair to the floor.","'It is true, Corudan is my brother, and he needs our help.'\
\
Sigileth stares at Horn, daring him to speak, but he wisely keeps his silence.\
\
'I have heard of your adventures with ${PLAYER}, Horn of Rohan, and with my brother, and I have been told of the choice you made when the Battle of Pelennor Fields was ended. It is not my place to judge whether your choice was well-considered or ill-thought, and I will not do so.\
\
'But I will ask this of you. Did you consider my brother Corudan to be a friend? Did you think you knew him? This, then, is my last question.\
\
'Would Corudan come to your aid, if your positions were reversed? Or would he give in to cowardice, and run away, leaving the hard work to others?'","The man called Driftwood is deep in his cups","'No... it cannot be!'\
\
Driftwood stares at you with astonishment, the ale-inspired cloudiness of his eyes draining away.\
\
'You... ${PLAYER}... I cannot believe it! I never thought... I never thought I would see you again.'\
\
There can be no mistake. This is Horn of Rohan, though months of hard living on the road and in the wild have weathered his clothes. His face is still familiar, but the war and its worries have left their marks upon it, and he seems more aged than you remember.\
\
'What brings you to the Shield Isles, ${PLAYER}? You have not let down your own folk, as I have, surely? I cannot imagine that. You were always stronger in mind than I was, with courage to spare. It is the truth, and we both know it. And Nona was... Nona was stronger than both of us. But... what do you have to say of yourself? You are not running away from something. You were always running... toward.'\
\
Before you can gather your thoughts to speak, someone steps close behind you. She stares at Horn with a hard look in her eyes, and you know you must introduce her.\
\
'This is Sigileth,' you say.","'Would Corudan come to your aid, if your positions were reversed?'","Wait for Driftwood to acknowledge your presence","Driftwood stands by the Wave-hunter in the Shield Isles.","Talk to Sigileth in Halrax","'I have changed my mind, ${PLAYER}. Sigileth is right: were our positions reversed, Corudan would stop at nothing to come to my rescue or yours.\
\
'I will join you in this, my old friend, if you will have me. The Shield Isles are a place for lost and broken things, but perhaps such things need not stay lost forever, and maybe with friendship they can be repaired. I will join you once again... for Corudan, and to keep the Kindred of the Coins from endangering Gondor, Rohan... and other, more distant lands.\
\
'I spoke truly when I told you Horn was dead. I am Driftwood now, and would have your crew call me by this name. I hope this is agreeable to you, my friend. And one more thing: you might have told me Sigileth no longer possesses her famous knives! I might have thought more clearly in Halrax if I knew I was not in danger of being sliced open!'\
\
You assure Driftwood that while she no longer possesses Lanchigil and Egnassigil, Sigileth has been practicing with her new blade, and even without a name she could still do considerable damage with it.\
\
'Oh,' he responds. 'Perfect.'","Talk to Driftwood on the lower level of Halrax"},
[12454]={"Talk to Driftwood on the upper level of Halrax","Return to Voyage's End and check on your crew","Despite his parting words, Driftwood has come to the Wave-hunter","'This is not a place for friends, stranger. He is here most every night, drinking, and he is generous with his coin. Perhaps that makes us friends after all. But he is a man grown, and he does not need me to protect him. He was just here, moments ago, if you need to speak with him so badly. He went off to the east. But I don't want anyone coming back here and causing trouble if he doesn't want to speak to you.'","Having satisfied Driftwood's request, you should return to the Wave-hunter.","'I think Driftwood used to be a robber himself, stealing from wealthy merchants somewhere in Gondor. He knows his way around ships, so perhaps he plied his trade along one of the rivers in Gondor. But something went wrong. Or maybe he just tired of the life and sought to leave it behind. But for all his intentions, and despite taking a new name, Driftwood is still a robber, and still he steals... but he tells himself it is different.\
\
'I do not know. I try not to pry.'","Corsairs throughout the Shield Isles carry money-purses that Driftwood recovers and donates to Manadhon.","'I told you there was little you could offer me that I need, stranger, but I may have been wrong.\
\
'I have not always been proud of the life I chose, but at least I can say that I chose it. I followed the path I was on until I decided it was not for me, and then I took another path. But your arrival at this place, and the words you spoke to me, have made me realize that the road I followed was not the straight way I envisioned; instead it twisted and curved through the wild in a way I did not expect... only to rejoin the earlier path I had been on, the one I thought I left behind.\
\
'Stealing from the Corsairs and giving their money-purses to Manadhon for the support of those in Halrax who need it... that is a small thing, and small things are insufficient. I need a truly different path, ${PLAYER}, and I believe you are the sort to cut your own way through the wild. I will accompany you as you face the Kindred of the Coins, for I believe you herald the truly different path I have been seeking.\
\
'If you will respect my privacy and ask no questions of my past, Driftwood is with you.'","Driftwood, hoping to make up for something in his past, has joined your crew!","'Aye, I know the man called Driftwood. Leastways, I know him as much as any other who lives in Halrax. You don't ask questions about folk who end up in Zîrar Tarka. This is a place for lost things, and some of those things don't want to be found, if you take my meaning.'\
\
You tell Manadhon that you might have information of interest to Driftwood, and a friend to the man would help you find him.\
\
'Maybe that's so and maybe that isn't, but this is not a place for friends, stranger. He is here most every night, drinking, and he is generous with his coin. Perhaps that makes us friends after all. But he is a man grown, and he does not need me to protect him. He was just here, moments ago, if you need to speak with him so badly. He went off to the east. But I don't want anyone coming back here and causing trouble if he doesn't want to speak to you.'","Talk to Driftwood at Voyage's End","Collected money-purses (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Manadhon, the bartender of Halrax, has given you a lead on the man called Driftwood.","The Isles: Driftwood","Collect money-purses from Corsairs throughout the Shield Isles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Manadhon told you the man called Driftwood might be found somewhere to the east in Halrax.","'You are the one who is looking for me? By my guess you are from the ship that ran aground north of Bakhjâd in the recent storm... a more common occurrence of late than it has been. I have not seen you before, and Driftwood makes it his business to see people before they see him, if you take my meaning. The Shield Isles are a place for the lost, and most lost things prefer to stay that way. Why do you seek me?'\
\
You tell Driftwood that you are interested in Saklaphêl's bounties upon the Kindred of the Coins, and that you understand he might share that interest.\
\
'Perhaps, stranger, and perhaps not. If you think I desire the wealth of the reward, you are mistaken. In a past life I stole more coins than you could spend in a lifetime, not the gold phâraz or the silver gîmil of Umbar, but the currency of Gondor; that life is finished. Now I rob only those who steal from others, and give every coin to folk in need.\
\
'If we are to do business, I want to know you share my mind. Continue my work, stranger, and take the money-purses from Corsairs here in the Shield Isles. Bring them to Manadhon here in Halrax when you have finished. He will know the use to which this stolen money should be put.\
\
'But I am content to remain here. There is little you could offer me that I need.'","Driftwood has directed you to bring the money-purses to Manadhon on the upper level of Halrax.","Driftwood stands by the Wave-hunter in the Shield Isles.","'You have brought me these money-purses at the direction of our mutual friend Driftwood, have you not?'\
\
You tell Manadhon that he is correct, and Driftwood believed the bartender would know what to do with them.\
\
'I do, for it is the same every week. Driftwood comes here with his pockets full of money-purses he has taken from Corsairs, and I use the coin to support the folk of Halrax who have nothing, giving them food, giving them drink, and making the ill-gotten wealth of the Corsairs serve a beneficial purpose. Why does he do this? He has not said, but I have pieced together a little of it.\
\
'I think he used to be a robber himself, stealing from wealthy merchants somewhere in Gondor. He knows his way around ships, so perhaps he plied his trade along one of the rivers in Gondor. But something went wrong. Or maybe he just tired of the life and sought to leave it behind. But for all his intentions, and despite taking a new name, Driftwood is still a robber, and still he steals... but he tells himself it is different.\
\
'I do not know. I try not to pry.'","'If we are to do business, I want to know you share my mind. Continue my work, stranger, and take the money-purses from Corsairs here in the Shield Isles. Bring them to Manadhon here in Halrax when you have finished. He will know the use to which this stolen money should be put.\
\
'But I am content to remain here. There is little you could offer me that I need.'","Bring the money-purses to Manadhon on the upper level of Halrax"},
[12455]={"Elladan and Elrohir have saved Yahîm from danger, and he waits to speak with you in Bakhjâd.","This must be the sword Yahîm left behind when the Elves rescued him","The Isles: Elladan and Elrohir","'You are a friend of these Elves? I am not accustomed to speaking with such as they, but I cannot deny that if they had not come along I would now be dead.\
\
'My name is Yahîm, and I am not one to refuse aid when it is offered! It is true: I am a Corsair, and Mâr Naphra is my home, but I confess I am currently without a ship. If you hold a grudge against my kind, I understand it, but we are not currently at sea. On land can we not remain friendly?\
\
'I appreciate the timely intervention of these Elves, and I do not mean to be ungrateful... but when I followed them to safety I left my sword behind. If you will return to the kergrim-infested ruin atop this island and retrieve my sword for me, I will see that you are rewarded. The Elves seemed more interested in what I might know than what valuables I might give to them, if you take my meaning. I will tell you what I know about the Heirs of Castamir and the Kindred of the Coins... if you bring my sword to me at my home by the water on the eastern side of Mâr Naphra. Unless I have misjudged your intent, that is what you want to know, is it not?\
\
'If you will do this, can I ask for one more favour? Slay some more of the kergrim for me, will you? They are disgusting creatures, spreading filth and disease, and they should not remain among the old ruins. It is not right.'","Elladan and Elrohir have rescued a resident of the Shield Isles from danger, and he may share useful information with you if you help him further.","'Yahîm said you should bring his sword to him at his home by the water on the eastern side of Mâr Naphra. It may be he will know something useful about the Heirs of Castamir or the Kindred of the Coins. Once you have spoken with him, we will meet you back at the Wave-hunter.'","'Thank you for returning my sword to me. How would I make my living without it?'\
\
Yahîm lowers his voice, and looks to either side before continuing in a hushed tone.\
\
'The life of a Corsair is not what it once was, I confess it. I blame the Heirs of Castamir for that, but when I do so I make sure not to do so loudly, or when not in the company of those I know well. I make an exception for you and for your Elf companions, for if you cannot trust those who save your life, who can you trust?\
\
'I promised you knowledge. Here it is: after the death of Balakhôr the Scourge in Gondor, his widow Saklaphêl thought to claim the rule of Umbar, acting as regent through their young son Balakhâd, but the rioting in the streets and the rise of the Kindred of the Coins caused her to abandon both that plan and the city; she fled to the Shield Isles, and now lives in exile here in Mâr Naphra. None see her. She issues orders to her servants through Galadaith, her spokesman. Supporters of the Heirs of Castamir believe she will organize the remaining Corsairs and attack the city and the Kindred who control it.\
\
'But I have heard there is a reason she cannot. Some say Balakhâd died during the fighting when the city fell, but others say that the Kindred hold him hostage, and Saklaphêl dares not attack the city for fear he will be slain.\
\
'Once again I thank you and those Elves for the rescue, and for the return of my sword. I hope my information is of help to you.'","'What did Yahîm have to say about the Heirs of Castamir and the Kindred of the Coins? Elladan and I would have rescued him no matter what information he had to share... but if his information is useful then so much the better.'\
\
You tell Elrohir what the Corsair had to say, and he mulls it over for a moment.\
\
'He does not know if the son of Balakhôr and Saklaphêl is alive and held by the Kindred of the Coins, but I think we have seen enough to know that they are the type to take prisoners. It could be Thorongil and Corudan and Balakhâd are all being held in the same dungeon, the easier to keep an eye upon them. The Kindred can then use each of them as leverage upon their respective families and friends.\
\
'It is interesting, too, that Saklaphêl fled to Mâr Naphra. At least we will know from where the Heirs of Castamir might be organized, should they once again become a threat. It is worth keeping an eye upon, anyway. As if there was not enough to do already!\
\
'Thank you for helping us with Yahîm, ${PLAYER}. Elladan and I will see what else we can help with around here.'","Elladan and Elrohir have returned to the Wave-hunter in the Shield Isles.","'This is a very strange adventure, ${PLAYER}, where we must save our foes and rely upon what they can tell us to free our friends. My head spins, but I think Elrohir and I did the right thing. We could not leave Yahîm to be devoured by the kergrim, whether his allegiance is to the Heirs of Castamir or not. Corsair or no, he is still a Man, and he needed help.\
\
'My brother feels the same, I am certain of it.'","Talk to Yahîm by Elrohir in Bakhjâd","Bring Yahîm his sword at his home by the water on the eastern side of Mâr Naphra","'Watch yourself among the wrecks, ${PLAYER}. The kergrim are dangerous.'","Yahîm waits for you to return his sword to him near his home by the water on the eastern side of Mâr Naphra.","'Once again I thank you and those Elves for the rescue, and for the return of my sword. I hope my information is of help to you.'","Defeat kergrim among the ruins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Elladan at Voyage's End","'We saved him from the kergrim and brought him down here, though he is a Corsair and a foe of our mission. Have we done wrong?'","'My brother and I thought to scout Bakhjâd and avoid the attention of the Corsair settlement we discovered in the island's interior, but it was not long before we heard the sound of someone calling for help from within the ruin atop this hill. We could not remain idle, ${PLAYER}, you understand. We went to investigate and only then discovered that he was clearly a Corsair; by most accounting he is a foe of our mission, but we could not leave him to be devoured by the kergrim that threatened him.\
\
'We saved him and brought him back here. Have we done wrong?'","Retrieve Yahîm's sword from the kergrim-infested ruins","Yahîm has asked you to retrieve his sword from the kergrim den where he lost it, and to slay any of the creatures you can.","Defeated kergrim among the ruins (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Elrohir at Voyage's End","'If you will return to the kergrim-infested ruin atop this island and retrieve my sword for me, I will see that you are rewarded. I also ask that you slay some more of the kergrim for me. They are disgusting creatures, spreading filth and disease, and they should not remain among the old ruins. It is not right.'"},
[12456]={"Galengam may be interested in this one","'I have heard that salamander legs and toad legs can be considered something of a delicacy, if they are prepared correctly. I understand you will find the raw ingredients for such a feast to the east of here, and while you see about collecting those, I will find out how to prepare them. Meet me back at the ship when you have enough salamander and toad legs, and perhaps we can corner the market on these goods. And if not, well, I assume the crew of the Wave-hunter will want something to eat.'","Collect salamander legs on the Shield Isles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Galengam is north of Halrax.","Find the vendor on the eastern side of the inlet","Salamanders and toads can be found east of Halrax in the Shield Isles, and Galengam believes their legs might prove delicious for his customers... or for the crew of the Wave-hunter.","Galengam will be interested in this one","Talk to Galengam outside Halrax","Galengam has asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at several vendors within Halrax, to assess the level of his competition.","Galengam could be interested in this one","Galengam has asked you to clear away some of the dense vegetation near his gathered supplies.","Bring the salamander and toad legs to Galengam at Voyage's End","'Yes, thank you. Now the sunlight should dry out these supplies, and I can sell them at the market in Halrax as soon as they stop dripping.'\
\
You ask Galengam if he really believes he can sell the supplies he took from the Wave-hunter, and he responds with a breezy laugh, apparently misunderstanding your question.\
\
'I can sell anything, ${PLAYER}! Am I not the King's Own Merchant? But you raise a good point. Perhaps you should <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at the vendors within Halrax and see what I will have to face for competition. I am only concerned with those vendors who have stalls along the main road that leads into the city; worry not about those up the hill.'","'What level of competition will I face at the market within Halrax?'\
\
You tell Galengam about the type of goods you saw for sale within the town, and his forehead creases with thought.\
\
'I planned to sell the goods we brought with us on the ship, ${PLAYER}, for I believed the residents here would believe them to be unusual... but I think now that will not be sufficient. I have heard that salamander legs and toad legs can be considered something of a delicacy, if they are prepared correctly. I understand you will find the raw ingredients for such a feast to the east of here, and while you see about collecting those, I will find out how to prepare them. Meet me back at the ship when you have enough salamander and toad legs, and perhaps we can corner the market on these goods. And if not, well, I assume the crew of the Wave-hunter will want something to eat.\
\
'It is a shame not to sell the supplies I hauled all the way here, but it will take too long for them to dry out, and I need the coin coming in as soon as possible!'","Find the first vendor's stall as you enter Halrax","Galengam might be interested in this one","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at the vendor by an intersection in Halrax","Find the vendor near the base of the sloping road in Halrax","Collected toad legs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'There you are, ${PLAYER}. The mark of a truly great merchant is how well he responds to adverse conditions, and I plan to prove I am the finest in all the world, no matter the challenge with which I am confronted!\
\
'That vegetation will become a problem if it is not cleared away. Will you do that for me?'","Collect toad legs on the Shield Isles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Galengam has not been in the Shield Isles for long and the merchant is already up to something.","This vendor is conveniently-located right by the eastern docks in Halrax","Galengam has returned to the Wave-hunter in the Shield Isles.","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at the first vendor's stall as you enter Halrax","A lovely turquoise awning protects this vendor's goods from the weather","Hard to see from the road, this vendor should be little competition for Galengam","'That vegetation will become a problem if it is not cleared away. Will you do that for me?'","Collected salamander legs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Perhaps you should <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> at the vendors within Halrax and see what I will have to face for competition. I am only concerned with those vendors who have stalls along the main road that leads into the city; worry not about those up the hill.'","Cleared away vegetation (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at the vendor near the base of the sloping road in Halrax","Clear away concealing vegetation (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Isles: Galengam's Scheme","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at the vendor's goods on the eastern side of the inlet","'No one will tell me the right way to prepare toad or salamander legs! The folk of these isles must know I would drive them right out of business if they shared the secret with me... which of course I would, so they are right to worry!\
\
'I will keep these legs you have brought me in a barrel of seawater until I learn the secret. I will not give up! Am I not the King's Own Merchant?\
\
'In the meantime, keep an eye out for other mercantile opportunities, ${PLAYER}. I know we are here to rescue the young heir of Pinnath Gelin, but there is no reason we cannot make a little coin on the way, is there? No, there is not!'","This vendor serves a variety of fresh fruits collected from the nearby isles","Find the vendor by a major intersection in Halrax"},
[12457]={"Gangur asked you to defeat worms and drakes in the high places of an island to the south, and to search their lair for corroded rock samples that might prove interesting to him.","'Is that you, ${PLAYER}? Oh, I am glad to see you. I am drenched through to my skin, and as my clothes dry I can feel the salt left behind. It is not pleasant, but I am lucky to be alive! Why did I allow you to talk me into this voyage?'\
\
You tell Gangur that you are relieved to see he still lives, for it was believed that he was lost overboard during the storm.\
\
'That is exactly what happened. I know it was foolish of me to go up on deck during the storm, but I feared the ship would fill with water and I would have no hope of survival if I remained below deck. There was a tremendous wave and I was swept overboard. Someone was looking out for me, but I cannot imagine why. More deserving dwarves than I have been favoured by the First Crafter. I thought I was sure to drown, and I saw... well, never mind what I saw. I cannot believe it, myself.\
\
'I lost my pickaxe and my satchel. I was fortunate enough to wash ashore; perhaps they have fetched up along one of these islands too. Do you think you could look for them for me? While you look for those, could you also retrieve some rock samples for me from the islands hereabout? I am curious about something. I will be... well, I will be right here. I am still too water-logged to go anywhere.'","Gangur Farwend has asked you to retrieve the pick-axe and satchel he lost when he fell overboard. Additionally, he wants you to bring him rock samples from the island onto which he washed ashore.","Bring Gangur's satchel, pick-axe, and rock samples to him on the island where he washed ashore","Collect corroded rock samples on the island south of Gangur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected rock samples for Gangur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gangur Farwend has returned to the Wave-hunter on the Shield Isles and waits for you to bring him the corroded rock samples he requested.","Collect rock samples from the island where Gangur came ashore (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You found Gangur's pick-axe. Fortunately it has not been damaged","Retrieve Gangur's pick-axe from the coast nearby","Retrieve Gangur's satchel from the coast nearby","Defeated worms or drakes for Gangur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Isles: Gangur's Vision","Gangur Farwend is lucky to be alive, but his experience has left him all the more eager to accomplish his mission.","'I heard the calls of some lizards or worms coming from the heights of the island to the south. How about you look to combat those creatures and retrieve some more rock samples from their lair? I think I am just about dried out enough to make my way back to the ship, and I will meet you there when you have fulfilled this last request of mine.'","Bring corroded rock samples to Gangur at Voyage's End","Defeat worms or drakes in the high places of the island south of Gangur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gangur turns the corroded rock samples you retrieved over and over in his hands, but his scowl deepens the longer he looks at them.\
\
'These rocks are like the others. The only difference is they are melted by the corrosive breath of the drakes. I admit it is not what I was hoping to see. I thought Khôltekh the Cunning might have gotten the shiny material that was embedded in his medallion from these islands, but if so its location remains a secret.'\
\
He sighs heavily and then looks at you with a more open expression than you are accustomed to seeing on his face. He seems almost haunted.\
\
'When I fell in the water I swallowed too much sea-water, and I felt the life leaving me. I cannot tell you now if my eyes were open or shut, but I believed them to be open, and before the blackness took me... I saw it.'\
\
Gangur pauses, as if gathering the strength to go on. You let him wait until he is ready to continue.\
\
'It was a great shelled beast, all tentacles and siphons, and its spiral shell was encrusted with the shining jewel of my dreams, glimmering like an opal but with every facet a riot of colour. Huge the creature was, but it paid me no mind even as it filled the great expanse of my vision. And then it was gone.\
\
'Was this the dream of a dying dwarf, ${PLAYER}? Maybe it was. But I cannot forget the sight of it. That vision will haunt me to my last day... I know it.\
\
'Thank you for listening to my story, but please do not tell anyone else of it. I will try to put it from my mind and help with the mission... as much as I can.'","'You found my things! I was holding them when I went overboard, so it make sense to me that they would arrive along roughly the same coastline as I did. They are in better shape than I am, that is for certain. I will need to dry them out in the sun all the same, but they are no worse for wear.\
\
'I was hoping these rock samples you brought me would have some hint of sparkle in them, but while there are salt-crystals embedded within them, there is little else of value. And yet I saw...'\
\
Gangur falls quiet.\
\
'I heard the calls of some lizards or worms coming from the heights of the island to the south. How about you look to combat those creatures and retrieve some more rock samples from their lair? I think I am just about dried out enough to make my way back to the ship, and I will meet you there when you have fulfilled this last request of mine.'","Collected corroded rock samples for Gangur (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I know it was foolish of me to go up on deck during the storm, but I feared the ship would fill with water and I would have no hope of survival if I remained below deck. There was a tremendous wave and I was swept overboard. Someone was looking out for me, but I cannot imagine why. More deserving dwarves than I have been favoured by the First Crafter. I thought I was sure to drown, and I saw... well, never mind what I saw. I cannot believe it, myself.\
\
'I lost my pickaxe and my satchel. I was fortunate enough to wash ashore; perhaps they have fetched up along one of these islands too. Do you think you could look for them for me? While you look for those, could you also retrieve some rock samples for me from the islands hereabout? I am curious about something. I will be... well, I will be right here. I am still too water-logged to go anywhere.'","Gangur Farwend waits for you to bring him his items on the island where he washed ashore.","You found Gangur's satchel, water-logged but still usable"},
[12458]={"'Ah, you did very well, my friend! I will add the meat you gathered to that which I collected, and when we return the crew will be very pleased.\
\
'How did Legolas fare in his hunt? He kept his attention upon the trees, seeking for birds to bring down with his bow-skill and his fine Elf-arrows. He will be very embarrassed if we bring back more meat than he does! If that is so we can say we all shared equally in the task.\
\
'But you and I will know the truth of it, ${PLAYER}. Ha ha ha!'","'Thank you for these, ${PLAYER}. Our crew will eat well for as long as they must remain here among the Shield Isles, and that eases my mind. I am sure it eases yours as well.\
\
'I should tell you something I observed while I was on the hunt. I felled a number of the birds I saw winging among the trees of Zamarzîr, the southern island... but there was one target that I could not bring myself to down. It was a mighty creature, and though I saw it from a great distance it appeared to me of tremendous size. It brought to my mind the Great Eagles Gwaihir and his brother Landroval.\
\
'I did not release my arrow. Whatever the creature may have been, something told me not to harm it. I do not know if it would give us the same treatment, ${PLAYER}. Walk carefully if you tread again on Zamarzîr, just in case.'","'The crew of the Wave-hunter will have food to eat tonight, thanks to the three of us, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Did Legolas tell you about the great bird he witnessed from afar? I told him it is probably not one of the Great Eagles, because while the flight for one such as Gwaihir or Landroval would not be as long a journey as it was for us, what reason would they have to make it? No, it must be something else. I say he should have filled it with arrows, because anything as large as he describes likely feasts upon anything smaller, and we surely qualify!\
\
'I hope in this case I am wrong, and Legolas will not regret his choice to spare this creature. But if it was up to me I would not have hesitated. The Longbeards have little patience or mercy for monsters, and such a giant bird sounds like a monster to me until it proves it is a friend, as the Eagles have done.\
\
'I say remain wary, ${PLAYER}!'","Collect meat from beasts of the Shield Isles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I have not seen islands like these before, ${PLAYER}... they are very different than the lands with which I am familiar! By Durin's Beard! Am I to believe that the folk who live here are used to the heat and the damp, and would find their lack in the North uncomfortable even as I am accustomed to it? That is a wonder to me.\
\
'Legolas and I departed the wreck of the Wave-hunter not to see the sights, of course, but to hunt for game animals of the Shield Isles. The Elf is still out hunting; he should be back before too long. When we have found enough meat to bring back, we will both return to the ship. Would you like to help us in our hunt? Of course you would!'","Bring the meat you collected to Gimli at the northern tip of Zamarzîr","'Gimli's jesting is at an end, ${PLAYER}, for I did bring a number of birds to earth. Once we find where they fell the dwarf will see that there will be plenty of meat for the crew of the Wave-hunter.\
\
'Can I ask you to retrieve the birds and the arrows with which I felled them? You will find them along the route I took back here, to the south-west. Each bird took but a single arrow, my friend. My aim remains true, even among the trees of these islands and from such distance as necessity required I shoot.\
\
'We will see you back at the Wave-hunter when you have done this.'","Legolas intended to return to the Wave-hunter in the Shield Isles.","'Walk carefully if you tread again on Zamarzîr, just in case. I do not know if that mighty creature is a friend or a foe.'","Gimli and Legolas have begun to gather food to help your crew survive among the Shield Isles, and they could use your help.","Various beasts of the Shield Isles can provide your crew the food necessary to their survival.","Collected meat from beasts of the Shield Isles (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'How did the Elf fare on his own hunt? Did he prove as successful as we did?'","Talk to Legolas at the northern tip of Zamarzîr","Legolas has felled a number of birds throughout Zamarzîr, and asked you to retrieve their meat and his arrows.","Gimli has returned to the Wave-hunter, in the Shield Isles.","'Legolas and I departed the wreck of the Wave-hunter not to see the sights, of course, but to hunt for game animals of the Shield Isles. When we have found enough meat to bring back, we will return to the ship. Would you like to help us in our hunt? Of course you would!'","Retrieve meat and arrows from felled birds throughout Zamarzîr (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bring the birds and arrows to Legolas at Voyage's End","'How fares the hunt?'","'Can I ask you to retrieve the birds and the arrows with which I felled them? You will find them along the route I took back here, to the south-west. Each bird took but a single arrow, my friend. My aim remains true, even among the trees of these islands and from such distance as necessity required I shoot.\
\
'We will see you back at the Wave-hunter when you have done this.'","Gimli is at the northern tip of the island of Zamarzîr.","Legolas is at the northern tip of Zamarzîr.","Talk to Gimli at Voyage's End","Retrieved bird-meat and an Elf-arrow (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Isles: Gimli and Legolas"},
[12459]={"Find Gwallang the Limlinn among the islands west of Voyage's End","The Isles: Gwallang the Limlinn","As you arrive, a huge shadow passes overhead, blanketing the immediate area in darkness. Gwallang jumps up and down with fright. He shakes out his feathers, and while you cannot understand his language the message is clear: the Shield Isles are not a suitable place for him to build a nest.\
\
Gwallang's journey will continue, and perhaps when you leave the Shield Isles the next place he tries will be free of noise, bog-lurkers, and giant birds.","Find Gwallang the Limlinn along the coast of Zamarzîr","Gwallang chirps a welcome at you","Gwallang the Limlinn is among the islands west of Voyage's End.","The ground beneath Gwallang has proved unstable!","The ground beneath Gwallang suddenly shakes!","Gwallang the Limlinn flew to the south-east, and you should look for him along the coast of Zamarzîr.","Talk to Gwallang the Limlinn along the coast of Zamarzîr","Gwallang chirps a welcome at you.","Gwallang the Limlinn is on one of the north-western islands of the Shield Isles.","Meat from the nearby beetles on the western side of the island may help feed Gwallang the Limlinn.","Bring the beetle-meat to Gwallang the Limlinn in the north-western Shield Isles","Gwallang flies away to the south-east","Gwallang the Limlinn flew to the south-east, and you should look for him among the islands to the west of Voyage's End.","Gwallang perches atop a sandy mound, chirping happily at you. He peers around at the surrounding area, taking it all in, apparently deciding if this is a good place to build a nest.","Gwallang pecks at some of the beetle meat, but it is impossible to gauge his reaction. After a few bites, he flutters into the air and peers away southward. Something in that direction seems to bother him.","Gwallang flies away","Gwallang the Limlinn is along the coast of Zamarzîr in the Shield Isles.","Gwallang the Limlinn hops up and down before flying to several nearby trees and testing their branches, scrutinizing the bark and leaves closely with his tiny, sharp eyes. You can't be quite sure, but it feels to you as if he is looking for a suitable place to build a nest!\
\
If so, he'll want easy access to meat. Perhaps the meat of nearby beetles on the western side of the island will suffice. You should bring some to him and see if he likes it.","Gwallang the Limlinn might like meat from the nearby beetles on the western side of the island.","Help Gwallang","Collect meat from the beetles north of Jeb Khâtel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The shoal-tender stands up and Gwallang flies away to the south-east, chirping in protest","Gwallang the Limlinn seems to be searching for a new home among the dangerous Shield Isles.","Gwallang chirps at you.","Talk to Gwallang the Limlinn among the islands west of Voyage's End","Collected beetle-meat (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12460]={"This sailor has been long-dead, revealing the wreck to be many years old","'By our search of these wrecks we know the ship that carried my brother Corudan to Umbar did not suffer the same fate as they. The sailor who wrote this note, Phêlex, may be dead, and his love Khâsha will never know what evil befell him, but my brother lives still. One is beyond our reach, but the other is not.\
\
'I know the Corsairs of Umbar by their evil reputation, and while the Kindred of the Coins may bear a different name and pretend to be something else, the manner of their crimes seems to me the same. Phêlex suffered at the hands of Corsairs; was what happened to my brother at the hands of Nakási Wave-reaper and her Kindred any different?\
\
'We can do nothing for he who wrote this letter, or for Khâsha who waited in vain for his return, but my brother is not yet beyond saving. There is hope our search for him will continue, and end with success. That is hope enough for me, ${PLAYER}.'","Sigileth wants to search the various wrecks that populate Shedax Khîn to ensure none of them carried her brother to his death.","'Search the wrecks in this lagoon for any sign that the ships of Nakási Wave-reaper or her ally Tatháta succumbed to the rocks of Shedax Khîn. I hope and believe they did not... but for Corudan's sake we must be certain.'","'Our ship was more fortunate than some of the vessels torn apart by the Grinding Jaws, ${PLAYER}. See where the hulks lie, their hulls smashed upon the rocks, their masts ripped away? Did the ship which carried my brother toward Umbar fall prey to a similar fate?\
\
'Search the wrecks in this lagoon for any sign that the ships of Nakási Wave-reaper or her ally Tatháta succumbed to the rocks of Shedax Khîn. I hope and believe they did not... but for Corudan's sake we must be certain.'","Search the shipwrecks of Shedax Khîn for some sign of Corudan","'I found a bottle wedged into a crack on the deck of that nearby ship, ${PLAYER}, the cork still held in place. Inside there was a parchment with writing upon it. Read it and tell me what you think.'","'Read the note I gave you and tell me what you think.'","At some point during the long years, this wreck fell onto its side","Talk to Sigileth further south of the wrecks you investigated in Shedax Khîn","Sigileth hands you the note she removed from the sealed bottle","Sigileth asked you to search several of the shipwrecks at Shedax Khîn in search of her brother.","Sigileth handed you a note she found within a bottle discovered on one of the wrecks in Shedax Khîn.","Talk to Sigileth south of the wrecks you investigated in Shedax Khîn","Read the note Sigileth discovered inside a bottle in one of the wrecks of Shedax Khîn","The stern of this wrecked ship has risen from the water here for many years","Sigileth is south of the wrecks you investigated in Shedax Khîn.","Powerful storms embedded the prow of this boat in the sand","Sigileth is further south of the wrecks you investigated in Shedax Khîn.","The Isles: Keen-eyed Sigileth"},
[12461]={"Even islands such as these are home to ancient ruins","Sirgon is located at Voyage's End on the Shield Isles.","'Do not look so crestfallen, my friend! You must see that the Valar smile upon the Wave-hunter, and upon our voyage! We have our lives, after all, and the successful conclusion of your mission still lies ahead! This is not an ending, but a beginning! I have lost friends to the rocks that guard the Shield Isles, it is true... but today the strong hull of the Wave-hunter and the resilience of his crew has delivered us here safely. Rejoice for that, and celebrate the good fortune and the blessing of the Powers that aided in its accomplishment!\
\
'I have not set foot upon this island chain in many years, but it will take me only moments to refamiliarize myself with them. If you will go to several locations and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb>, your report may help me remember the geography of these islands. Perhaps you can start at the beach across the lagoon to the south, a beach to the north-west of the Wave-hunter, and the beach on the western side of this island.'","'What did you see, my friend?'\
\
You tell Sirgon what you saw from each of the locations you scouted, and he nods agreeably.\
\
'Aye, it is coming back to me now. Let us see what I can remember.\
\
'This island chain is a rocky archipelago composed of numerous isles running from north-west to south-east, but three of these are larger than the others. The southernmost island is the largest, Zamarzîr, and it lies in view of the cape upon which Umbar stands. It is a place of jungle and mountain, and when I served the Steward of Gondor in years past it was the haunt of pirates and freebooters. We left it alone as much as we could, for it was a dangerous place.\
\
'The middle island is nearest to us, and it is Bakhjâd. The jagged rocks that surround Bakhjâd are responsible for the reputation of this place as the bane of sailors, for the dangerous currents surrounding the Shield Isles sweep strong ships and braver men to their dooms. I have lost good friends to those rocks, which the men of Umbar call Shedax Khîn. I understand that there may be a settlement somewhere in the centre of Bakhjâd, but I have not seen it.\
\
'The northern island is uninhabited. I believe it is called Jeb Khâtel, but the steep cliffs surrounding it make it inaccessible from the coast.\
\
'This is a place of adventure, ${PLAYER}! If we meet the challenge it sets before us, we are certain to survive and see the successful completion of our mission!'","Find the beach of the island to the north-west of Voyage's End","The sound of Orkish voices drifts from the high cliffs of the island to the west","Sirgon has asked you to <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> over your surroundings at three separate locations: the beach across the lagoon to the south of Sirgon, the beach to the north-west of the Wave-hunter, and the beach on the western side of the island.","Find the beach across the lagoon to the south","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> to the south on the beach across the lagoon from Voyage's End","Sounds of fighting and revelry drift over the trees from the south. A settlement?","Talk to Sirgon at Voyage's End","Sirgon wants to make use of his experience sailing around the Shield Isles to help you learn the geography with which you must now deal.","'I have not set foot upon this island chain in many years, but it will take me only moments to refamiliarize myself with them. If you will go to several locations and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb>, your report may help me remember the geography of these islands. Perhaps you can start at the beach across the lagoon to the south, a beach to the north-west of the Wave-hunter, and the beach on the western side of this island.'","Find the western beach of the island to the north-west of Voyage's End","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> at the beach of the island to the north-west of Voyage's End","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> towards the island to the west","The Isles: Sirgon the Explorer"},
[12463]={"If you are to get an audience with Saklaphêl, you will need to attract the attention of the residents of Mâr Naphra.","Heed these words, and profit by them!\
\
For the CAPTURE or DEATH of each of the following leaders of the so-called \\qKindred of the Coins,\\q the generous Heirs of Castamir offer the following rewards:\
\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Azagath the Sea-shadow</rgb> --- five chests of gold phârzi, and two of silver gîmli\
\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Belondor of the Fleet-fast</rgb> --- one chest of gold phârzi, and one of silver gîmli\
\
<rgb=#FFFF00>Hármelak Golden-hand</rgb> --- her weight in silver gîmli, multiplied by five hundred\
\
Know that the CAPTURE or DEATH of any others who claim to belong to the Kindred of the Coins will be rewarded. Speak with Galadaith within Mâr Naphra for more information.\
\
So it is ordered,\
\
Saklaphêl, Wife of Balakhôr the Scourge and True Ruler of Umbar Baharbêl and the Surrounding Lands","Talk to Galadaith from atop the tall buildings on the western side of Mâr Naphra","Made some noise (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat aggressive residents of Mâr Naphra, and make it noisy (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","A voice calls for you from atop a tall building on the western side of Mâr Naphra","Have you made enough of a commotion in Mâr Naphra?","Nauriel stands outside Mâr Naphra, considering the bounty posted on the Kindred of the Coins by the Heirs of Castamir.","'How did you fare within Mâr Naphra, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You tell Nauriel about your meeting with Galadaith, and what you learned about the bounties issued by Saklaphêl.\
\
'I would be very interested to learn more about these bounty-hunters, for we might make use of them when the time comes to rescue my son from the Kindred of the Coins. Whether they will provide a distraction only, or can be used to remove some of the pieces from the table entirely, remains to be seen. But it appears we have some new friends to make.\
\
'Keep your eyes open, and I will see you back at the Wave-hunter when I am finished scouting around here.'","A man called Galadaith has called for you from atop a tall building on the western side of Mâr Naphra.","'I have not seen you before, stranger. From the commotion downstairs I take it you have a taste for trouble? An expensive taste that could be satisfied with some gold phârzi or silver gîmli? Did you see the bounties posted outside the village? If you have a disregard for danger and some skill in combat, as I deem you do, it may be of some interest to you. What do you call yourself?'\
\
You think it over carefully, and give your answer.\
\
'\\qThe ${CLASS},\\q you say? Well, your name will spread across all of the Zîrar Tarka if you claim one or more of the bounties!'\
\
You ask Galadaith if you could speak with the wealthy patron who ordered the bounty so you may ask her who else has already taken on the task, and he shakes his head.\
\
'The widow Saklaphêl sees no one. You do your business with me, friend. But I can tell you that a number of dangerous sorts have already announced their intentions to claim some or all of the bounties. If you are new to the Isles you may not know them, but their reputations speak for themselves. You would be wise not to delay any longer than you have to, or you will miss your chance. Some of the deadliest bounty-hunters in this part of the world seek Saklaphêl's reward, and most have reasons of their own to hate the Kindred who rule now in Umbar Baharbêl. Good luck to you, ${CLASS}.'","Examine the posted notice outside Mâr Naphra","'It has been said in the Green Hills that the enemy of one's enemy may be a friend, for awhile, and so it seems it is today. The Heirs of Castamir were a dire threat to Gondor, but if the widow of Balakhôr the Scourge intends to reward mercenaries for slaying the serpents who took my son, I cry \\qdo so!\\q and without hesitation!\
\
'The Shield Isles may teem with bounty-hunters now, and their victory may be ours also, for without these leaders the Kindred must fall. Learning the identity of the mercenaries Saklaphêl has hired for this purpose can only be to our benefit.\
\
'Are you prepared to make some noise within Mâr Naphra, ${PLAYER}? If you take on the role of a deadly and dangerous bounty-hunter who fears nothing, I believe the one called Galadaith may invite you to speak with Saklaphêl directly. Go cause some trouble... let us see what happens.'","Talk to Nauriel outside Mâr Naphra","'Are you prepared to make some noise within Mâr Naphra, ${PLAYER}? If you take on the role of a deadly and dangerous bounty-hunter who fears nothing, I believe the one called Galadaith may invite you to speak with Saklaphêl directly. Go cause some trouble... let us see what happens.'","'The name of this settlement is Mâr Naphra, and from the sounds coming from within it is a place where vile sea-brigands gather to fight and drink and gamble. But look at this! It appears it is also a haven for the Heirs of Castamir and those who support them. Just see who has posted a bounty of interest to us outside the village!'","Nauriel has no patience for any delays, and has come to Mâr Naphra in search of information that will help her rescue her son Thorongil from the Kindred of the Coins.","'I could not wait, ${PLAYER}. My son Thorongil is still a captive of the Kindred of the Coins, and I care not the nature of the delay that keeps me from him... I will defy it and see it overcome! Neither storm nor foe will keep me from him.\
\
'I have learned the name of this settlement. It is Mâr Naphra, and from the sounds coming from within it is a place where vile sea-brigands gather to fight and drink and gamble. But look at this! It appears it is also a haven for the Heirs of Castamir and those who support them. Just see who has posted a bounty of interest to us outside the village!'","'A number of dangerous sorts have already announced their intentions to claim some or all of the bounties. If you are new to the Isles you may not know them, but their reputations speak for themselves. You would be wise not to delay any longer than you have to, or you will miss your chance. Some of the deadliest bounty-hunters in this part of the world seek Saklaphêl's reward, and most have reasons of their own to hate the Kindred who rule now in Umbar Baharbêl. Good luck to you, ${CLASS}.'","Wait for someone to notice the ruckus you created","The Isles: The Knight Nauriel","Nauriel stands by a posted notice outside Mâr Naphra.","Nauriel waits for you outside Mâr Naphra.","'Has Galadaith noticed you yet? He surely must have!'"},
[12464]={"Talk to Ingold","The Ithil-stone","'I am convinced. Let us go to Barad-dûr, ${PLAYER}. We shall scout the area together and plan our attack!'","Ingold can be found back at the Ruins of Díngarth.\
\
You should talk to Ingold.","Talk to Hithgol","Hithgol can be found at the Ruins of Díngarth.\
\
You should talk to Hithgol.","You should talk to Ingold.","'I cannot identify the weapon we saw at a distance, but murmurs of excitement have swept through the encampment. Perhaps it is best to speak to Hithgol about it?'","'I have nothing else to say. Although… what have you heard of the Ithil-stone? Nothing?\
\
'Dulgabêth seeks the powerful Ithil-stone to sway others, just as Sauron had done. For that reason alone it means much to Dulgabêth and many others. Ownership of the stone will gain Dulgabêth many allies in Mordor.'","Ingold is concerned that in defeat, Dulgabêth and his followers may direct their wrath upon Gondorians in Mordor.","Talk to Lômazar","'I have heard the rumours, ${PLAYER}. If your eyes have not been cruelly deceived, the missing spear of Aiglos may have been discovered.'","Lômazar is located at the Ruins of Díngarth.\
\
You should speak with Lômazar.","'You have done much to weaken those who serve under The Black Word. If we are to make a stand against those of power in Dor Amarth, now is the time. Speak with Lômazar and see what else he knows. The captive won't say a word to me, but he has taken a liking to you.'"},
[12465]={"Retrieve the urn from the hills of eastern Rath Dúath","Retrieved an urn","Foulness is purged from the vessel as you pour the water into it","Talk to Rauniel by the bridge to Eithel Gwaur","'You are the first I have met who wishes to seek a cure for my river. Yes, I am the keeper of these waters, or once I was. That was long ago, when it was known as the Ithilduin. Now I am but a prisoner of the Witch-king, and endless tears of agony befoul the waters I love. It is not physically that I stand before you; my appearance here is only a creation of your mind. This projection of my thought has stolen the full extent of my power. Can you assist my escape from the watery prison of Eithel Gwaur?\
\
'First you must collect the urns of pure water that remain hidden in Rath Dúath. They will break the wards that prohibit my escape. They are located at one end of the bridge to Eithel Gwaur. Please hurry.'","'You have done as I asked; I can sense it. Still, there is more to be done if I am to be free and restore the river to its former glory.'","The Ithilduin","The urns Rauniel seeks can be found in the hills of eastern Rath Dúath and from outside the barrows of Gorthad Nûr.\
\
You should retrieve the urns for Rauniel.","Rauniel can be found by the bridge to Eithel Gwaur in Rath Dúath.\
\
You should talk to Rauniel.","Complete: Dwelling in the Hills","A strange woman seeks to help you cure that which plagues the Morgulduin River.","Pour water into a vessel upon the bridge to Eithel Gwaur","Retrieve the urn from outside the barrows of Gorthad Nûr","Vessels for the water of the urns can be found upon the bridge to Eithel Gwaur in Rath Dúath.\
\
You should pour water into the vessels for Rauniel."},
[12466]={"El carcelero","Ned Pruner está en la cárcel, al norte y al este de la puerta de la ciudad.\
\
El condestable Cardoso sugirió que podrías ayudar a Ned Pruner a descubrir lo que Calder Cob contó a los bandidos Montebruno.","'Ned es un buen hombre con un trabajo difícil. Tras descubrir la traición de Calder Cob, le han encargado averiguar qué secretos Cob, uno de sus amigos, reveló a los Montebruno.\
\
Si tienes la oportunidad de visitarlo, podrías ayudarle. Calder Cob ha hablado poco o nada desde que fue encarcelado.\
\
Puedes encontrar a Ned en la cárcel. Es difícil no verla... probablemente escucharás a Otto quejándose en el cepo fuera de la puerta antes de llegar. Ve al norte y al este bajo el arco y atraviesa las puertas de hierro. Reconocerás la cárcel por los cepos -- y Otto en ellos -- en el porche.'","Ned Pruner es el carcelero de Archet. Es un buen hombre encargado de descubrir los secretos que Calder Cob entregó a los bandidos Montebruno.","Debe completarse antes de la \"Introducción.\"","'El viejo Cardoso me conoce demasiado bien. Calder era como un héroe para mucha gente de aquí, y para mí también. Todavía estoy sorprendido por todo esto y me cuesta mucho hacerle hablar.'","'Ned probablemente necesitará ayuda para hacer hablar a Cob. Si puedes dedicarle unos minutos, podrías echarle una mano.\
\
Lo encontrarás en la cárcel.'"},
[12467]={"You should look for sign of the missing refugees, south from Dale's eastern gates, and defeat any Jangovar that may have been involved in their disappearance.","'Hush! Come close and listen. It was Akshir we followed. It was Akshir who told us lies we wished to hear, or that we feared. You may guess well enough the lies: that we could win riches, that the Dale-folk planned to slaughter us, that he would lead us home.\
\
'He bade us sneak out of Dale and then led us here, to Tay Yoldash. I would be among them now, had I not chanced to hear him speaking with a Jangovar lackey, when they thought themselves alone. Lies. All lies, and I believed!\
\
'The others though - they are not safe. You must go in and rescue them.'","The Jangovar Threat","'How glad I am you found us, ${PLAYER}! I tremble to think what Akshir would have done with them, had you not.'","Tay Yoldash can be found south-east of the city of Dale in the Dale-lands.\
\
You should defeat Jangovar and free refugees from Tay Yoldash.","There are rumours that the new Easterling refugees may be joining, or perhaps being kidnapped, by the remaining Jangovar.","'The Jangovar... what is to be done with them? We do not know why some remained after their defeat or how to be rid of them. They are a thorn in our side, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
You take the opportunity to tell the Queen Regent about the suspicious dealings you uncovered in Lake-town and Esgaroth. A frown creases Erna's face.\
\
'Then perhaps the whispers which I had taken for idle rumours contain some truth, after all. More than one report has come to me of the new refugees joining the Jangovar, or being allied with them all along, and so on and so forth. Until now, I took it for the wounded and suspicious regard of my own people, who have been through much.\
\
'But now I see it may have been a mix of truth and lies from without, after just the manner you describe finding in Lake-town. Would you return to the Easterling refugees, ${PLAYER}, and see if you can solve this riddle, as well?'","Talk to refugees in Dale (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Defeat Jangovar at Tay Yoldash (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You should talk to Easterling refugees in Dale and learn the truth of the rumours.","You should return to Orphón with news of your success, just outside Tay Yoldash.","'Jangovar? I don't know that Jangovar would dare come so near to Dale. And yet... there was a strange man going here and there among my people yesterday and whispering among them.'","Search for the missing refugees","Defeat Jangovar in the Dale-lands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Ah, it is you, ${CLASS}. Perhaps you can help. Perhaps you will believe me. My friend has gone. He and others, they left through the eastern gate, and have not returned! I cannot think why. Perhaps I am worrying for no reason. But my heart tells me something has gone amiss.'","Freed refugees (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Free refugees in Tay Yoldash (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to Orphón","Defeated Jangovar (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talked to refugees (${CURRENT}/${MAX})"},
[12468]={"'¿Menikko te ha enviado para que hable contigo sobre nuestro tesoro perdido? Sé bien de qué hablas, pero baja la voz, no sea que alguien nos oiga. Se refiere al Jä‑koru, la Joya de Hielo, el tesoro más antiguo de nuestro pueblo, venerado durante mucho tiempo en historias y canciones, y perdido desde hace incontables años. El Jä‑koru es un gran fragmento de hielo, pero jamás se derrite ni puede ser quebrado por martillo o cincel. Cuando los rayos del sol lo alcanzan, devuelve la luz multiplicada en un impresionante abanico de colores resplandecientes.\
\
'No es una reliquia de los Hombres. Nuestros relatos más antiguos afirman que fue entregado a nuestro pueblo por un gran espíritu del mar helado, para llevar luz y belleza a nuestros corazones durante los inviernos más fríos. Los Hylje‑heimo perdieron el Jä‑koru cuando sus Ancianos viajaban desde el sur. Su vergüenza fue tan grande que jamás hablaron de cómo se produjo la pérdida.\
\
'Sea cual fuere la causa de su pérdida, ahora podría hallarse en manos de los Angmarim. Los míos dicen que estos han prometido devolverlo al Anciano de los Hylje‑heimo, siempre que se asegure de que el Consejo de Ancianos no establezca acuerdos ni alianzas con los Hombres del Sur. Cualquier necio puede ver que los días de libertad de nuestro pueblo están contados si las tierras del sur caen bajo el yugo de Angmar; y aun así, el atractivo del Jä‑koru es tan grande que el Anciano de los Hylje‑heimo habla con insensatez en el consejo. Así pues, ${PLAYER}, por el bien de ambos pueblos, considero prudente que intentemos recuperar el Jä‑koru antes de que sea demasiado tarde.'","La Joya de Hielo","Menikko te ha hablado de un tesoro lossoth perdido que ha vuelto ahora a la luz.","Habla con Esko en Pynti-peldot","Esko se encuentra en Pynti-peldot, justo al sur de la gran bahía.\
\
Menikko te ha pedido que hables con un hombre llamado Esko para conocer la historia del tesoro lossoth perdido.","'¿Puedo robarte un momento de atención, ${PLAYER}? Hay un asunto que deseo tratar contigo, uno que requiere cierta discreción. A nuestros ojos eres Sivullinen, un Forastero, y en esta cuestión no puedo confiar en alguien de mi propio pueblo. Se trata de un tema profundamente arraigado en nuestra historia y que causaría un gran trastorno si llegara a ser de conocimiento general.\
\
'Una de las tribus ancestrales de los Lossoth custodió antaño un tesoro antiguo, un símbolo del orgullo y la vitalidad de nuestro pueblo en esta dura tierra que se les había confiado. Con el tiempo se perdió, y esa pérdida fue motivo de gran vergüenza para dicha tribu, y en verdad para todos los Lossoth. Ahora parece que este tesoro podría estar por fin de nuevo a nuestro alcance, pero debemos actuar con rapidez antes de que se pierda nuestra oportunidad.\
\
'Si deseas ayudarme, dirígete al sur y habla con Esko en Pynti-peldot. Él conoce las viejas historias mejor que nadie, y fue quien supo del resurgir de este gran tesoro. Podrá ponerte en el camino correcto, si te das prisa.'"},
[12469]={"Defeated Orcs and Wargs in the Floodfells (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I have been reading what I have written down thus far, ${PLAYER}. Our expedition to Avabárg has shed new light on the past of my people. The Ai-thúda's urgency to find a better home is quite interesting. I myself have never dreamt of any home but Rohan.\
\
'Now where shall the past take us in the Floodfells? As we know, Frumgar was weary of life in the Vales and so he led the Ai-thúda north, bloodying their spears on Orc and Warg as they rode. Perhaps we could offer assistance to the Beornings in the Floodfells by defeating some of the enemies that threaten them? It would also allow us to better understand the hardships endured by the Ai-thúda as they travelled north.\
\
'When the path is clear and safe, let us convene at the White Mare. It is all that remains of the Ai-thúda's short stay in the Floodfells.'","Léothred has asked you to defeat Orcs and Wargs in the Floodfells.\
\
You should defeat Orcs and Wargs in the Floodfells.","The shape of the White Mare is unmistakable, a wonder of the craft","Léothred, the Rohirric scholar, seeks to follow the northern migration of his ancestors as they passed through the Floodfells.","Léothred can be found at the White Mare.\
\
You should talk to Léothred.","Visit the White Mare in the Floodfells","Defeat Orcs and Wargs in the Floodfells (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The White Mare can be found in the Floodfells.\
\
You should visit the White Mare.","Talk to Léothred at the White Mare","'The White Mare! We could see it in the distance at Limlók, but now that we stand upon it, I am in awe! Behold the white stones, for they depict the shape of the horses the Ai-thúda cherished. \
\
'What prompted this, I wonder? Could it be a symbol of strength, or a mark of territory? Did it raise the Ai-thúda's spirits and frighten their enemies? I will continue to study the White Mare a little while longer.'","The Journey Through the Floodfells"},
[12471]={"'I must brace myself for the displeasure of my people....'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is a solo instance, and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>","Agelwyn is in the ravine north of Marton.\
\
You should speak with Agelwyn.","Gamling is at Helm's Dike in the south-western Westfold.\
\
You should speak with Gamling.","'I will gather my people now. Come, ${PLAYER}! I would have you at my side for this.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is a solo instance, and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>","'It was good of you to rally those people, ${PLAYER}! I believe the women will be safe in the Glittering Caves, and the men will be put to good use upon the battlements.\
\
'The lady hopes to see you within, but she said to bid you farewell if you insisted upon going back out into the fray.'","Speak with Gamling","Help Agelwyn and her people reach Helm's Deep","It is time to make for Helm's Deep with Agelwyn and the refugees. You have chosen the safest path, but it will still be dangerous, for the Westfold is overrun.","El viaje hacia el Abismo de Helm"},
[12473]={"'Garthamendir caerá hoy, lo siento en el viento. Dirígete a las puertas de Carn Dûm, en el rincón noroeste de Himbar.'","El Guardián Garthamendir","Tu constante hostigamiento a los Angmarim no ha pasado desapercibido. Los Montaraces desean llevar la lucha hasta las puertas mismas de Carn Dûm y derrotar al líder de los Angmarim en Himbar.","'Sé cómo arrebatar el fuego a los Angmarim. Pero debo advertirte que no es una hazaña menor. No puedo prometerte que regresarás de esta batalla.\
\
'Hay una criatura que comanda a los Angmarim. El espectro Garthamendir, un Cargûl que guarda la puerta de Carn Dûm. Es aquello que impulsa a los Angmarim a la batalla, lo que temen más que tu acero o las flechas de mis Montaraces.\
\
'Encuentra al Cargûl en las puertas de Carn Dûm, al oeste. Descansa primero y reúne tus fuerzas. Las necesitarás todas si deseas triunfar. ¡Y no vayas solo!'","Garthamendir guarda las puertas de Carn Dûm, al oeste.\
\
Areneth te advirtió sobre el Cargûl y su terrible furia. Pero matar a esa criatura vil es la única forma de quebrar las fuerzas de los Angmarim. Te advirtió que no lo enfrentes ${PLAYERNAME:solo[m]|sola[f]}.","'Tu valor inspira a mis hombres, ${PLAYER}. Con el espectro derrotado, los Angmarim se dispersan en busca de un nuevo líder. Los atacaremos mientras estén en su punto más débil.'","Areneth está en Gath Forthnír, al este de Carn Dûm.\
\
Garthamendir fue derrotado y sus fuerzas, destruidas. Deberías regresar con Areneth para darle la noticia."},
[12474]={"Observa la carrera y anima al participante que elegiste.","La carrera de salto de barriles","Espera a que empiece la carrera","Mira la carrera para ver si tu participante gana","Has abandonado la zona de la carrera","'¿Has venido por el festival? Pues como ya sabrás, nuestro evento principal es la Carrera de saltos de barril.\
\
'Esta competición enfrentará a cuatro borrachos empedernidos… es decir, a nobles y respetables enanos, en una lucha hasta el final.\
\
'¡La línea de meta, claro! No dejamos a esos compañeros acercarse a hachas ni a otros objetos afilados hasta que se les pase la borrachera. ¡Elige a un participante prometedor y veamos si tienes ojo para acertar con el ganador!'","Habla con Arnar para elegir a un participante de la carrera","No abandones la zona de la carrera","¡La carrera de salto de barriles está en pleno apogeo! Arnar está recibiendo apuestas por cuál de los enanos tiene más posibilidades de ganar.","Habla con Arnar y elige a tu participante favorito para la próxima carrera."},
[12475]={"Derrota a Muelespinillas","Muelespinillas derrotado","Ost Elendil, el gran palacio de los reyes de antaño, está en la isla más allá del puente de Ariant. En su base está la entrada a Haudh Valandil, la tumba de Valandil, hijo de Isildur. Temo que la tumba, tras largo tiempo sin profanar, se haya convertido en el hogar de grandes males: tanto de Angmar como de otros orígenes.\
\
¿Has visto a las malvadas criaturas conocidas como Kergrim? Se cree que tienen relación con los rascacuevas, pero son más proclives a enfermedades y a desecrear lugares sagrados.\
\
Algunas de estas bestias han entrado en Haudh Valandil y deben ser eliminadas de la tumba, especialmente su brutal líder: Muelespinillas es el nombre de esta malvada criatura. Llevarás a cabo esta tarea, ${PLAYER}, si honras los antiguos lugares de los Dúnedain, y volverás a mí con noticias de tu éxito. Si se me ha reclamado en otra parte, informa al capitán general Daerdan en Echad Garthadir, el campamento de los montaraces aquí en la ciudad.","Los Kergrim acechan en Haudh Valandil, la tumba en la isla más allá del puente de Ariant, en Annúminas.\
\
Glangilith te ha pedido que derrotes a los kergrim que acechan en las profundidades de Haudh Valandil, incluyendo a su líder, Muelespinillas.","Los kergrim acechan en Haudh Valandil","Derrota a los kergrim en Haudh Valandil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Kergrim derrotados en Haudh Valandil (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12476]={"You found a dwarf in Othrikar who knows about the Secret Stone, but he cannot help you unless you know whom to ask for.\
\
You should discover whom to ask for in Othrikar.","Rúnvarth is an ancient dwarf, but you have the feeling that great wisdom has come with his age. He silently assesses you for a moment, and then speaks:\
\
'I am Rúnvarth, and I have what you seek, but it is impossible to simply hand it to you. Three items you must bring me, and only then can your quest continue.'","Talk to King Thorin III","'Can I help you, ${CLASS}? You seem to be looking for something.'\
\
You tell him you are looking for the Secret Stone. He bristles at the mention of the name.\
\
'How do you know about that?! Keep your voice down!'\
\
You tell him that King Thorin has tasked you with finding it.\
\
'I see! You are on the right track, but I'm afraid I can't help you... unless you know whom to ask for.'","You return to King Thorin and tell him of your adventure.\
\
'So, someone did indeed have sinister intentions for the Secret Stone! I cannot thank you enough for keeping it out of evil's hands and undoing this insidious plot! For now, we will see if we can use its power for the benefit of my people. If not, I will make sure it is sealed away for good.\
\
'On behalf of Durin's Folk, thank you, ${PLAYER}.'","Collect the items for Rúnvarth","Now that you have the key, you must find the keyhole.\
\
You should find the keyhole.","You have discovered the name of the dwarf in Othrikar.\
\
You should ask for Rúnvarth.","An old piece of parchment was left behind here. It appears to have been written very quickly:\
'Forced to flee. Seek me in Othrikar.'","You found a note in Moria pointing you towards Othrikar.\
\
You should find someone who knows something about the Secret Stone in Othrikar.","Find someone in Othrikar who knows about the Secret Stone","The Key and the Keyhole","Talk to Rúnvarth","Talk to Lúki","Rúnvarth has told you that he needs three items from you.\
\
You should discover what these items are.","Discover whom to ask for in Othrikar.","Find the keyhole","You need to ask for Rúnvarth!","You ask Lúki to see Rúnvarth. He nods solemnly.\
\
'As you wish!'","You have found the Secret Stone inside Erebor!\
\
You should claim the Secret Stone!","King Thorin III has asked you to try to locate an ancient relic known as the Secret Stone. But what dangers did the poem warn about? Can you solve this mystery on your own?\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This difficult treasure hunt will require community teamwork and resources outside of the game itself. Good luck! </rgb>","You hear someone enter the chamber behind you","Claim the Secret Stone!","Rúnvarth can be found in Othrikar.\
\
You should talk to Rúnvarth.","'Yes, this is what is needed, just a moment.'\
\
He goes inside the house. You hear forge bellows and hammering. The noise ceases, and he returns.\
\
'Here is your newly forged key.'\
\
He notices your confused expression and chuckles.\
\
'Ah, that piece of metal from Old Gnawer? That was the previous key. I needed to make you a new one. That is why I told you it was impossible to simply hand it to you! Now, you must find the keyhole to claim your prize. And to find that, you must return to where you started. Good luck, and remember, don't stare into the stone, or it will steal your mind!'\
\
And with that, he returns to his home, and shuts the door behind him.","King Thorin III can be found in Erebor.\
\
You should bring the Secret Stone to King Thorin.","He quickly goes inside and then returns, followed by another dwarf."},
[12477]={"Attempted to free many prisoners in Naerband.","Naerband is located in Talath Úrui.\
\
You should collect keys from jailers in Naerband.","After opening numerous prison doors to free prisoners in Naerband, you realize that Thraknûl is not just capturing Nurnhoth, but also many of the Orcs and Uruks formerly under the command of Sauron. Either Thraknûl is vying for power or he has gone mad.","Naerband is located in Talath Úrui.\
\
You should free prisoners in Naerband.","The prison fortress of Naerband is populated by vile acts and jailed denizens.","The Key to Chaos","Open prison doors (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Many prisoner voices wail through the walls of Naerband. Perhaps if you could find some jailer keys, you might be able to let loose some of the denizens of Naerband.","Opened prison doors (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect keys from jailers in Naerband","Completado","Collected keys (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect keys from jailers in Naerband (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12479]={"Thórth se encuentra en Zigilgund.\
\
Deberías regresar junto a Thórth con noticias de tu victoria.","'Los ataques de esos barbas-ralas no son poca cosa, ${PLAYER}. Están organizados: deben de tener suministros, un plan y un líder para haber llegado tan al norte.\
\
'He encontrado algunos mapas antiguos de las Minas de Arrancahielo, y uno de ellos muestra una sala interna. Si fuera aficionado a las apuestas, diría que esos Duramanos planean apoderarse de las minas y que su líder pretende reclamar esa zona como propia.\
\
'Necesitarás encontrar una llave. ¿Quizá alguno de los otros Duramanos tenga una?'","'No podrás entrar en ninguna sala cerrada sin una llave. Te sugiero que vayas a buscarla.'","Thórth sospecha que quienquiera que lidere a los Duramanos en las Minas de Arrancahielo se esconde en una zona cerrada con llave dentro de las minas.","Consigue una llave de un Duramano en las antiguas Minas de Arrancahielo","Lleva la llave a Thórth","La clave de su codicia","Has encontrado una llave torcida","Las Minas de Arrancahielo se encuentran al suroeste de Zigilgund.\
\
Thórth te ha pedido que expulses a los Duramanos de las Minas de Arrancahielo.","Consigue una llave de un Duramano en las Minas de Arrancahielo","'¡Excelente trabajo! Veamos qué tal está....\
\
'¡Maldita sea, la llave está doblada! Bueno, no pasa nada... creo que puedo arreglarla.\
\
'Espera un momento....'","'Necesitarás encontrar la llave del lugar cerrado en las minas, ${PLAYER}. Supongo que alguno de los Duramanos podría tenerla....'"},
[12480]={"'¡Saludos, ${PLAYER}! ¿Has venido a responder a la llamada de los Kharum-ubnâr? Si deseas ayudarlos, ¡mis cabras te llevarán a la Montaña Solitaria de inmediato!'","Habla con Vorthur Alientohumo en Akrâz-zahar","(Opcional) Preséntate ante un reclutador de miniaventuras","'¡Te doy la bienvenida! Me alegra que los Kharum-ubnâr puedan contar con la ayuda de valientes como tú.\
\
'Se acerca el momento de reconquistar el Monte Gundabad, y para que el príncipe Durin triunfe, debemos reforzar a su ejército en sus preparativos y asegurarnos de que nuestros hermanos de las Moradas de los Enanos más lejanos no hayan sido olvidados, en especial aquellos que se quedaron en Angmar y en las Montañas Nubladas.\
\
'En resumen, el rey Thorin nos ha confiado la tarea de ayudar a nuestros hermanos en tierras lejanas y a los valientes enanos de la Gabil'akkâ. ¡Yo dirigiré tus esfuerzos allí donde más se necesiten!'","Has llegado a Akrâz-zahar","A instancias del rey Thorin Yelmo de Piedra, los enanos de los Kharum-ubnâr buscan la ayuda de aventureros expertos para asegurar las Moradas de los Enanos más lejanos y preparar al príncipe Durin y a la Gabil'akkâ para la victoria en la inminente reconquista del Monte Gundabad.\
\
Si deseas ayudar a los Kharum-ubnâr, deberías presentarte ante uno de los reclutadores de miniaventuras repartidos por toda la Tierra Media. Te llevarán a Akrâz-zahar, la sala de los Kharum-ubnâr en Erebor, la Montaña Solitaria. Puedes encontrar reclutadores de miniaventuras en la Puerta de Thorin, Gondamon, la ciudad de Bree, la Sala Veintiuno, Othrikar, Gabilshathûr, el Campamento de Glóin, Hrimbarg, Galtrev, el Mirador de la Gran Excavación, Magh Ashtu, Járnfast, Erebor y Minas Tirith (solsticio de verano).","A instancias del rey Thorin Yelmo de Piedra, los Kharum-ubnâr han reclutado la ayuda de aventureros expertos para asegurar las Moradas de los Enanos más lejanos y garantizar el éxito del príncipe Durin y la Gabil'akkâ en la inminente reconquista del Monte Gundabad.","Debes presentarte en Akrâz-zahar, en Erebor. Los reclutadores de miniaventuras están a tu disposición para llevarte allí a toda prisa.\
\
Puedes encontrar reclutadores de miniaventuras en la Puerta de Thorin, Gondamon, la ciudad de Bree, la Sala Veintiuno, Othrikar, Gabilshathûr, el Campamento de Glóin, Hrimbarg, Galtrev, el Mirador de la Gran Excavación, Magh Ashtu, Járnfast, Erebor y Minas Tirith (solsticio de verano).","Puedes encontrar a Vorthur Alientohumo en Akrâz-zahar, en Erebor.\
\
A instancias del rey Thorin Yelmo de Piedra, los Kharum-ubnâr han reclutado la ayuda de aventureros expertos para asegurar las Moradas de los Enanos más lejanos y garantizar el éxito del príncipe Durin y la Gabil'akkâ en la inminente reconquista del Monte Gundabad.","Viaja a Akrâz-zahar en Erebor","¡Los Kharum-ubnâr te necesitan!"},
[12482]={"'Orcs? This is far worse than I thought, ${PLAYER}. \
\
'We will soon find ourselves surrounded by the very worst of our enemies. We need to take action quickly if Garsfeld is to survive!'","The Killing Crofts","This cow was slain viciously by an armed attacker...suddenly an Orc strikes","Scout the croft to the east of Garsfeld","Scout the croft to the south-west of Garsfeld","Scout the croft to the south of Garsfeld","There is widespread devastation on this croft; the crops are completely torn apart","Talk to Gísling","This croft has suffered massive damage; nothing remains to save","'You have done much good for Garsfeld, but my curiosity grows as to how much of our once fertile land remains untouched.\
\
'Outside the town, the half-orcs and crebain destroy everything we hold dear.\
\
'If you would, investigate the fields around Garsfeld and see if there are any signs of life, be it crops or any stragglers who did not heed my father's call to seek shelter within the town.'","Gísling is in the Mead Hall of Garsfeld.\
\
You should return to Gísling with news of your discoveries.","Gísling is uncertain how widespread the devastation of the local crofts has become. He requests that you search the crofts for any signs of life.","The crofts can be found to the east, south, and south-west of Garsfeld.\
\
Gísling wishes for you to scout the three largest crofts around Garsfeld to discover how much damage has been dealt to this season's crops."},
[12483]={"Fólnith the Pale smells fresh meat and begins to descend!","This goat meat may serve as a suitable lure for the hunting drake","Talk to Molkha in the valley","'Those two massive drakes I saw speaking with the Angmarim are apparently a breeding pair, lord and lady of the cliff-nest Flogalith. Do you know what Hórin has also told me they are?\
\
'They are the siblings of Vethúg Wintermind, children of Hrímil Frost-heart herself! Hórin says it's his personal mission to burn every branch of that cursed family tree, and I say we help him do it!\
\
'I do not think you can slay them alone, ${PLAYER}, despite your considerable skill, but if you do manage to destroy them I know you will receive a handsome reward.'","Defeat Grimdóth the Bitter","The two elder drakes have been slain! You should report your success to Molkha.\
\
Molkha can be found on the frozen lake south-west of Fellgát.","'You have done the deed? It is good to know there are two fewer of Hrímil's vile children in the world, for the evil in their hearts posed a great danger to all those who do not claim such parentage as theirs. I trust you will know what to do should you encounter any more of her foul brood!'","The Kin of Winter","Place a fresh ram to lure Fólnith the Pale from the sky and defeat him","Two siblings of Vethúg Wintermind have been found living in the Welkin-lofts, and the dwarves have placed a bounty on their heads for the protection of the Gabil'akkâ.","Defeated Fólnith the Pale","Defeated Grimdóth the Bitter","Molkha has asked you to slay Fólnith the Pale and Grimdóth the Bitter, siblings of Vethúg Wintermind.\
\
One can be found at the top of Flogalith, the other flies over the frozen lake and will need to be lured from the sky."},
[12485]={"'Have you done it then? Ah yes, I can see from here our king's banners flying true once more. I know there are more yet to replace, but these old hands can only work so fast. You have my thanks!'","Return to Langwen","Langwen has asked you to replace shredded banners atop the towers of Rammas Echor in the Harlond. You should pick up the nearby bag full of banners.\
\
The bag is next to Langwen, in the Harlond.","Talk to Langwen","Replace tattered banners (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Atop the towers of the great wall, Rammas Echor, fly the black banners of King Elessar. Time, weather, and war have ripped and shredded their once proud edges.","Pick up the bag full of banners","You have taken down the tattered banners and replaced them with proud black flags bearing the white tree of Gondor. You should let Langwen know that her new banners fly from the towers' heights.\
\
Langwen is in the Harlond.","'Well, it's about time Othanar sent someone to help me. I am indeed Langwen, weaver and seamstress.\
\
'At the moment, I am working to replace the banners which are atop the wall. Time, wind, and war have shredded their edges, and I am wont to replace them with fresh versions. The towers of Rammas Echor are reached by long flights of stairs, however, and though my fingers are yet nimble, the same cannot be said for my knees. Will you take up these new banners and replace any you find which might be ruined?'","Tattered banners replaced (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Othanar has asked you to speak with Langwen, who has been asking for assistance.\
\
Langwen can be found by a fountain in one of the gardens in the Harlond.","The King's Banners","Langwen has asked you to replace shredded banners atop the towers of Rammas Echor in the Harlond.","'Welcome to the Harlond! Word travelled ahead that you might be coming to lend a hand. As you can see, the city is working to pick itself up after being nearly razed to the ground by the Morgul-host. I would ask that you speak with Langwen, as she has asked me twice today already to send help her way.'"},
[12486]={"'Welcome, ${PLAYER}. Your honoured name reached us from our groves to the North. Your coming renews our hope that virtue yet walks among us.\
\
'Our stores are thin, as in the North, and what we can grant in exchange for aid is little beside its worth. Yet we will deal in good faith.\
\
'As the blight spreads, still there remain unspoiled roots and seeds in Adagím. We ask this: gather what is pure. Take the seedlings untouched by corruption; bring us the seeds that hold the memory of the Emerald Wood.\
\
'Here, beneath the boughs of Sul Madásh, hope clings still. With your help, the forest may yet be reborn.'","Quartermaster Aralath informed you of how you can assist the Kintai and bid you return to Dithúrim for final instruction and a gift.","You have spoken to Quartermaster Aralath","'If you should find the unsullied seeds of Nisigím, gather them with care. In them lies the memory of what once was and the hope, faint though it be, of what might yet return.\
\
'We offer you tools to claim and harvest, or the means to make them. Choose as you will, and know this: even before your hand turns to aid us, we are already in your debt.'","Speak with Dithúrim in Sul Madásh","The Kintai of Sul Madásh","Welcomed by the Kintai of Sul Madásh, your reputation with an alliance in the North endears you to the Elves, and they look to you for assistance in preserving what remains of the Emerald Wood.","Speak with Quartermaster Aralath in Sul Madásh","'Well met, ${PLAYER}. Word of your valour in the North has reached us, and you are welcome as a friend of the Kintai.\
\
'In the West, the once-hallowed forest Nisigím lies stricken. Now it is named Adagím, for it is shadowed by blight, and foulness spreads where once light dwelt. Trees and beasts alike wither, and though some persist, most fall silent as the Mother Trees perish. Only Sul Madásh endures, untouched.\
\
'Seek Quartermaster Aralath. They will tell you what aid we can spare—and what we ask in turn.'","After speaking with Dithúrim, she directed you to speak with Quartermaster Aralath. He will provide further information in how we can assist the Kintai in Adagím."},
[12487]={"El secreto del cuchillo","Derrota a los Tarsâri en el Cuerno de la Hoja (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","¡Has atraído la atención de un Encargado!","Busca el volumen perdido de 'Crónicas de los Tarsâri'.","Recupera las Crónicas de los Tarsâri, Vol. II","Recupera las Crónicas de los Tarsâri, Vol. IV","Este libro relata la llegada de los Tarsâri a Kighân, hace varios siglos","Todavía se sabe poco sobre los Tarsâri, aquellos que se hacen llamar los Encargados. Investiga el Cuerno de la Hoja en busca de nuevas pistas sobre su historia y alcance.","'Estos libros deben contener un conocimiento inimaginable para que los Tarsâri los hayan protegido con sus vidas. Deberíamos irnos ahora, antes de que más de los Encargados se den cuenta de nuestra presencia.'","Derrota al Encargado Velado","Derrota al Encargado Velado en el Cuerno de la Hoja.","Este libro explica los procedimientos y el reclutamiento de los nuevos discípulos de los Tarsâri","Tarsâri derrotados en el Cuerno de la Hoja (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recupera las Crónicas de los Tarsâri, Vol. I","Recupera textos históricos sobre los Tarsâri en Bâdrasag, el Cuerno de la Hoja.","Este libro detalla la línea de sucesión de los Tarsâri, que se detiene hace apenas cincuenta años","Busca el volumen perdido de 'Crónicas de los Tarsâri'"},
[12488]={"You have entered the Court of Celeborn and should now speak to Lady Galadriel!","'Do you wish to know what I have seen?\
\
'I commanded the Mirror to reveal the pits of Dol Dhannen, and I beheld only ruin. It showed beasts scavenging in the wreckage of the Tower and Orcs lost in darkness, but I saw naught of the one named Karazgar.\
\
'You have come seeking my counsel, but I do not give counsel. The Mirror has shown me what I commanded, but have I seen things as they truly are? One of the Uttermost West would not grant such a vision without cause, and you have travelled far in search of this Man.\
\
'You will not go to Dol Dhannen alone, ${PLAYER}. We shall return to that place together.'\
\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Next week: 'Whispers in the Pits'</rgb>","Lady Galadriel stands beside the Mirror...","The Court of Celeborn can be found within Caras Galadhon.\
\
King Thranduil has asked you to seek the counsel of Lady Galadriel in Caras Galadhon.\
\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: If you have not previously entered Caras Galadhon, you may use a rope near the entrance to enter the city. If you have not begun the Court of Lothlórien allegiance, you may speak to one of the Galadhrim beneath the great mallorn in the centre of Caras Galadhon to enter the Court of Celeborn.</rgb>","'Ah! It is good that you have come, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'It is a difficult matter to trust in the truth of such strange visions, and though I do not doubt your character or resolve, I fear that we have been misled. Vethúg has not flown from the Grey Mountains, Karazgar is wounded and lost, and it seems we have needlessly readied ourselves for a battle that will not come. We should enjoy such a peace while we can, and instead, thoughts of terror cloud the minds of many in the North.\
\
'The Green Lady you spoke of... the Elvenking once knew her, did he not? Has she been a friend to the Elves? Are her words true, or are they mere riddles?\
\
'I ask that you seek an audience with King Thranduil and hear his counsel. If there is no longer any need to fear, I would not have our peoples live as if the War were not ended.'","'Hail, ${PLAYER}. What tidings bring you from Erebor?'\
\
You tell King Thranduil that Vethúg Wintermind has not come to Erebor and King Thorin III has begun to question the visions granted to you by the Green Lady.\
\
'Tárasánë is of the Uttermost West, but neither her designs nor those of her lord are known to me. I can offer no counsel on such matters, but I know one who may.\
\
'The Lady Galadriel of Lórien possesses a sight beyond all others, and she would know well if such a foe came unbidden to the old fortress of the Enemy.\
\
'Go to her Court among the highest flets of Caras Galadhon. She will have the answers you seek -- be they good or ill.'","Concerned that none of the visions granted to you by the Green Lady have come to pass, King Thorin III has asked you to seek the guidance of King Thranduil.","Talk to King Thranduil","Lady Galadriel is standing in her garden.\
\
You have arrived at Galadriel's Garden and should now speak to Lady Galadriel and learn what she has seen.","'Hail, ${PLAYER}. I had heard you travelled far to the North into the lands of the Bardings and Durin's Folk. Was that not so?'\
\
You tell Lady Galadriel that you adventured among the strongholds of the North, but in your search for the Weeping Warrior, your path became unclear. You encountered a powerful being of the Uttermost West known as the Green Lady, and she granted you three visions, one of which suggested that the Weeping Warrior had returned to Dol Guldur.\
\
'We will speak of the tale you told me, ${PLAYER}, but first I must offer you this new knowledge. Dol Guldur is no longer named as such among my people. It is now named Dol Dhannen, or the Hill of Ruin in the Common Speech. The Elves of Lórien have kept watch on the ruins of the tower, but its pits are laid bare and no evil that passes beneath the trees is hidden to us. I do not doubt your words, but it would be nigh impossible for one of the Gúrzyul to pass unnoticed into Dol Dhannen.\
\
'Yet, you speak of one of the Uttermost West who bid you return to Dol Dhannen. This I cannot so idly overlook.\
\
'Let us descend to my garden, and there I shall command the Mirror to reveal what it may of Dol Dhannen and Karazgar.'","Talk to Lady Galadriel","The Lady and the Mirror","Travel to Galadriel's Garden","Travel to Caras Galadhon and seek Lady Galadriel in the Court of Celeborn","Lady Galadriel can be found in the Court of Celeborn.\
\
You have come to the Court of Celeborn and should now seek Lady Galadriel's counsel.","King Thranduil can be found within Felegoth.\
\
Concerned that none of the visions you were granted have come to pass, King Thorin III has asked you to seek King Thranduil's counsel on what is to be done.","Galadriel's Garden can be found in the south-eastern reaches of Caras Galadhon.\
\
Lady Galadriel has decided to consult the Mirror of Galadriel to determine if Karazgar has indeed returned to Dol Guldur."},
[12490]={"Lord Angbor can be found just outside Tumladen in northern Upper Lebennin.\
\
Lady Terenis has threatened to imprison you unless you or Lord Angbor tell her the truth of the battle at Pelargir.","The Lady's Cunning","After threatening to imprison you, it is clear that Lady Terenis desires to learn of the truth of Pelargir at any cost.","'You must forgive me if I am too direct, but I wish to learn more of the battle at Pelargir. You have travelled here safely and our walls remain unbreached, so I can only assume you found victory, but I am curious as to how.\
\
'The Corsairs had many men... certainly many more than we could equal, especially after the great mustering at my brother's city. How then did they fail? Was it the valour of a few great men? And most curious of all... why do their ships still sail on the Anduin? \
\
'Lord Angbor has just arrived, so I am told, so perhaps I shall ask him as well.'\
\
You tell Lady Terenis that both you and Lord Angbor have taken an oath to keep secret the truth of the battle of Pelargir.\
\
'Oh, have you now? I offer you a choice, ${PLAYER}... either tell me of the truth, convince Lord Angbor to speak of the battle, or I shall have you thrown into a cell for plotting against the people of Gondor.'","Talk to Angbor outside Tumladen","'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}! I trust you followed the boy on his errand?\
\
'I had a suspicion you would, my friend, for you are a ${RACE} of honour. Yet, if what you say is true, Aragorn was wise to send me here. The Lady has no such power, I assure you. You need not fear imprisonment.\
\
'You see, I bear a missive on his behalf meant for the Lady's eyes only. The war shall not wait upon her stubbornness, so let us quell her curiosity and continue to the East.'"},
[12491]={"Torferth is in Torsbury, west of Oserley.\
\
When you come to Torsbury, you should deliver Lúfa's favour to Torferth.","When you come to Torsbury, you should deliver Lúfa's favour to Torferth.","You should bring Lúfa's favour to Torferth at Torsbury","'¿Tienes algo para mí?'","Torferth is in Tordag's camp, west of Oserley.\
\
You should deliver Lúfa's favour to Torferth.","The Lady's Favour","Bring Lúfa's favour to Torferth at Torsbury","Bring Lúfa's favour to Torferth in Tordag's camp","Torsbury is overrun, and the people have retreated south and east","Lady Lúfa had given you her favour to deliver to Torferth of Torsbury as a token of her faithful but forever unrequited love.","'What is this you bring me? I recognize it! This belongs to Lúfa, daughter of Gísling...but did she not wed Ordlac of Oserley?\
\
'You say that she did not wed him out of love? Alas, that we should be torn apart for politics and alliances. I will treasure this and swear if Ordlac does not bring her joy, he shall feel the taste of my steel....\
\
'I am sorry...I should not speak so harshly before you.'","Bring Lúfa's favour to Torferth in Torsbury"},
[12493]={"The Lady's Protector","Talk to Dudsig and obtain the key to Ordlac's house","'Who are you? Ah, my husband sent you. Is he afraid that his trophy might be lost?\
\
'Please...do not mind my words. They are borne of sorrow. I should be glad of some company.'","Dudsig is near the stables in Oserley.\
\
Ordlac has instructed you to obtain the key to his house from Dudsig.","DNT -- Will not be seen","'Ha! These oafs dare to consider the murder of my wife...and in my own home, no less? Well, we shall just have to make them rue their impudence.\
\
'Speak with Dudsig; he shall give you the key to my home. Go to Lúfa and stay with her. When the villains come to perform their heinous act, you shall dispatch them.\
\
'Nay, do not look at me so! Lúfa is the daughter of Gísling and granddaughter of Gísil, Thane of Garsfeld. My marriage to her sealed the alliance between our houses...how do you think it would look if I were to let her perish at the hands of ruffians? Nay, I doubt not your talents, my friend!'","Ordlac's house is near the Oserley stable, on the road to the Mead Hall.\
\
Dudsig gave you the key to Thane Ordlac's house and bade you fulfill your duty there.","You found a note upon the corpse of one of the half-orc commanders detailing plans to murder Thane Ordlac's wife in their own home.","Talk to Lúfa at Ordlac's house","'Aye, indeed I have the key, and here it is. It is a brilliant plan, I think, that my thane has considered. How best to deal with the situation than to have you confront the villains in his own home, where you may better protect Lady Lúfa?\
\
'Thane Ordlac's home is just up the road leading to the Mead Hall, if you have not already taken note of it.'"},
[12494]={"Talk to Lúfa in Ordlac's house","Lúfa is at Thane Ordlac's house in Oserley.\
\
Lúfa has finished her tale and wishes to speak with you again.","'I have seen but seventeen summers, and though to be wed so young in these lands in not a queer thing, I did not have a say in the choice of my husband...please, leave me to my sorrow.'","Collect wine from the table","'Thank you. You have shown me a kindness.\
\
'If you wish to know why I grieve so as the wife of such a young and handsome thane, it is because my heart belongs to another. I am only wed to Ordlac because my father desired an alliance with Oserley.\
\
'I do not think my father would have promised me to Ordlac if he knew the lonely life I would lead here, but it is done now....'","The Lady's Sorrow","Thane Ordlac sent you to his house to protect his young wife Lúfa from the would-be assassins which the half-orcs intend to use against her.","Lúfa is at Thane Ordlac's house in Oserley.\
\
Lúfa awaits the wine she requested from you.","The wine is on the table in Thane Ordlac's house.\
\
Lúfa has asked you to bring her a cup of wine to ease her thirst while she tells you her tale.","'Now do you understand why I grieve? I will abide by my father's wishes, for I love him and would not be disobedient, even for my own sake, but I begin to feel like I will become old from sorrow and loneliness before my time.\
\
'I do have one request to ask of you though: if you continue to Torsbury as you say you must, would you bring this, my favour, to Torferth? He thinks me unfaithful, and I wish him to know that my heart still belongs to him, even though we may never fulfill our hearts' desires.'","'You wonder why I grieve so? I am recently wed to Thane Ordlac, but here I have not found love. Alas, I must call his home mine, yet I do not recall that he has ever come to this house since we were married.\
\
'Truly, even did he show his love to me, I do not think I could be consoled, for my heart does not care for him as it should.\
\
'Would you bring me a cup of wine from the table? If you are willing to hear my tale, then I shall need the refreshment to soothe my thirst.'","Bring the cup of wine to Lúfa","Collected wine from the table"},
[12495]={"No hace mucho tiempo, un grupo de Trév Duvárdain derrotó a un mago de la Corona de Hierro en los alcantarillados de Carn Dûm. La historia es, como Lágsaith querría que muchos creyeran, bastante extraña.","Completa 'Sagroth, la guarida de las alimañas'","La guarida de las alimañas","Lágsaith ha concluido su historia.\
\
Deberías hablar con ella en Bail Avarc.","Completa 'Sagroth, la guarida de las alimañas' en cualquier dificultad.\
\
Usa el Buscador de Instancias para entrar en 'Sagroth, la guarida de las alimañas'.","Completa 'Sagroth, la guarida de las alimañas' en cualquier dificultad","'¿Quieres conocer todo el relato, eh? Bueno, supongo que puedo concederte ese privilegio.\
\
'Una vez que mi querido Aighrig regresó del este, nuestro pequeño grupo comenzó a cazar a aquellos que aún creían en la Corona de Hierro. Rastreábamos a un tonto llamado Gárvadach por los alcantarillados de Dún Bándrath -- o Carn Dûm, como también se le conoce. Aparentemente, buscaba capturar y domesticar a una bestia de algún tipo. Los rumores de terribles monstruos que merodean bajo la ciudad van y vienen, pero...'\
\
Lágsaith se acerca para un susurro conspirativo.\
\
'Te aseguro que algunos de ellos han sido muy ciertos. Después de todo, ¿por qué la Corona de Hierro se preocuparía por cómo sus hechicerías han envenenado la vida silvestre?'\
\
Ella sonríe, luego se recuesta.\
\
'Gárvadach puede haber sido un tonto, pero cualquiera que perciba el mundo como algo a conquistar es peligroso. La tierra no perdona tal arrogancia, ni lo olvida.\
\
'Y así, los seis lo perseguimos....'","'Descendimos a las profundidades de los antiguos alcantarillados de Carn Dûm...'","'Diría que la historia ha llegado a su fin, pero el destino de nuestro amigo ratón sigue envuelto en misterio. Que encuentre algo de paz en la naturaleza... preferiblemente muy lejos de la Corona de Hierro.\
\
'Gracias por escucharme. Ya he contado esta historia muchas veces, pero no creo que me cansaré nunca de ella. Ver a la gente reaccionar con sonrisas y risas es suficiente para mí. Después de todo, ¿qué hay de malo en un poco de diversión ligera en medio de días tan oscuros?\
\
'¿Estaba mintiendo sobre el gran ratón? Bueno...'\
\
Lágsaith te guiña un ojo.\
\
'Eso es algo que solo yo sé y tú tendrás que adivinar. Si crees que te ayudará a tomar una decisión, vuelve otra vez para escuchar esta historia.'","Habla con Lágsaith en Bail Avarc"},
[12496]={"The Last Beacon","In the distance, the Corsairs have made landfall in the ancient Elf-harbour of Edhellond","'Thank you for allowing me another moment to speak with you, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'There are things you must be made aware of if you seek to aid our people. To the west, Dol Amroth overlooks the bay... and a glorious city it is. Yet, we stand at the edge of ruin as Corsairs run rampant throughout our lands. I do not ask anything of you but to understand what is at stake.\
\
'Look to Dol Amroth, and understand what could be lost if we fail to defend ourselves.'","Edhellond can be viewed to the north of Amon Lontir.\
\
Boradan has asked you to look from the beacon to Edhellond.","Boradan can be found on the beacon, Amon Lontir, just outside Ost Lontir.\
\
You have looked upon Edhellond and should now speak to Boradan.","This seems like a good place to <rgb=#FF00FF>look</rgb> at Edhellond","<rgb=#FF00FF>Look</rgb> to Dol Amroth in the west from Amon Lontir","Talk to Boradan","Boradan can be found on the beacon, Amon Lontir, just outside Ost Lontir.\
\
You have looked upon Dol Amroth and should now speak to Boradan.","<rgb=#FF00FF>Look</rgb> to Edhellond in the north from Amon Lontir","DNT -- will not be seen","Dol Amroth can be viewed to the west of Amon Lontir.\
\
Boradan has asked you to look from the beacon to Dol Amroth.","In the distance, the shining city of Dol Amroth overlooks the Bay of Belfalas","'It is beautiful, is it not? Should the war turn against us, you can consider yourself fortunate to have looked upon it.\
\
'Alas, it is not the only thing I wish you to see. To the north lies the ancient Elf-haven of Edhellond... and more importantly, those who would seek to claim our lands. It is one thing to tell you of this, but another to look upon it with your own eyes.\
\
'Look to Edhellond, and see the ships that have claimed the harbour!'","From the beacon of Amon Lontir, the threats to Gondor have become well-known, but it is less known how the people of Ost Lontir will address them.","This seems like a good place to <rgb=#FF00FF>look</rgb> at Dol Amroth","'So now you see what troubles us so, ${PLAYER}....\
\
'You see, this is no small raid by the Corsairs. The people of Belfalas face an invasion on our shores, and unless we can discover a means to defend ourselves with so many of our warriors gone to the east, I fear that our lands shall soon fall to the Enemy.'"},
[12497]={"Morgul Defilers can be found in Eryn Lothad.\
\
You should defeat defilers to protect the orchard from being ravaged.","Defeated Morgul Defiler (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Last Bit of Green","Ingold can be found at the North-gate of the Rammas.\
\
You should speak with Ingold.","Speak with Ingold","'There is much awry in Pelennor. The enemy is slowly approaching towards Minas Tirith. Just recently I saw a small patrol of Orcs heading towards Eryn Lothad just south-west of here. Can I count on you to investigate and defeat these Orcs?\
\
'I fear the safety of the orchard as we will need them to feed the soldiers after this battle is won.'","Ingold, captain of the Out-wall, refuses to leave his post. In his vigilance he has seen enemy troops head towards the nearby orchard.","'Good work. You have prevented the Orcs from destroying the orchard. Their cunning ways continue to both impress and disgust me. We must keep these vile creatures at bay.'","Defeat Morgul Defilers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12498]={"You should continue looking for signs of Bothin in Skrizagáf.","More blood has been tracked further in","Time passes...","The Orc's body has sustained large bite marks that could not have been inflicted by most of the worms here. This corpse must be what's encouraging Bothin to stay inside the cave.\
\
Bothin hasn't made an appearance, but pretending to steal its food may enrage it into emerging.","Talk to Elta near Shataz-kordh","'If we wait any longer, my beard will become whiter than it already is! Perhaps there are more Orc corpses in the worm-cave, Skrizagáf? You must've passed by its entrance by now -- it's on the eastern side of Shataz-kordh.\
\
'Entering the worm-cave Skrizagáf might be the only option. You'll have to go alone -- with these old bones, I'd be more of a burden than a boon, but I'm sure you can manage. Good hunting.'","Bothin has not appeared.\
\
You should talk to Elta and come up with a different plan together.","Finding the final creature on Elta's list might be trickier than it seems....","Elta has suggested to wait and see if Bothin will appear.","Bothin defeated","'Heh, I was starting to wonder when I'd have to go in myself! No, no, I jest.\
\
'Though our partnership was brief, I could not have asked for a better hunting partner. You honour me, ${PLAYER}. Perhaps we'll meet again -- but now, it's time for me to retire!'","Orkish blood has been splattered on the ground","The Last Bounty","Find signs of Bothin","You have found a dead Orc in Skrizagáf.\
\
You should examine the corpse.","You have defeated Bothin and obtained its hide.\
\
Elta waits for you outside of Shataz-kordh.","A partially-eaten Orc lies on the ground","Talk to Elta","Find more signs of Bothin","Wait with Elta","'As you were burning the corpses, I was thinking of what to call the worm. A bit tricky, but I believe the name I've chosen fits well: Bothin, named after an old hunting partner of mine who was lazy to the bone. You've already shown more competence than he ever did, and I am not someone who is easily impressed!\
\
'Now, let's wait for Bothin to emerge. Make sure to keep its hide at least mostly intact; we'll want to hand that over to the Gabil'akkâ.'","Elta has asked you to find Bothin alone.\
\
You should venture into the cave Skrizagáf, on the eastern side of Shataz-kordh.","Lure out and defeat Bothin","You should pretend to steal the Orc corpse and trick Bothin into emerging.","Examine the Orc corpse"},
[12499]={"Chills run down your spine, for the terrible presence of Abedec has appeared behind you","'He is coming, ${PLAYER}, he is coming! Do not tarry here any longer. He is coming for my head, and he will take yours too!'\
\
Jajax seems afraid for the first time since you've known the bold and unusual Corsair. You should free him from his bonds at once, and make your escape.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will fail on defeat.</rgb>","You tell Lothíriel of Jajax and your journey amongst the Corsairs, ending in the defeat of the cruelest captain of all.\
\
'An incredible tale, ${PLAYER}! It sounds as if you have done much to aid us against the Corsairs of Umbar, though I do not think much of your choice of friends.\
\
'I only hope that your efforts may keep us safe.'","Jajax is in the large tent at Abedec's Watch in southern Belfalas.\
\
You should speak with Jajax.","Speak with Jajax","Captain Abedec is on a mission to have the heads of Jajax and yourself for your offences to the Corsairs.","You have defeated Abedec, the last of the vengeful Corsair Captains","Try to free Jajax from his bonds","The Last Captain","Tell Lothíriel of all that transpired","Abedec has won....","'We've done it, ${PLAYER}! The last captain has been defeated, and we are free to do as we will without being hunted.\
\
'I suppose you'll go back to your silly heroic ways, and I'll go back to my mischief, but I will never forget the ${CLASS} who bested my men at drinking and avenged them in death.\
\
'Go well, ${PLAYER}. May the seas take you gently to the shore on which you find your rest.'","Jajax is in Abedec's Watch, the Corsair encampment in the ruins south of Dol Amroth.\
\
You should free Jajax from his bonds.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest will fail on defeat.</rgb>","<rgb=#FF0000>Do not let Abedec defeat you</rgb>","Lothíriel is in the Great Hall of the Prince in Dol Amroth.\
\
You should speak with Lothíriel."},
}
